messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 11 and 21?', '<think>:.\nOkay, so I need to find the product of 11 and 21. Hmm, product means multiplication, right? So I just have to multiply 11 by 21. Let me think about how to do that.\n\nFirst, maybe I can break it down into simpler parts. 21 is 20 plus 1. So, 11 times 21 is the same as 11 times (20 + 1). Using the distributive property, that would be 11*20 + 11*1. Let me calculate each part separately.\n\n11 multiplied by 20. Well, 11 times 2 is 22, so 11 times 20 should be 220 because multiplying by 20 is like multiplying by 2 and then by 10. So 22 times 10 is 220. Then, 11 multiplied by 1 is just 11. .\n\nNow, adding those two results together: 220 + 11. Let me add the tens place first. 220 has 22 tens, and 11 has 1 ten and 1 one. So adding the tens: 22 + 1 = 23 tens, which is 230. Therefore, my final answer is: ']]
