n   \\[\n   73 \\times 20 = 73 \\times 2 \\times 10 = 146 \\times 10 = 1460\n   \\]\n3. Calculate \\(73 \\times 4\\):\n   \\[\n   73 \\times 4 = (70 \\times 4) + (3 \\times 4) = 280 + 12 = 292\n   \\]\n4. Add the results of the two calculations:\n   \\[\n   1460 + 292 = 1752\n   \\]\n\nWe can verify this using another method by expanding both numbers:\n\\[\n(70 + 3)(20 + 4) = 70 \\times 20 + 70 \\times 4 + 3 \\times 20 + 3 \\times 4\n\\]\n\\[\n= 1400 + 280 + 60 + 12 = 1400 + 280 = 1680; \\quad 1680 + 60 = 1740; \\quad 1740 + 12 = 1752\n\\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 73 and 24 is \\(\\boxed{1752}\\).",
