:\n\\[\n24 \\times 80 = 24 \\times 8 \\times 10 = 192 \\times 10 = 1920\n\\]\n\nNext, calculate \\(24 \\times 8\\):\n\\[\n24 \\times 8 = (20 \\times 8) + (4 \\times 8) = 160 + 32 = 192\n\\]\n\nAdd the two results together:\n\\[\n1920 + 192 = 2112\n\\]\n\nWe can verify this using another method by recognizing \\(88 = 8 \\times 11\\):\n\\[\n24 \\times 88 = 24 \\times (8 \\times 11) = (24 \\times 8) \\times 11 = 192 \\times 11\n\\]\n\nCalculating \\(192 \\times 11\\):\n\\[\n192 \\times 11 = 192 \\times (10 + 1) = 1920 + 192 = 2112\n\\]\n\nAnother verification using the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n   24 \\\\\n\\times 88 \\\\\n\\hline\n  192 \\quad (\\text{24} \\times 8) \\\\\n+1920 \\quad (\\text{24} \\times 80) \\\\\n\\hline\n  2112 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nAll methods confirm the result is \\(\\boxed{2112}\\).",
