yover 3.  \n5 x 2 =10, plus 3 =13. So the second partial product is 130 (since it's shifted one place to the left, it's 1300).  \n\nAdding 78 + 1300: 1300 +70 is 1370, plus 8 is 1378. Yep. \n\nAlright, that seems correct. I can't find any mistakes in the calculation steps. So the answer must be 1378.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 26 and 53 is calculated as follows:\n\n1. **Break down the multiplication using the distributive property:**\n   \\[\n   26 \\times 53 = 26 \\times (50 + 3)\n   \\]\n   \n2. **Multiply each part separately:**\n   - \\(26 \\times 50 = 1300\\)\n   - \\(26 \\times 3 = 78\\)\n   \n3. **Add the results together:**\n   \\[\n   1300 + 78 = 1378\n   \\]\n\n**Final Answer:**  \nThe product of 26 and 53 is \\(\\boxed{1378}\\).",
