 356 more than 3600, which makes sense because 43 is 3 more than 40, and 92 is 2 more than 90. The extra comes from those increments. \n\nAlternatively, maybe compute (40 + 3)(90 +2)=40\u00d790 +40\u00d72 +3\u00d790 +3\u00d72, which we did earlier. \n\nAlternatively, think of 43\u00d792 as 43\u00d7(90+2). \n\nWait, that's the same as the distributive method. \n\nAlternatively, maybe use the difference of squares? Hmm, not sure if that applies here. \n\nAlternatively, think of 43\u00d792 as (45 -2)\u00d792. Not sure if that's helpful. \n\n45\u00d792 would be ... 45\u00d790=4050, 45\u00d72=90, so total 4140. Then subtract 2\u00d792=184, so 4140-184=3956. \n\nAh, that works too. So that's another way. \n\nSo yeah, that gives the same answer again. \n\nTherefore, I feel confident that 43 multiplied by 92 is indeed 3956. \n\nI don't see any mistakes in my calculations, and multiple methods confirm the same result. So I think that's the correct product.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 43 and 92 is calculated as follows:\n\n**Step-by-Step Solution:**\n\n1. **Break down the multiplication using the distributive property:**\n   \\[\n   43 \\times 92 = 43 \\times (90 + 2)\n   \\]\n   \n2. **Expand the terms:**\n   \\[\n   = (43 \\times 90) + (43 \\times 2)\n   \\]\n   \n3. **Calculate each part:**\n   - \\(43 \\times 90 = 3,870\\)\n   - \\(43 \\times 2 = 86\\)\n   \n4. **Add the results:**\n   \\[\n   3,870 + 86 = 3,956\n   \\]\n\n**Verification with Alternative Methods:**\n\n- **Standard Multiplication Algorithm:**\n  \\[\n  \\begin{array}{r}\n    \\quad 43 \\\\\n  \\times 92 \\\\\n  \\hline\n    \\quad 86 \\quad (\\text{43 \u00d7 2}) \\\\\n  + 3,870 \\quad (\\text{43 \u00d7 90, shifted left}) \\\\\n  \\hline\n    3,956 \\\\\n  \\end{array}\n  \\]\n\n- **Alternative Distributive Approach:**\n  \\[\n  (40 + 3) \\times (90 + 2) = 40 \\times 90 + 40 \\times 2 + 3 \\times 90 + 3 \\times 2\n  \\]\n  \\[\n  = 3,600 + 80 + 270 + 6 = 3,956\n  \\]\n\n**Final Answer:**  \n\\boxed{3956}",
