o digits for 84 (8 and 4) and two digits for 12 (1 and 2). So a 2x2 grid. \n\nMultiplying each digit:\n\nTop row by right column: 8\u00d71=8 and 8\u00d72=16; then 4\u00d71=4 and 4\u00d72=8. Wait, actually I might be mixing up the steps. Let me recall lattice method properly. \n\nWait, perhaps this is getting too complicated. Since all other methods have given me the same answer, I can be fairly confident that 1008 is correct. \n\nAlternatively, maybe estimate to check if it's reasonable. 80\u00d710 is 800, and 80\u00d712 would be 960, which is close. Since 84 is a bit more than 80, so 84\u00d712 should be a bit more than 960, which 1008 is. That makes sense. \n\nAlternatively, 100\u00d712 is 1200, so 84 is 16 less than 100. Each 1 less in the 84 would reduce the product by 12, so 16\u00d712=192. So 1200-192 = 1008. That also works. That's another way to compute it. \n\nYes, that seems correct. 100\u00d712=1200. Subtract 16\u00d712 (which is 192) from that. 1200 - 192: 1200 - 200 is 1000, but since it's only 192, add back 8, so 1008. Exactly. \n\nTherefore, I think the answer is definitely 1008. All different methods of computation lead to the same result, so I can be confident there's no mistake here. \n\nI guess that's it. The product of 84 and 12 is 1008.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 84 and 12 is \\boxed{1008}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 84 and 12, we can use the standard multiplication method:\n\n1. Multiply 84 by the digit in the ones place of 12 (which is 2):\n   \\[\n   84 \\times 2 = 168\n   \\]\n\n2. Multiply 84 by the digit in the tens place of 12 (which is 1, representing 10):\n   \\[\n   84 \\times 10 = 840\n   \\]\n\n3. Add the two partial products together:\n   \\[\n   168 + 840 = 1008\n   \\]\n\nWe can verify this result using different methods:\n- Using the distributive property: \\(84 \\times 12 = 84 \\times (10 + 2) = 84 \\times 10 + 84 \\times 2 = 840 + 168 = 1008\\)\n- Breaking down 84 into 80 and 4: \\((80 + 4) \\times 12 = 80 \\times 12 + 4 \\times 12 = 960 + 48 = 1008\\)\n- Estimating and adjusting: \\(100 \\times 12 - 16 \\times 12 = 1200 - 192 = 1008\\)\n\nAll methods confirm that the product of 84 and 12 is \\(\\boxed{1008}\\).",
