with expanding (20+4)(60+7): 20*60=1200, 20*7=140, 4*60=240, 4*7=28. 1200+140=1340, 1340+240=1580, 1580+28=1608. Correct.\n\nThird method: 24*70=1680, minus 24*3=72. 1680-72=1608. Correct.\n\nAll methods lead to 1608, so I think that's the right answer. I don't see any errors in my calculations. \n\nAlternatively, maybe I can do the multiplication vertically again, just to be thorough.\n\nLet me write it out:\n\n```.\n    24  \n  x67  \n  ------  \n    168   (24 x 7)  \n  1440    (24 x 60, shifted one position to the left)  \n  ------  \n   1608  \n```.\n\nYes, that's correct. \n\nAlternatively, if I reverse the numbers, multiplying 67 by 24, should get the same result. Let me try that way.\n\n67  \nx24  \n------  \nFirst, 67*4: 60*4=240, 7*4=28, so 240+28=268.  \nThen, 67*20: 67*2=134, so 1340.  \nAdding them: 268+1340=1608. Same result. \n\nAlright, that works too. \n\nI think I've verified it through multiple methods. The answer is 1608. \n\nWait, just to ensure I didn't make a mistake in any of the basic multiplications. Let me confirm 24*7. 24*7: 20*7=140, 4*7=28, so 140+28=168. Correct. 24*60: 24*6=144, so 144*10=1440. Correct. 168+1440: 168+1440. Let's see, 1440 + 168. 1440 + 100 is 1540, plus 68 is 1608. Correct.\n\nAlternatively, if I add 168 + 1440, starting from the units: 8+0=8, 6+4=10, carry over 1. 1+4+1=6. Then the thousands digit is 1. So 1608. Correct. \n\nSo I think that's solid. I can't see a mistake here. So the product of 24 and 67 is 1608.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 24 and 67 is \\boxed{1608}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 24 and 67, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n1. Multiply 24 by 7 (the ones digit of 67):\n   \\[\n   24 \\times 7 = 168\n   \\]\n   - \\(20 \\times 7 = 140\\)\n   - \\(4 \\times 7 = 28\\)\n   - \\(140 + 28 = 168\\)\n\n2. Multiply 24 by 60 (the tens digit of 67, which is 6 in the tens place):\n   \\[\n   24 \\times 60 = 1440\n   \\]\n   - \\(24 \\times 6 = 144\\)\n   - \\(144 \\times 10 = 1440\\)\n\n3. Add the two partial products together:\n   \\[\n   168 + 1440 = 1608\n   \\]\n\nVerification using different methods:\n- **Distributive Property**:\n  \\[\n  24 \\times 67 = 24 \\times (60 + 7) = (24 \\times 60) + (24 \\times 7) = 1440 + 168 = 1608\n  \\]\n\n- **Expanding the numbers**:\n  \\[\n  (20 + 4) \\times (60 + 7) = 20 \\times 60 + 20 \\times 7 + 4 \\times 60 + 4 \\times 7 = 1200 + 140 + 240 + 28 = 1608\n  \\]\n\n- **Alternative approach**:\n  \\[\n  24 \\times 70 - 24 \\times 3 = 1680 - 72 = 1608\n  \\]\n\nAll methods confirm the result is consistent. \n\nThe product of 24 and 67 is \\(\\boxed{1608}\\).",
