d74. 5\u00d74=20, carryover 2. 3\u00d74=12 plus 2 is 14. So 140. Correct.\n\nSecond step: 35\u00d77 (but since it's the tens place, it's \u00d770). 35\u00d77: 5\u00d77=35, carryover 3. 3\u00d77=21 plus 3 is 24. So 245, then \u00d710 becomes 2450. Correct.\n\n2450 +140: 2450+100=2550, then +40=2590. Correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe another method: 35\u00d774. Let me think of 35 as 5\u00d77, so 5\u00d77\u00d774. 7\u00d774 is 518, then 5\u00d7518. Hmm, 5\u00d7500=2500 and 5\u00d718=90, so total 2590. That also works. So that's another way to see it. Yep, 2590 again.\n\nAlright, all my different methods are giving me the same answer. I think that's solid. Therefore, the product of 35 and 74 is 2590.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 35 and 74 is \\boxed{2590}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 35 and 74, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n1. Multiply 35 by 4 (the units digit of 74):\n   \\[\n   35 \\times 4 = 140\n   \\]\n\n2. Multiply 35 by 70 (the tens digit of 74, which is equivalent to 7 in the tens place):\n   \\[\n   35 \\times 70 = 2450\n   \\]\n\n3. Add the results of the two multiplications:\n   \\[\n   140 + 2450 = 2590\n   \\]\n\nWe can verify this using the distributive property:\n\\[\n35 \\times 74 = 35 \\times (70 + 4) = (35 \\times 70) + (35 \\times 4) = 2450 + 140 = 2590\n\\]\n\nAnother verification using the FOIL method on the expanded form:\n\\[\n(30 + 5)(70 + 4) = 30 \\times 70 + 30 \\times 4 + 5 \\times 70 + 5 \\times 4 = 2100 + 120 + 350 + 20 = 2590\n\\]\n\nAll methods confirm that the product of 35 and 74 is \\(\\boxed{2590}\\).",
