 by 5 (the ones digit of 95):\n\n5\u00d73 =15, write down 5, carryover 1.\n\n5\u00d72 =10 +1=11. So first partial product is 115.\n\nThen multiply 23 by 9 (the tens digit of 95, which is actually 90). So we need to shift one position to the left.\n\nStarting with the ones place: 9\u00d73 =27, write down 7, carryover 2.\n\nThen 9\u00d72 =18 +2=20. Since we're in the tens place, this partial product is 207 shifted one place left, so it's 2070.\n\nAdding 115 +2070:\n\n115  \n+2070  \n------  \n2185. \n\nYes, that's correct. All right, so after verifying through multiple methods, I believe the product of 23 and 95 is indeed 2185. So the answer should be 2185.\n\nWait, just to ensure I haven't made a calculation mistake anywhere, let me do 23\u00d795 on a calculator. But since I can't use an actual calculator, I'll do the multiplication step-by-step once again.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use another approach: 23\u00d795.\n\nLet me think of 23\u00d795 as (20 +3)(90 +5). Expanding this:\n\n20\u00d790 +20\u00d75 +3\u00d790 +3\u00d75.\n\n20\u00d790 = 1800.\n\n20\u00d75=100.\n\n3\u00d790=270.\n\n3\u00d75=15.\n\nAdding all together: 1800 +100 =1900; 270 +15=285. Then 1900+285=2185. Yep, same answer.\n\nAlternatively, cross-verify by division: if 23\u00d795=2185, then 2185 divided by 23 should be 95. Let me check that.\n\nDivide 2185 by 23.\n\n23\u00d790=2070. Subtract that from 2185: 2185-2070=115.\n\nThen 115 divided by 23 is 5. So total is 90+5=95. That's correct. So that checks out.\n\nAlternatively, divide 2185 by 95. Let's see if that equals 23.\n\n95\u00d720=1900. Subtract that from 2185: 2185-1900=285.\n\n95\u00d73=285. So 20+3=23. Perfect, that also works.\n\nTherefore, I can confirm that the product is indeed 2185. I think this is solid. I've checked it multiple ways and each time it comes out the same. So I feel confident that's the right answer.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 23 and 95 is \\boxed{2185}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 23 and 95, we can use the distributive property and verify through multiple methods:\n\n1. **Standard Multiplication Algorithm**:\n   - Multiply 23 by 5 (the ones digit of 95):\n     \\[\n     \\begin{array}{r}\n       23 \\\\\n     \\times 5 \\\\\n     \\hline\n       115 \\\\\n     \\end{array}\n     \\]\n   - Multiply 23 by 90 (the tens digit of 95, shifted one place to the left):\n     \\[\n     \\begin{array}{r}\n       23 \\\\\n     \\times 90 \\\\\n     \\hline\n       2070 \\\\\n     \\end{array}\n     \\]\n   - Add the partial products:\n     \\[\n     \\begin{array}{r}\n       115 \\\\\n     + 2070 \\\\\n     \\hline\n       2185 \\\\\n     \\end{array}\n     \\]\n\n2. **Distributive Property**:\n   - Break down 95 into 90 + 5:\n     \\[\n     23 \\times 95 = 23 \\times (90 + 5) = (23 \\times 90) + (23 \\times 5)\n     \\]\n   - Calculate each part:\n     \\[\n     23 \\times 90 = 2070 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 23 \\times 5 = 115\n     \\]\n   - Sum the results:\n     \\[\n     2070 + 115 = 2185\n     \\]\n\n3. **Alternative Breakdown**:\n   - Express 95 as 100 - 5:\n     \\[\n     23 \\times 95 = 23 \\times (100 - 5) = (23 \\times 100) - (23 \\times 5)\n     \\]\n   - Calculate each part:\n     \\[\n     23 \\times 100 = 2300 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 23 \\times 5 = 115\n     \\]\n   - Subtract the results:\n     \\[\n     2300 - 115 = 2185\n     \\]\n\n4. **Verification by Division**:\n   - Divide 2185 by 23:\n     \\[\n     2185 \\div 23 = 95\n     \\]\n   - Divide 2185 by 95:\n     \\[\n     2185 \\div 95 = 23\n     \\]\n\nAll methods confirm that the product of 23 and 95 is \\(\\boxed{2185}\\).",
