n   - Calculate each term:\n     - \\( 30 \\times 80 = 2400 \\),\n     - \\( 30 \\times 8 = 240 \\),\n     - \\( 2 \\times 80 = 160 \\),\n     - \\( 2 \\times 8 = 16 \\).\n   - Sum all terms: \\( 2400 + 240 + 160 + 16 = 2816 \\).\n\n3. **Alternative method using complement to 100**:\n   - Rewrite \\( 88 = 100 - 12 \\).\n   - Compute \\( 32 \\times 100 = 3200 \\).\n   - Subtract \\( 32 \\times 12 = 384 \\): \\( 3200 - 384 = 2816 \\).\n\nAll methods confirm the result is consistent. \n\n**Answer:** The product of 32 and 88 is \\(\\boxed{2816}\\).",
