p, that's correct. Okay, so I feel confident that 45 multiplied by 91 is 4095. I used multiple methods: breaking into parts, distributive property, different groupings, and each time I got the same result. That must be the correct product.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 45 and 91 is \\boxed{4095}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 45 and 91, we can use multiple methods to ensure accuracy:\n\n1. **Distributive Property**:\n   - Break down 91 into 90 + 1.\n   - Calculate \\(45 \\times 90\\) and \\(45 \\times 1\\):\n     - \\(45 \\times 90 = 4050\\)\n     - \\(45 \\times 1 = 45\\)\n   - Add the results: \\(4050 + 45 = 4095\\)\n\n2. **Standard Multiplication Algorithm**:\n   - Multiply 45 by 1 (units place of 91): \\(45 \\times 1 = 45\\)\n   - Multiply 45 by 90 (tens place of 91): \\(45 \\times 90 = 4050\\)\n   - Add the results: \\(4050 + 45 = 4095\\)\n\n3. **Expanding Using Distributive Property**:\n   - Expand \\((40 + 5)(90 + 1)\\):\n     - \\(40 \\times 90 = 3600\\)\n     - \\(40 \\times 1 = 40\\)\n     - \\(5 \\times 90 = 450\\)\n     - \\(5 \\times 1 = 5\\)\n   - Add the results: \\(3600 + 40 + 450 + 5 = 4095\\)\n\n4. **Alternative Method Using 100**:\n   - Express 91 as \\(100 - 9\\):\n     - \\(45 \\times 100 = 4500\\)\n     - \\(45 \\times 9 = 405\\)\n   - Subtract the results: \\(4500 - 405 = 4095\\)\n\nAll methods consistently yield the result 4095. \n\nThe product of 45 and 91 is \\(\\boxed{4095}\\).",
