u00d730 +7\u00d71.\n\n70\u00d730 is 2100, 70\u00d71 is 70, 7\u00d730 is 210, 7\u00d71 is 7. Adding all those:\n\n2100 + 70 is 2170, plus 210 is 2380, plus 7 is 2387. So that's correct.\n\nHmm, okay, so maybe I was just second-guessing myself, but all methods point to 2387. Wait, but let me do it step by step again, just to be thorough.\n\nMultiplying 77 by 31:\n\nFirst, write 77  \n\u00d7\u00a031  \n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500  \nMultiply 77 by 1: 77  \nMultiply 77 by 3 (but since it's the tens place, it's actually 30, so shift one position to the left):  \n77 \u00d7 3 = 231, so written as 2310.  \nAdd them together:  \n\u2003\u00a077  \n+2310  \n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500  \n2387.  \n\nYes, that's correct. So, the product of 77 and 31 is 2387. Wait, but let me confirm with another method. Maybe using the fact that 77 is 7\u00d711 and 31 is a prime?\n\nAlternatively, 77\u00d731 = 7\u00d711\u00d731. Maybe multiply 7\u00d731 first. 7\u00d731 is 217, then multiply by 11. 217\u00d711. Hmm, 217\u00d710 is 2170, plus 217 is 2387. Yep, same result.\n\nAlright, so after checking multiple ways, I think the answer is 2387. I must have been overthinking when I was confused earlier, but all methods confirm that. So I can be confident that's the right answer.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 77 and 31 is \\boxed{2387}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 77 and 31, we can use the distributive property and standard multiplication steps.\n\nFirst, we break down the numbers using the distributive property:\n\\[\n(70 + 7)(30 + 1)\n\\]\nExpanding this, we get:\n\\[\n70 \\times 30 + 70 \\times 1 + 7 \\times 30 + 7 \\times 1\n\\]\nCalculating each term:\n\\[\n70 \\times 30 = 2100\n\\]\n\\[\n70 \\times 1 = 70\n\\]\n\\[\n7 \\times 30 = 210\n\\]\n\\[\n7 \\times 1 = 7\n\\]\nAdding these results together:\n\\[\n2100 + 70 + 210 + 7 = 2100 + 70 = 2170\n\\]\n\\[\n2170 + 210 = 2380\n\\]\n\\[\n2380 + 7 = 2387\n\\]\n\nWe can also verify this using the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n   77 \\\\\n\\times 31 \\\\\n\\hline\n   77 \\quad (\\text{77 multiplied by 1}) \\\\\n+2310 \\quad (\\text{77 multiplied by 30, shifted one position to the left}) \\\\\n\\hline\n  2387 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nAnother verification using prime factors:\n\\[\n77 \\times 31 = (7 \\times 11) \\times 31 = 7 \\times (11 \\times 31)\n\\]\nCalculating step-by-step:\n\\[\n11 \\times 31 = 341\n\\]\n\\[\n7 \\times 341 = 2387\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 77 and 31 is \\boxed{2387}.",
