 Answer**\nThe product of 94 and 80 is \\boxed{7520}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 94 and 80, we can break down the problem using different methods to ensure accuracy:\n\n1. **Breaking into smaller parts**:\n   - Multiply 94 by 8 first:\n     \\[\n     94 \\times 8 = (90 + 4) \\times 8 = 90 \\times 8 + 4 \\times 8 = 720 + 32 = 752\n     \\]\n   - Then multiply the result by 10:\n     \\[\n     752 \\times 10 = 7520\n     \\]\n\n2. **Standard multiplication algorithm**:\n   - Multiply 94 by 80:\n     \\[\n     \\begin{array}{r}\n       \\quad 94 \\\\\n     \\times 80 \\\\\n     \\hline\n       \\quad 0 \\quad \\text{(from 94 \u00d7 0)} \\\\\n     + 7520 \\quad \\text{(from 94 \u00d7 80, shifting one position to the left)} \\\\\n     \\hline\n       7520 \\\\\n     \\end{array}\n     \\]\n\n3. **Distributive property**:\n   - Expand 94 as \\(90 + 4\\) and multiply by 80:\n     \\[\n     (90 + 4) \\times 80 = 90 \\times 80 + 4 \\times 80 = 7200 + 320 = 7520\n     \\]\n\n4. **Alternative approach using 100**:\n   - Calculate 100 times 80 and subtract 6 times 80:\n     \\[\n     100 \\times 80 - 6 \\times 80 = 8000 - 480 = 7520\n     \\]\n\nAll methods confirm that the product of 94 and 80 is \\(\\boxed{7520}\\).",
