\n\n1 +0 =1. So total 2301. Yep.\n\nAlright, so multiple methods confirm that the product is 2301. I think that's solid. I don't see any mistakes in my calculations. So the answer should be 2301.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 39 and 59 is \\boxed{2301}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 39 and 59, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n1. Write the numbers vertically aligned by place value:\n   ```\n   \u2003\u00a039\n   \u00d7\u00a059\n   -------\n   ```\n\n2. Multiply 39 by the ones digit of 59 (which is 9):\n   - \\(9 \\times 9 = 81\\), write down 1 and carry over 8.\n   - \\(9 \\times 3 = 27\\), add the carried over 8 to get 35.\n   - The first partial product is 351.\n\n3. Multiply 39 by the tens digit of 59 (which is 5, representing 50). Shift the result one place to the left:\n   - \\(5 \\times 9 = 45\\), write down 5 and carry over 4.\n   - \\(5 \\times 3 = 15\\), add the carried over 4 to get 19.\n   - The second partial product is 1950 (shifted left by one digit).\n\n4. Add the partial products:\n   ```\n   \u2003\u00a0351\n   +1950\n   -------\n   \u20032301\n   ```\n\nTo verify, we can use the distributive property:\n- \\((40 - 1)(60 - 1) = 40 \\times 60 - 40 \\times 1 - 1 \\times 60 + 1 \\times 1 = 2400 - 40 - 60 + 1 = 2301\\).\n\nAnother verification using the FOIL method:\n- \\((30 + 9)(50 + 9) = 30 \\times 50 + 30 \\times 9 + 9 \\times 50 + 9 \\times 9 = 1500 + 270 + 450 + 81 = 2301\\).\n\nAll methods confirm the product is \\(\\boxed{2301}\\).",
