messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 91 and 41?', "<think>:.\nOkay, so I need to find the product of 91 and 41. Hmm, let's see. I remember that multiplying two numbers means adding one number to itself as many times as the other number says. But doing that manually for 91 and 41 would take a while. Maybe there's a faster way?.\n\nWait, maybe I can use the standard multiplication algorithm. Let me recall how that works. If I write 91 times 41, I can break it down into parts. Let me think, 41 is 40 plus 1, right? So maybe I can use distributive property here. That would be 91 times 40 plus 91 times 1. That might be easier to calculate.\n\nFirst, let me calculate 91 times 40. 91 multiplied by 40. Well, 91 times 4 is 364, so multiplying that by 10 gives me 3640. Wait, no, actually, 40 is 4 times 10, so 91*4 is 364, then 364*10 is 3640. Yeah, that seems right.\n\nThen, 91 times 1 is just 91. So adding those two results together: 3640 plus 91. Let me add those. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
