messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 21 and 66?', '<think>:.\nOkay, so I need to find the product of 21 and 66. Hmm, let me think. Multiplication, right? Alright, 21 times 66. Let me recall how to multiply two numbers. Maybe I can do it step by step. .\n\nFirst, I remember that multiplying by a two-digit number can be broken down. So 66 is 60 plus 6. Maybe I can use the distributive property here. That would mean 21 times 60 plus 21 times 6. Let me try that.\n\nCalculating 21 times 60 first. Hmm, 21 times 6 is 126, right? So if I multiply that by 10, since 60 is 6 times 10, that would be 1260. Wait, no, actually, 21 times 60 is 21*6*10, which is indeed 126*10 = 1260. Okay, that seems right.\n\nNow, the other part is 21 times 6. Let me do that. 20 times 6 is 120, and 1 times 6 is 6, so adding those together gives 126. So 21*6 is 126. .\n\nNow, adding the two parts together: 1260 + 126. Let me add those. Therefore, my final answer is: ']]
