ed using several methods. Here's a straightforward approach:\n\n1. **Breakdown using distributive property**:\n   \\[\n   30 \\times 98 = 30 \\times (100 - 2)\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   = 30 \\times 100 - 30 \\times 2\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   = 3000 - 60 = 2940\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiplying step-by-step**:\n   - First, multiply \\(98 \\times 3 = 294\\).\n   - Then multiply by 10: \\(294 \\times 10 = 2940\\).\n\nBoth methods confirm the result is consistent.\n\n\\boxed{2940}",
