. 750 times 10 is 7500. Yep. All right, I think that's solid. No mistakes here. The answer must be 7500.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 100 and 75 is calculated by multiplying the two numbers together:\n\n\\[\n100 \\times 75 = 7500\n\\]\n\n**Step-by-Step Explanation:**\n1. **Understand the operation:** \"Product\" means multiplication.\n2. **Multiply 100 by 75:**\n   - Since multiplying by 100 adds two zeros to the end of the number, \\(75 \\times 100 = 7500\\).\n   - Alternatively, break it down:  \n     \\(75 \\times 100 = 75 \\times (10 \\times 10) = (75 \\times 10) \\times 10 = 750 \\times 10 = 7500\\).\n\n**Final Answer:**  \n\\boxed{7500}",
