t's do 2340 + 300 =2640, then +90 is 2730. Yep, same.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can check with a calculator? Wait, but since I don't have a calculator here, but I can do division to check. If 2730 divided by 35 is 78, then that's correct.\n\nLet me try dividing 2730 by 35. 35\u00d770 is 2450. 2730 -2450=280. Then 35\u00d78=280. So total is 70+8=78. Perfect, that works. So that confirms the answer is correct.\n\nAlternatively, 2730 divided by 78 should be 35. Let me check that. 78\u00d730=2340. Subtract that from 2730: 2730-2340=390. Then 78\u00d75=390. So 30+5=35. That also works. So division checks out.\n\nAlright, so through multiple methods and checks, I can be confident that the product of 78 and 35 is 2730. I don't see any mistakes in my calculations, and all the different approaches cross-validate each other. So I think that's the right answer.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 78 and 35 is \\boxed{2730}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 78 and 35, we can use the standard multiplication method along with the distributive property for verification.\n\nFirst, we perform the multiplication step-by-step:\n\n1. Multiply 78 by 5 (the ones place of 35):\n   \\[\n   78 \\times 5 = 390\n   \\]\n   - 5 \u00d7 8 = 40 (write down 0, carry over 4)\n   - 5 \u00d7 7 = 35 + 4 (carry) = 39\n\n2. Multiply 78 by 30 (the tens place of 35, which is 3 \u00d7 10):\n   \\[\n   78 \\times 30 = 2340\n   \\]\n   - 78 \u00d7 3 = 234 (then add a zero: 2340)\n\n3. Add the results of the two multiplications:\n   \\[\n   390 + 2340 = 2730\n   \\]\n\nTo verify, we use the distributive property:\n\\[\n78 \\times 35 = 78 \\times (30 + 5) = (78 \\times 30) + (78 \\times 5) = 2340 + 390 = 2730\n\\]\n\nAnother verification using different breakdown:\n\\[\n(70 + 8) \\times (30 + 5) = 70 \\times 30 + 70 \\times 5 + 8 \\times 30 + 8 \\times 5\n\\]\n\\[\n= 2100 + 350 + 240 + 40 = 2730\n\\]\n\nChecking by division:\n- \\(2730 \\div 35 = 78\\)\n- \\(2730 \\div 78 = 35\\)\n\nBoth divisions confirm the result.\n\n### Final Answer\nThe product of 78 and 35 is \\boxed{2730}.",
