d{4956}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 59 and 84, we can use the distributive property by breaking down the numbers into smaller parts:\n\n1. Break down 59 into 50 + 9 and 84 into 80 + 4.\n2. Apply the distributive property:\n   \\[\n   (50 + 9)(80 + 4) = 50 \\times 80 + 50 \\times 4 + 9 \\times 80 + 9 \\times 4\n   \\]\n3. Calculate each term:\n   - \\(50 \\times 80 = 4000\\)\n   - \\(50 \\times 4 = 200\\)\n   - \\(9 \\times 80 = 720\\)\n   - \\(9 \\times 4 = 36\\)\n4. Sum the results:\n   \\[\n   4000 + 200 + 720 + 36 = 4956\n   \\]\n\nVerification using the standard multiplication algorithm:\n- Multiply 59 by 4 (units place):\n  \\[\n  59 \\times 4 = 236\n  \\]\n- Multiply 59 by 80 (tens place, shifted one position left):\n  \\[\n  59 \\times 80 = 4720\n  \\]\n- Add the results:\n  \\[\n  236 + 4720 = 4956\n  \\]\n\nAnother verification using the distributive property with 60 - 1:\n- \\( (60 - 1) \\times 84 = 60 \\times 84 - 1 \\times 84 \\)\n- Calculate each term:\n  - \\(60 \\times 84 = 5040\\)\n  - \\(1 \\times 84 = 84\\)\n- Subtract:\n  \\[\n  5040 - 84 = 4956\n  \\]\n\nAll methods confirm the product is \\(\\boxed{4956}\\).",
