ndard Multiplication Algorithm:**\n   - Multiply 87 by 5 (the ones place of 75):\n     \\[\n     87 \\times 5 = 435\n     \\]\n   - Multiply 87 by 70 (the tens place of 75):\n     \\[\n     87 \\times 70 = 6090\n     \\]\n   - Add the results:\n     \\[\n     435 + 6090 = 6525\n     \\]\n\n2. **Distributive Property:**\n   - Expand using \\((80 + 7) \\times (70 + 5)\\):\n     \\[\n     80 \\times 70 + 80 \\times 5 + 7 \\times 70 + 7 \\times 5\n     \\]\n   - Calculate each term:\n     \\[\n     80 \\times 70 = 5600, \\quad 80 \\times 5 = 400, \\quad 7 \\times 70 = 490, \\quad 7 \\times 5 = 35\n     \\]\n   - Sum the terms:\n     \\[\n     5600 + 400 + 490 + 35 = 6525\n     \\]\n\n3. **Difference of Squares Approach:**\n   - Express 75 as \\(100 - 25\\):\n     \\[\n     87 \\times 75 = 87 \\times (100 - 25) = 87 \\times 100 - 87 \\times 25\n     \\]\n   - Calculate each term:\n     \\[\n     87 \\times 100 = 8700, \\quad 87 \\times 25 = 2175\n     \\]\n   - Subtract the results:\n     \\[\n     8700 - 2175 = 6525\n     \\]\n\n4. **Breaking into Factors:**\n   - Express 75 as \\(25 \\times 3\\):\n     \\[\n     87 \\times 75 = 87 \\times 25 \\times 3\n     \\]\n   - Calculate step-by-step:\n     \\[\n     87 \\times 25 = 2175, \\quad 2175 \\times 3 = 6525\n     \\]\n\nAll methods confirm that the product of 87 and 75 is \\(\\boxed{6525}\\).",
