, I think it's safe.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 44 and 24 is \\boxed{1056}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 44 and 24, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n\\quad 44 \\\\\n\\times 24 \\\\\n\\hline\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nFirst, multiply 44 by the ones place of 24 (which is 4):\n\n\\[\n44 \\times 4 = 176\n\\]\n\nNext, multiply 44 by the tens place of 24 (which is 2, representing 20). This result is shifted one place to the left:\n\n\\[\n44 \\times 20 = 880\n\\]\n\nAdd the two results together:\n\n\\[\n176 + 880 = 1056\n\\]\n\nWe can verify this using the distributive property:\n\n\\[\n44 \\times 24 = (40 + 4) \\times (20 + 4)\n\\]\n\nExpanding this, we get:\n\n\\[\n40 \\times 20 + 40 \\times 4 + 4 \\times 20 + 4 \\times 4 = 800 + 160 + 80 + 16 = 1056\n\\]\n\nAnother verification method using the fact that \\(44 \\times 24 = 44 \\times (25 - 1)\\):\n\n\\[\n44 \\times 25 - 44 = 1100 - 44 = 1056\n\\]\n\nAll methods confirm that the product of 44 and 24 is \\(\\boxed{1056}\\).",
