 (which is 3, representing 30). This result is shifted one place to the left:\n   \\[\n   21 \\times 30 = 630\n   \\]\n\n3. Add the two partial products together:\n   \\[\n   189 + 630 = 819\n   \\]\n\nWe can verify this using the distributive property:\n\\[\n(20 + 1) \\times (30 + 9) = 20 \\times 30 + 20 \\times 9 + 1 \\times 30 + 1 \\times 9 = 600 + 180 + 30 + 9 = 819\n\\]\n\nAnother verification method:\n\\[\n21 \\times 40 - 21 = 840 - 21 = 819\n\\]\n\nAll methods confirm that the product of 21 and 39 is \\(\\boxed{819}\\).",
