messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 16 and 73?', "<think>:.\nOkay, so I need to find the product of 16 and 73. Hmm, let me think. Multiplication, right? But I want to make sure I do this correctly. Let me recall how multiplication works. If I have 16 times 73, that means I have to add 16 to itself 73 times, or 73 to itself 16 times. Either way, that's a lot of adding. Maybe there's a better way than doing it the long way. .\n\nWait, maybe I can break it down into smaller parts. Like, using the distributive property? Let me remember, the distributive property is when you split a number into parts to make multiplication easier. So, for example, 16 times 70 plus 16 times 3? Because 73 is 70 plus 3. Let me try that.\n\nFirst, 16 multiplied by 70. Hmm, 16 times 7 is 112, right? So if it's 16 times 70, that's 10 times 70, so 112 times 10. Wait, no, that's not quite right. Let me think again. Actually, 16 times 70 is the same as 16 multiplied by 7 multiplied by 10. Since 70 is 7 times 10. So 16 times 7 is 112, then times 10 would be 1120. Okay, that makes sense.\n\nNow, the other part is 16 times 3. That's straightforward. 16 times 3 is 48. So if I add those two results together, 1120 plus 48, that should give me the total. Let me add those. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
