 91 \u00d7 3)  \n          8190   (this is 91 \u00d7 90, shifted one position to the left)  \n        --------\n          8463  \n\nAdding those two results: 273 + 8190. Let's add them again. 8190 + 200 is 8390, then +73 is 8463. Correct. \n\nAlternatively, using another approach: 91 \u00d7 93 = (90 +1)(90 +3) = 90\u00d790 + 90\u00d73 + 1\u00d790 + 1\u00d73 = 8100 + 270 + 90 +3 = 8100+270 is 8370, plus 90 is 8460, plus 3 is 8463. Yep, same answer.\n\nI think that's solid. All different methods cross-verify to the same result, so I can be confident the product of 91 and 93 is 8463.\n\nWait, but hold on a second\u2014just to ensure there's no arithmetic mistake in my head. Let me try multiplying 91 by 93 in another way. Let's take 91 \u00d7 93. \n\nAlternatively, think of 93 as 100 -7. So 91 \u00d7 (100 -7) = 91\u00d7100 - 91\u00d77 = 9100 - 637. Compute 9100 minus 637: 9100 - 600 is 8500, then subtract 37 more: 8500 - 37 = 8463. Again, same result. \n\nHmm, that's a fourth method giving the same answer. I think it's safe. \n\nAlternatively, maybe use a calculator? But since I can't here, but all manual methods confirm the same number, I think it's correct. \n\nSo I think the answer is 8463.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 91 and 93 is \\boxed{8463}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 91 and 93, we can use the difference of squares formula. Notice that 91 and 93 are equidistant from 92:\n\n\\[\n91 = 92 - 1 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 93 = 92 + 1\n\\]\n\nUsing the difference of squares formula \\((a - b)(a + b) = a^2 - b^2\\):\n\n\\[\n(92 - 1)(92 + 1) = 92^2 - 1^2\n\\]\n\nCalculating \\(92^2\\):\n\n\\[\n92^2 = (90 + 2)^2 = 90^2 + 2 \\cdot 90 \\cdot 2 + 2^2 = 8100 + 360 + 4 = 8464\n\\]\n\nThus,\n\n\\[\n92^2 - 1 = 8464 - 1 = 8463\n\\]\n\nTo verify, we can use direct multiplication:\n\n\\[\n91 \\times 93 = 91 \\times (90 + 3) = 91 \\times 90 + 91 \\times 3 = 8190 + 273 = 8463\n\\]\n\nAnother verification using the distributive property:\n\n\\[\n(90 + 1)(90 + 3) = 90 \\times 90 + 90 \\times 3 + 1 \\times 90 + 1 \\times 3 = 8100 + 270 + 90 + 3 = 8463\n\\]\n\nAll methods confirm the result is consistent. Therefore, the product of 91 and 93 is \\(\\boxed{8463}\\).",
