50\n     \\]\n   - Add the partial products:\n     \\[\n     680 + 4250 = 4930\n     \\]\n\n2. **Distributive Property:**\n   - Break down the numbers:\n     \\[\n     (80 + 5)(50 + 8) = 80 \\times 50 + 80 \\times 8 + 5 \\times 50 + 5 \\times 8\n     \\]\n   - Calculate each term:\n     \\[\n     80 \\times 50 = 4000, \\quad 80 \\times 8 = 640, \\quad 5 \\times 50 = 250, \\quad 5 \\times 8 = 40\n     \\]\n   - Sum the results:\n     \\[\n     4000 + 640 + 250 + 40 = 4930\n     \\]\n\n3. **Alternative Method (Using 60 - 2):**\n   - Calculate \\(85 \\times 60\\) and subtract \\(85 \\times 2\\):\n     \\[\n     85 \\times 60 = 5100, \\quad 85 \\times 2 = 170\n     \\]\n   - Subtract the results:\n     \\[\n     5100 - 170 = 4930\n     \\]\n\nAll methods confirm that the product of 85 and 58 is \\(\\boxed{4930}\\).",
