 their components:\n   - \\(82 = 80 + 2\\)\n   - \\(42 = 40 + 2\\)\n\n2. Apply the distributive property:\n   \\[\n   (80 + 2)(40 + 2) = 80 \\times 40 + 80 \\times 2 + 2 \\times 40 + 2 \\times 2\n   \\]\n\n3. Calculate each term:\n   - \\(80 \\times 40 = 3200\\)\n   - \\(80 \\times 2 = 160\\)\n   - \\(2 \\times 40 = 80\\)\n   - \\(2 \\times 2 = 4\\)\n\n4. Sum the results of each term:\n   \\[\n   3200 + 160 + 80 + 4 = 3200 + 160 = 3360\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   3360 + 80 = 3440\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   3440 + 4 = 3444\n   \\]\n\n5. Verify using another method (standard multiplication):\n   - Multiply 82 by 2: \\(82 \\times 2 = 164\\)\n   - Multiply 82 by 40: \\(82 \\times 40 = 3280\\)\n   - Add the results: \\(164 + 3280 = 3444\\)\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 82 and 42 is \\(\\boxed{3444}\\).",
