gin{array}{r}\n     58 \\\\\n   \\times 9 \\\\\n   \\hline\n     522 \\\\\n   \\end{array}\n   \\]\n   - \\(9 \\times 8 = 72\\) (write down 2, carry over 7)\n   - \\(9 \\times 5 = 45 + 7 = 52\\)\n\n2. **Multiply 58 by 70 (the tens digit of 79, shifted one position to the left):**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{array}{r}\n     58 \\\\\n   \\times 70 \\\\\n   \\hline\n    4060 \\\\\n   \\end{array}\n   \\]\n   - \\(7 \\times 8 = 56\\) (write down 6, carry over 5)\n   - \\(7 \\times 5 = 35 + 5 = 40\\)\n   - This result is shifted one position to the left, making it 4060.\n\n3. **Add the partial products:**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{array}{r}\n     522 \\\\\n   +4060 \\\\\n   \\hline\n     4582 \\\\\n   \\end{array}\n   \\]\n   - \\(522 + 4060 = 4582\\)\n\nTo verify, we can use the distributive property:\n\\[\n(50 + 8)(70 + 9) = 50 \\times 70 + 50 \\times 9 + 8 \\times 70 + 8 \\times 9\n\\]\n\\[\n= 3500 + 450 + 560 + 72 = 3500 + 450 = 3950 + 560 = 4510 + 72 = 4582\n\\]\n\nAnother verification using compensation:\n\\[\n58 \\times 79 = 58 \\times (80 - 1) = 58 \\times 80 - 58 = 4640 - 58 = 4582\n\\]\n\nAll methods confirm the result is consistent.\n\n### Final Answer\nThe product of 58 and 79 is \\boxed{4582}.",
