Treat 41 as \\(50 - 9\\):\n     - Calculate \\(87 \\times 50 = 4350\\)\n     - Calculate \\(87 \\times 9 = 783\\)\n   - Subtract the results: \\(4350 - 783 = 3567\\)\n\nAll methods consistently yield the result 3567. Thus, the product of 87 and 41 is \\(\\boxed{3567}\\).",
