ent that the product of 67 and 70 is 4690.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 67 and 70 can be calculated efficiently by breaking down the multiplication:\n\n1. **Step 1:** Multiply 67 by 7:  \n   \\[\n   67 \\times 7 = (60 \\times 7) + (7 \\times 7) = 420 + 49 = 469\n   \\]\n\n2. **Step 2:** Multiply the result by 10 (since 70 = 7 \u00d7 10):  \n   \\[\n   469 \\times 10 = 4,\\!690\n   \\]\n\n**Final Answer:**  \n\\[\n\\boxed{4690}\n\\]",
