p Explanation:**\n\n1. **Break down 13 into 10 + 3** to simplify the multiplication:\n   \\[\n   94 \\times 13 = 94 \\times (10 + 3)\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 94 by 10:**\n   \\[\n   94 \\times 10 = 940\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 94 by 3:**\n   \\[\n   94 \\times 3 = 282\n   \\]\n\n4. **Add the results of the two multiplications:**\n   \\[\n   940 + 282 = 1222\n   \\]\n\n**Verification:**\n- Using **distributive property** with \\( (90 + 4) \\times 13 \\):\n  \\[\n  90 \\times 13 = 1170 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 4 \\times 13 = 52 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad 1170 + 52 = 1222\n  \\]\n- Using **alternative method** (subtracting from 100):\n  \\[\n  100 \\times 13 = 1300 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 6 \\times 13 = 78 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad 1300 - 78 = 1222\n  \\]\n\nAll methods confirm the result is consistent.\n\n**Final Answer:**  \nThe product of 94 and 13 is \\(\\boxed{1222}\\).",
