0\\):\n\n\\[\n80 \\times 40 = 3200\n\\]\n\nNext, calculate \\(80 \\times 2\\):\n\n\\[\n80 \\times 2 = 160\n\\]\n\nAdd the two results together:\n\n\\[\n3200 + 160 = 3360\n\\]\n\nWe can verify this using another method by recognizing that \\(80 \\times 42\\) is equivalent to \\( (8 \\times 10) \\times 42 \\):\n\n\\[\n8 \\times 420 = 3360\n\\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 80 and 42 is \\(\\boxed{3360}\\).",
