      "text": "8184? Wait, that doesn't seem right. Let me check my addition again. Wait, 264 + 7920.\n\nAlternatively, 7920 + 264. 7920 + 200 is 8120, then +64 is 8184. Okay, that seems correct. So 88 \u00d7 93 is 8184?\n\nWait, but let me verify another way to be sure. Maybe using the distributive property: (90 - 2)(90 + 3). Hmm, maybe expanding it. Let's see.\n\nAlternatively, 88 \u00d7 93 can be written as (80 + 8)(90 + 3). Expanding this gives:\n\n80\u00d790 + 80\u00d73 + 8\u00d790 + 8\u00d73.\n\nCalculating each term:\n\n80\u00d790: 7200.\n\n80\u00d73: 240.\n\n8\u00d790: 720.\n\n8\u00d73: 24.\n\nAdding all these up: 7200 + 240 = 7440; 7440 + 720 = 8160; 8160 + 24 = 8184. Okay, so that matches the previous result. So that's good.\n\nAlternatively, maybe another method. Let me try using the difference of squares or something. Hmm, 88 and 93 aren't symmetric around a central number, but maybe I can adjust. Let me see.\n\nWait, 88 \u00d7 93. Let me think of 88 as (90 - 2), so (90 - 2) \u00d7 93 = 90\u00d793 - 2\u00d793.\n\nCalculating 90\u00d793: 90\u00d790 is 8100, plus 90\u00d73 is 270, so total 8100 + 270 = 8370. Then subtract 2\u00d793 = 186. So 8370 - 186 = ?\n\n8370 - 100 is 8270, then subtract 86 more: 8270 - 86 = 8184. Yep, same answer again.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using the standard algorithm again step by step.\n\nWait, let me check the initial multiplication again because I might have messed up the steps there. Let me go through it again carefully.\n\nMultiplying 88 by 93 using the standard method:\n\nFirst, write 88 \u00d7 93.\n\nStarting with the 3 in the ones place:\n\n3 \u00d7 8 (units place) = 24. Write 4, carryover 2.\n\n3 \u00d7 8 (tens place) = 24. Add the carried 2 to get 26. So first partial product is 264.\n\nThen moving to the 9 in the tens place (which is actually 90), so the next partial product is shifted one place to the left (equivalent to multiplying by 10).\n\n9 \u00d7 8 (units place of 88) = 72. Write down 2, carryover 7.\n\n9 \u00d7 8 (tens place of 88) = 72. Add the carried over 7 to get 79. So the second partial product is 7920 (since it's shifted one place left, so 792 \u00d7 10 = 7920).\n\nAdding the two partial products:\n\n264 + 7920.\n\n264 + 7920. Let's add 264 + 7920:\n\n7920 + 200 = 8120,\n\n8120 + 64 = 8184. Correct.\n\nSo, all methods are giving me 8184. I think that's correct. But just to be thorough, let me check with another approach.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps using a calculator method: since I don't have a calculator here, but maybe breaking down the numbers further.\n\nAlternatively, 88 \u00d7 93 = (80 + 8)(90 + 3) as before. Wait, already did that. Alternatively, 88 \u00d7 93 = 88 \u00d7 (90 + 3) = 88\u00d790 + 88\u00d73.\n\n88\u00d790: 88\u00d79 \u00d710. 88\u00d79 is 792, so \u00d710 is 7920.\n\n88\u00d73 is 264. So 7920 + 264 = 8184. Yep, same result.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps using the complement method or some Vedic math technique?\n\nHmm, not sure. Alternatively, let me check if 88 \u00d7 93 is equal to 89 \u00d7 92 minus or plus something. Maybe that complicates.\n\nAlternatively, let me see if 8184 divided by 88 gives me 93. Let's do the division to verify.\n\n8184 \u00f7 88. Let's see:\n\n88 \u00d7 90 = 7920. Subtract that from 8184: 8184 - 7920 = 264.\n\n264 \u00f7 88 = 3. So total is 90 + 3 = 93. Perfect, that checks out. So division confirms that 88 \u00d7 93 is indeed 8184.\n\nAlternatively, another division check: 8184 divided by 93 should be 88.\n\n93 \u00d7 80 = 7440. 8184 - 7440 = 744.\n\n93 \u00d7 8 = 744. So 80 + 8 = 88. That works too.\n\nAlright, so all methods are confirming that the product is 8184. I think that's solid. I don't see any mistakes in my calculations. I used multiple methods: standard algorithm, distributive property, breaking into easier numbers, and verification through division. All lead to the same result. So I'm confident that the answer is 8184.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 88 and 93 is \\boxed{8184}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 88 and 93, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n1. Write the numbers vertically aligned by place value:\n   ```\n    88\n  \u00d7 93\n  ------\n   ```\n\n2. Multiply 88 by the ones place (3) of 93:\n   \\[\n   3 \\times 88 = 264\n   \\]\n   This gives the partial product 264.\n\n3. Multiply 88 by the tens place (9) of 93, remembering to shift one position to the left (equivalent to multiplying by 10):\n   \\[\n   9 \\times 88 = 792\n   \\]\n   Shifting one position left gives the partial product 7920.\n\n4. Add the partial products together:\n   \\[\n   264 + 7920 = 8184\n   \\]\n\nVerification using the distributive property:\n\\[\n88 \\times 93 = (80 + 8)(90 + 3) = 80 \\times 90 + 80 \\times 3 + 8 \\times 90 + 8 \\times 3\n\\]\n\\[\n= 7200 + 240 + 720 + 24 = 8184\n\\]\n\nVerification using division:\n\\[\n8184 \\div 88 = 93 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 8184 \\div 93 = 88\n\\]\n\nAll methods confirm that the product of 88 and 93 is \\(\\boxed{8184}\\).",
