\(51 \\times 10\\):\n\n\\[\n51 \\times 10 = 510\n\\]\n\nNext, calculate \\(51 \\times 5\\):\n\n\\[\n51 \\times 5 = 255\n\\]\n\nAdd the two results together:\n\n\\[\n510 + 255 = 765\n\\]\n\nWe can verify this using another method by breaking down 15 into \\(3 \\times 5\\):\n\n\\[\n51 \\times 15 = 51 \\times (3 \\times 5) = (51 \\times 3) \\times 5\n\\]\n\nFirst, calculate \\(51 \\times 3\\):\n\n\\[\n51 \\times 3 = 153\n\\]\n\nThen multiply the result by 5:\n\n\\[\n153 \\times 5 = 765\n\\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 51 and 15 is \\(\\boxed{765}\\).",
