messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 93 and 66?', "<think>:.\nOkay, so I need to find the product of 93 and 66. Hmm, let me think about how to do this. Multiplying two numbers can sometimes be tricky, especially if they're both two-digit numbers. Maybe I can break it down into smaller parts to make it easier.\n\nFirst, I remember that multiplying numbers can be done using the distributive property. That is, 93 times 66 is the same as 93 multiplied by (60 + 6). Let me write that out: 93 × (60 + 6). Then, according to the distributive property, this becomes (93 × 60) + (93 × 6). .\n\nAlright, let me compute each part separately. Starting with 93 × 60. To make this easier, I can think of 60 as 6 × 10. So, 93 × 6 × 10. Let me first do 93 × 6. .\n\nCalculating 93 × 6: 90 × 6 is 540, and 3 × 6 is 18. Adding those together gives 540 + 18 = 558. Then, multiplying by 10 gives 558 × 10 = 5,580. Okay, so that part is 5,580.\n\nNow, the second part is 93 × 6. Wait, isn't that the same as the first part before multiplying by 10? Let me check again. 93 × 6: 90 × 6 is 540, plus 3 × 6 is 18, so 540 + 18 = 558. Yep, that's right. So, 93 × 6 is 558.\n\nNow, adding the two parts together: 5,580 + 558. Let me add these step by step. 5,580 + 500 is 6,080. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
