 \\]\n\n2. **Using the standard multiplication algorithm**:\n   - Multiply 38 by 40 by considering the 4 in the tens place:\n     \\[\n     38 \\times 4 = 152 \\quad \\text{(then shift one position to the left)} \\quad \\Rightarrow 1520\n     \\]\n\n3. **Distributive property**:\n   - Express 38 as \\(40 - 2\\) and apply the distributive property:\n     \\[\n     (40 - 2) \\times 40 = 40 \\times 40 - 2 \\times 40 = 1600 - 80 = 1520\n     \\]\n\n4. **Another distributive approach**:\n   - Break down 38 into 30 and 8:\n     \\[\n     (30 + 8) \\times 40 = 30 \\times 40 + 8 \\times 40 = 1200 + 320 = 1520\n     \\]\n\nAll methods consistently yield the result 1520. Therefore, the product of 38 and 40 is \\(\\boxed{1520}\\).",
