messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 99 and 18?', "<think>:.\nOkay, so I need to find the product of 99 and 18. Hmm, let's see. Multiplying two numbers together, right? 99 times 18. I remember that multiplication is essentially repeated addition, but adding 99 eighteen times would take forever. There must be a smarter way to do this.\n\nMaybe I can break down the numbers into smaller parts to make it easier. Let me think.. 99 is close to 100, which is a nice round number. If I can use 100 instead of 99, that might simplify things. So, 99 is 100 minus 1. So, 99 × 18 is the same as (100 - 1) × 18. .\n\nUsing the distributive property here, which says that (a - b) × c = a×c - b×c. So applying that, it would be 100×18 minus 1×18. Let me calculate each part separately. .\n\nFirst, 100 multiplied by 18. Well, multiplying by 100 is straightforward; you just add two zeros to the end of 18. So 18 becomes 1800. That part is easy. .\n\nThen, the second part is 1 times 18, which is just 18. .\n\nNow subtract the second result from the first: 1800 minus 18. Let me do that subtraction. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
