messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 99 and 20?', "<think>:.\nOkay, so I need to find the product of 99 and 20. Hmm, product means multiplication, right? So I just have to multiply 99 by 20. Let me think about how to do this step by step.\n\nFirst, I know that multiplying by 20 is the same as multiplying by 2 and then by 10. Because 20 is 2 times 10. Maybe that can make it easier. Let me try that. So if I take 99 times 2 first, what's 99 times 2? Well, 100 times 2 is 200, so 99 is one less than 100. So 200 minus 2 would be 198. So 99 times 2 is 198.\n\nNow I need to multiply that result by 10. Because we broke down 20 into 2 and 10. So 198 times 10. That should be straightforward. Multiplying by 10 just adds a zero at the end of the number. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
