1200+225=1425. That works too. \n\nSo, using different methods and cross-verifying, I can confirm that the product of 19 and 75 is 1425. \n\nI think that's solid. I don't see any mistakes in my calculations, and all the different methods lead to the same result. Therefore, I can be confident that 19 multiplied by 75 equals 1425.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 19 and 75 is calculated as follows:\n\n**Step-by-Step Explanation:**\n\n1. **Break down using distributive property:**  \n   \\( 19 \\times 75 = (20 - 1) \\times 75 \\)\n\n2. **Apply the distributive property:**  \n   \\( = (20 \\times 75) - (1 \\times 75) \\)\n\n3. **Calculate \\( 20 \\times 75 \\):**  \n   \\( 20 \\times 75 = 1500 \\)  \n   *(Because \\( 20 \\times 70 = 1400 \\) and \\( 20 \\times 5 = 100 \\); \\( 1400 + 100 = 1500 \\).)*\n\n4. **Calculate \\( 1 \\times 75 \\):**  \n   \\( 1 \\times 75 = 75 \\)\n\n5. **Subtract the results:**  \n   \\( 1500 - 75 = 1425 \\)\n\n**Verification (Alternative Method):**  \nMultiply directly:  \n- \\( 19 \\times 70 = 1330 \\)  \n- \\( 19 \\times 5 = 95 \\)  \n- Add: \\( 1330 + 95 = 1425 \\)\n\n**Final Answer:**  \nThe product of 19 and 75 is \\(\\boxed{1425}\\).",
