\u2500\u2500\n  ```\n\n2. Multiply 54 by 9 (the units digit of 39):\n   ```\n     54\n  \u00d7  9\n  \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n    486\n  ```\n   Calculation: \\(9 \\times 54 = 486\\).\n\n3. Multiply 54 by 30 (the tens digit of 39, which is 3 in the tens place):\n   ```\n     54\n  \u00d7 30\n  \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n   1620\n  ```\n   Calculation: \\(3 \\times 54 = 162\\), then shift one place to the left to account for the tens place, resulting in 1620.\n\n4. Add the two partial products together:\n   ```\n    486\n  +1620\n  \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n   2106\n  ```\n   Calculation: \\(486 + 1620 = 2106\\).\n\nTo verify, we can use the distributive property:\n- \\(54 \\times 39 = 54 \\times (40 - 1) = 54 \\times 40 - 54 \\times 1 = 2160 - 54 = 2106\\).\n\nAnother verification using the FOIL method:\n- \\((50 + 4)(30 + 9) = 50 \\times 30 + 50 \\times 9 + 4 \\times 30 + 4 \\times 9\\)\n- \\(1500 + 450 + 120 + 36 = 2106\\).\n\nAll methods confirm the result is consistent.\n\n### Final Answer\nThe product of 54 and 39 is \\boxed{2106}.",
