5760 - 100 =5660,\n\n5660 -92 =5568. Yep, same result.\n\nOkay, so multiple methods confirm that the product is 5568. I think that's solid. So the answer should be 5568.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 64 and 87 is \\boxed{5568}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 64 and 87, we can use the standard multiplication method:\n\n1. Multiply 64 by 7:\n   \\[\n   64 \\times 7 = 448\n   \\]\n2. Multiply 64 by 80 (since the 8 in 87 is in the tens place):\n   \\[\n   64 \\times 80 = 5120\n   \\]\n3. Add the two partial products together:\n   \\[\n   448 + 5120 = 5568\n   \\]\n\nWe can verify this result using different methods:\n- **Distributive Property**:\n  \\[\n  (60 + 4)(80 + 7) = 60 \\times 80 + 60 \\times 7 + 4 \\times 80 + 4 \\times 7\n  \\]\n  \\[\n  = 4800 + 420 + 320 + 28 = 5568\n  \\]\n\n- **Breaking down 87 into 90 - 3**:\n  \\[\n  64 \\times (90 - 3) = 64 \\times 90 - 64 \\times 3\n  \\]\n  \\[\n  = 5760 - 192 = 5568\n  \\]\n\nAll methods confirm that the product of 64 and 87 is \\(\\boxed{5568}\\).",
