\\boxed{1394}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 17 and 82, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n1. Write the numbers vertically:\n   ```\n    82\n  \u00d7 17\n  ------\n  ```\n\n2. Multiply 82 by 7 (the units digit of 17):\n   - \\(7 \\times 2 = 14\\), write down 4 and carry over 1.\n   - \\(7 \\times 8 = 56\\), add the carried over 1 to get 57.\n   - This gives the partial product 574.\n\n3. Multiply 82 by 1 (the tens digit of 17, which is actually 10):\n   - \\(1 \\times 2 = 2\\), \\(1 \\times 8 = 8\\), resulting in 82.\n   - Shift this result one position to the left (because it represents the tens place), giving 820.\n\n4. Add the two partial products:\n   - \\(574 + 820 = 1394\\).\n\nTo verify, we can use the distributive property:\n- Break down \\(17 \\times 82\\) as \\((10 + 7) \\times (80 + 2)\\).\n- Expand the terms:\n  - \\(10 \\times 80 = 800\\)\n  - \\(10 \\times 2 = 20\\)\n  - \\(7 \\times 80 = 560\\)\n  - \\(7 \\times 2 = 14\\)\n- Sum the results: \\(800 + 20 + 560 + 14 = 1394\\).\n\nAnother verification using the commutative property:\n- \\(82 \\times 17 = 82 \\times (10 + 7)\\)\n- \\(82 \\times 10 = 820\\)\n- \\(82 \\times 7 = 574\\)\n- Sum the results: \\(820 + 574 = 1394\\).\n\nAll methods confirm the product is \\(\\boxed{1394}\\).",
