messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 53 and 94?', "<think>:.\nOkay, so I need to find the product of 53 and 94. Hmm, let me think. Multiplying two numbers can sometimes be tricky, especially when they're both two digits. I remember that one way to do it is by breaking it down into smaller parts. Maybe I can use the distributive property here. Let me recall: the distributive property is when you split one of the numbers into tens and units, right?.\n\nSo, 53 times 94. Let me write that out as 53 × 94. Hmm, maybe I can break down 94 into 90 and 4. That way, I can do 53 times 90 plus 53 times 4. That should work. Let me try that.\n\nFirst, calculating 53 × 90. Wait, 53 times 90 is the same as 53 × 9 × 10, right? Because 90 is 9 times 10. So maybe I can compute 53 × 9 first and then multiply by 10. Let's see, 53 × 9. Let me do that step by step. 50 times 9 is 450, and 3 times 9 is 27. Adding those together, 450 + 27 = 477. Then, multiplying by 10 gives 4770. Okay, so 53 × 90 is 4770. Got that part.\n\nNow the other part is 53 × 4. Let me calculate that. 50 times 4 is 200, and 3 times 4 is 12. Adding them together gives 200 + 12 = 212. So 53 × 4 is 212.\n\nNow, adding the two results together: 4770 + 212. Let me add those. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
