messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 60 and 85?', "<think>:.\nOkay, so I need to find the product of 60 and 85. Hmm, let me think. The product means multiplication, right? So I just have to multiply 60 by 85. Alright, let me try to remember how to do this. .\n\nFirst, maybe I can break it down into simpler parts. I know that 60 times 80 is a start. Wait, but 85 is 80 plus 5. Maybe I can use the distributive property here. Let me see. .\n\nSo, 60 multiplied by 85 is the same as 60 times (80 + 5). If I split it like that, then it becomes 60*80 plus 60*5. That might be easier to calculate. Let me do each part separately. .\n\nStarting with 60 times 80. Hmm, 60 times 8 is 480, right? So if I have 60 times 80, that's 60 times 8 times 10. So 480 times 10 would be 4800. Okay, that part makes sense. .\n\nNow the other part is 60 times 5. That's straightforward. 60*5 is 300. So if I add those two results together, 4800 plus 300, that should give me the total. .\n\nAdding them up: 4800 + 300. Let me check that. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
