times 2 = 160\n\\]\n\nSubtract the second result from the first:\n\\[\n8000 - 160 = 7840\n\\]\n\n**Verification with standard multiplication:**\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n   98 \\\\\n\\times 80 \\\\\n\\hline\n  7840 \\quad (\\text{since } 98 \\times 8 \\times 10 = 784 \\times 10 = 7840)\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\n**Alternative method using \\(90 + 8\\):**\n\\[\n80 \\times (90 + 8) = (80 \\times 90) + (80 \\times 8) = 7200 + 640 = 7840\n\\]\n\nAll methods confirm the result is consistent. \n\n**Final Answer:** \\boxed{7840}",
