8) = 70\u00d780 +70\u00d78 +9\u00d780 +9\u00d78.\n\nCompute each term:\n\n70\u00d780 = 5600.\n\n70\u00d78 = 560.\n\n9\u00d780 = 720.\n\n9\u00d78 =72.\n\nNow add them all together:\n\n5600 +560 is 6160.\n\n6160 +720 is 6880.\n\n6880 +72 is 6952. Yep, same answer. So that's four different methods all confirming the same result. I think that's solid.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use calculator-like step-by-step:\n\nMultiply 79 \u00d788:\n\nFirst, 88 \u00d770 = 6160 (because 88\u00d77=616, so \u00d710 gives 6160).\n\nThen 88 \u00d79 = 792. Adding 6160 +792. Let's see, 6160 +700 is 6860, plus 92 is 6952. Yep, that works too.\n\nAll right, so regardless of the method I choose, the result is consistently 6952. Therefore, I can be confident that the product of 79 and 88 is indeed 6952. I don't think I made any mistakes here since all methods cross-validate each other. It's always good to check using different approaches to avoid any arithmetic errors. Especially when dealing with larger numbers, it's easy to miscalculate a step, but since all paths lead to the same answer, I think it's correct.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 79 and 88 is \\boxed{6952}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 79 and 88, we can use the distributive property by breaking down the numbers into smaller parts:\n\n1. **Using the distributive property:**\n   \\[\n   79 \\times 88 = 79 \\times (80 + 8) = (79 \\times 80) + (79 \\times 8)\n   \\]\n   - Calculate \\(79 \\times 80\\):\n     \\[\n     79 \\times 80 = 79 \\times 8 \\times 10 = 632 \\times 10 = 6320\n     \\]\n   - Calculate \\(79 \\times 8\\):\n     \\[\n     79 \\times 8 = 632\n     \\]\n   - Add the results:\n     \\[\n     6320 + 632 = 6952\n     \\]\n\n2. **Alternative method using another distributive approach:**\n   \\[\n   88 \\times 79 = 88 \\times (80 - 1) = (88 \\times 80) - (88 \\times 1)\n   \\]\n   - Calculate \\(88 \\times 80\\):\n     \\[\n     88 \\times 80 = 88 \\times 8 \\times 10 = 704 \\times 10 = 7040\n     \\]\n   - Calculate \\(88 \\times 1\\):\n     \\[\n     88 \\times 1 = 88\n     \\]\n   - Subtract the results:\n     \\[\n     7040 - 88 = 6952\n     \\]\n\n3. **Breaking down both numbers:**\n   \\[\n   (70 + 9)(80 + 8) = 70 \\times 80 + 70 \\times 8 + 9 \\times 80 + 9 \\times 8\n   \\]\n   - Calculate each term:\n     \\[\n     70 \\times 80 = 5600, \\quad 70 \\times 8 = 560, \\quad 9 \\times 80 = 720, \\quad 9 \\times 8 = 72\n     \\]\n   - Add the results:\n     \\[\n     5600 + 560 + 720 + 72 = 6952\n     \\]\n\nAll methods confirm that the product of 79 and 88 is \\(\\boxed{6952}\\).",
