ernatively, maybe use another approach such as the difference of squares formula? Let's see, but that requires something like (a + b)(a -b) = a\u00b2 - b\u00b2, but 89 and 88 aren't in that form. Unless I can adjust the numbers.\n\nAlternatively, maybe express one of the numbers as a difference. Let me see, but perhaps this is overcomplicating. Since all the methods so far give 7832, I can be confident that's the correct answer.\n\nWait, just to make sure, perhaps do the multiplication step by step again, but more carefully.\n\nLet me write it out:\n\nMultiplying 89 by 88:\n\nFirst, write 89\n\ntimes 88\n\n________\n\nStarting with the units digit of the bottom number (8):\n\n8 * 9 = 72. Write down 2, carryover 7.\n\n8 * 8 = 64, plus 7 is 71. So first partial product is 712.\n\nThen, moving to the tens digit of 88, which is 8 (representing 80):\n\nSo we need to multiply 89 by 80. Since it's the tens place, the result is shifted one position to the left.\n\nSo, 8 *9 =72, write down 2, carryover7.\n\n8*8 =64 +7=71, so that gives 712, but shifted left, so 7120.\n\nNow add 712 and 7120:\n\n712\n\n+7120\n\n______\n\nAdding units digits: 2 +0=2\n\nTens place:1 +2=3\n\nHundreds place: 7 +1=8\n\nThousands place: 1 (from 7120) +0=1. Wait, wait, hold on, actually, let me align them properly:\n\n   712\n\n+7120\n\n--------\n\nLet's write the numbers aligned:\n\n   712\n\n+7120\n\nAlign the digits:\n\n   712\n\n+7120\n\nIt's actually:\n\n   712\n\n+7120\n\n= 712 + 7120 = 7832.\n\nWait, but if I write them vertically:\n\n  712\n\n+7120\n\n------\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nUnits place: 2 + 0 =2\n\nTens place:1 + 2 = 3\n\nHundreds place:7 +1 =8\n\nThousands place: 0 (from 712) +7 (from 7120) =7.\n\nWait, so that gives 7 (thousands), 8 (hundreds), 3 (tens), 2 (units) \u2192 7832. Correct. So that adds up.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps using another method, like breaking down 89 into 80 +9 and 88 into 80 +8, then using the distributive property:\n\n(80 +9)(80 +8) = 80*80 + 80*8 +9*80 +9*8.\n\nCompute each term:\n\n80*80 = 6400\n\n80*8 = 640\n\n9*80 = 720\n\n9*8 =72\n\nAdd them all together:\n\n6400 + 640 =7040\n\n7040 +720 =7760\n\n7760 +72 =7832. Yep, same result again.\n\nAlright, so all these methods are giving me the same answer, so I feel confident that 89 multiplied by 88 is indeed 7832.\n\nWait, just to be absolutely thorough, maybe use another approach, like the Russian peasant multiplication or something. Let's see.\n\nRussian peasant multiplication involves doubling and halving. Let me try that.\n\nStart with two columns, one for each number. Let's set 89 and 88.\n\nWe need to halve the first number (discarding remainders) and double the second number until the first column reaches 1.\n\nBut since 89 is odd, let's see:\n\nFirst row: 89 | 88\n\nNext, halve 89 \u2192 44.5, but we discard the remainder, so 44. Double 88 \u2192 176.\n\nSecond row: 44 | 176\n\nNow, 44 is even, so halve again to 22, double 176 to 352.\n\nThird row:22 | 352\n\nHalve 22 to 11, double 352 to 704.\n\nFourth row:11 |704\n\n11 is odd, so next row: halve 11 to 5 (discard .5), double 704 to 1408.\n\nFifth row:5 |1408\n\n5 is odd, halve to 2, double to 2816.\n\nSixth row:2 | 2816\n\n2 is even, halve to 1, double to 5632.\n\nSeventh row:1 |5632\n\nNow, we discard any rows where the first column is even. Wait, actually, in the Russian peasant method, you add the numbers in the second column when the first column is odd. Let me recall the exact steps:\n\n- Start with the two numbers.\n\n- Repeatedly halve the first number (discarding remainders) and double the second number until the first column is 1.\n\n- Then add up all the numbers in the second column that correspond to odd numbers in the first column.\n\nSo let's go through the rows again, noting which first numbers are odd:\n\nFirst row:89 (odd) \u2192 include 88\n\nSecond row:44 (even) \u2192 exclude 176\n\nThird row:22 (even) \u2192 exclude 352\n\nFourth row:11 (odd) \u2192 include 704\n\nFifth row:5 (odd) \u2