0 = 2000\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   40 \\times 2 = 80\n   \\]\n4. Add the results together:\n   \\[\n   2000 + 80 = 2080\n   \\]\n\nVerification using the standard multiplication algorithm:\n- Multiply 40 by 2: \\(40 \\times 2 = 80\\)\n- Multiply 40 by 50: \\(40 \\times 50 = 2000\\)\n- Add the results: \\(2000 + 80 = 2080\\)\n\nAnother method:\n- Convert 40 to \\(4 \\times 10\\) and multiply by 52:\n  \\[\n  (4 \\times 52) \\times 10 = 208 \\times 10 = 2080\n  \\]\n\nAll methods confirm the result is consistent.\n\n### Final Answer\nThe product of 40 and 52 is \\boxed{2080}.",
