 \\)\n\n2. **Standard vertical multiplication**:\n   - Multiply 34 by 3 (ones place): \\( 34 \\times 3 = 102 \\)\n   - Multiply 34 by 10 (tens place): \\( 34 \\times 10 = 340 \\)\n   - Adding the results: \\( 102 + 340 = 442 \\)\n\n3. **Distributive property**:\n   - Expand \\( (30 + 4)(10 + 3) \\):\n     - \\( 30 \\times 10 = 300 \\)\n     - \\( 30 \\times 3 = 90 \\)\n     - \\( 4 \\times 10 = 40 \\)\n     - \\( 4 \\times 3 = 12 \\)\n   - Adding the terms: \\( 300 + 90 + 40 + 12 = 442 \\)\n\n4. **Reversing the numbers**:\n   - \\( 13 \\times 30 = 390 \\)\n   - \\( 13 \\times 4 = 52 \\)\n   - Adding the results: \\( 390 + 52 = 442 \\)\n\nAll methods consistently yield the result 442.\n\n### Final Answer\nThe product of 34 and 13 is \\boxed{442}.",
