      "text": "3000 + 150 equals 3150. Wait, hold on, let me double-check that to make sure I didn't make a mistake.\n\nAlternatively, maybe there's another way to compute this. Let me try multiplying 42 by 75 the standard way, just to confirm.\n\nWriting it out vertically:\n\n\u2003\u00a042\n\u00d775\n------\nFirst multiply 42 by 5: 42*5 = 210.\n\nThen multiply 42 by 70 (since the 7 is in the tens place, so it's 70). 42*70. Let me compute that. 42*7 is 294, so 42*70 is 2940.\n\nNow add the two results: 210 + 2940. Let's see, 210 + 2940. 2940 + 200 is 3140, then +10 more is 3150. Okay, same answer. That matches the first method. So that's reassuring.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use another method, like breaking down 75 into factors. 75 is 25 times 3, or 75 is 100 minus 25. Hmm, let's see. Let's try 75 as 75 = 25 * 3. Then 42 * 75 would be 42 *25 *3. Maybe compute 42*25 first. 42*25. 25 is a quarter of 100, so 42*25 is like 42*(100/4) which is (42/4)*100. Wait, 42 divided by 4 is 10.5, so 10.5*100 is 1050? Wait, that can't be right. Let me actually compute 42*25 properly.\n\nAlternatively, 25 times 40 is 1000, and 25 times 2 is 50, so 25*(40 +2)=1000 +50 = 1050. So 42*25 is 1050. Then multiply by 3: 1050*3. 1000*3 is 3000, and 50*3 is 150, so 3000 +150 = 3150. Same answer again. Hmm, that works too.\n\nAnother way: 42 times 75. Maybe notice that 75 is 3/4 of 100. Wait, not sure. Alternatively, 42 times 75 can be thought of as (40 +2)(70 +5). Wait, that's expanding it out. Let me try that.\n\n(40 + 2)(70 +5) = 40*70 + 40*5 + 2*70 + 2*5.\n\nCalculating each term:\n\n40*70 = 2800,\n\n40*5 = 200,\n\n2*70 = 140,\n\n2*5 =10.\n\nAdding all those together: 2800 + 200 is 3000, plus 140 is 3140, plus 10 is 3150. Yep, same result again. So all methods point to 3150.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using some other trick. Let me think. Since 75 is 3/4 of 100, so 42 * 75 = 42 * (3/4)*100. So that would be (42*3)/4 *100? Wait, no, actually 42*(3/4)*100 = (42*3)*(100/4). Wait, maybe that's complicating it.\n\nAlternatively, 42*75 = (42/4)*300, but not sure that's helpful. Hmm, maybe not. Anyway, since all methods so far give me 3150, I can be confident that's the right answer. Let me check with a calculator approach.\n\nWait, 42 multiplied by 75. Let me do 42*75:\n\n42*70 is 2940, plus 42*5 is 210, totaling 3150. Yep. All right, so I think that's solid. I don't see any mistakes in my calculations. So the product of 42 and 75 is 3150.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 42 and 75 is \\boxed{3150}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 42 and 75, we can use the distributive property by breaking down the numbers into smaller parts:\n\n1. Break down 42 into 40 + 2:\n   \\[\n   42 \\times 75 = (40 + 2) \\times 75\n   \\]\n2. Apply the distributive property:\n   \\[\n   (40 + 2) \\times 75 = 40 \\times 75 + 2 \\times 75\n   \\]\n3. Calculate each part separately:\n   - For \\(40 \\times 75\\):\n     \\[\n     40 \\times 75 = 40 \\times (70 + 5) = 40 \\times 70 + 40 \\times 5 = 2800 + 200 = 3000\n     \\]\n   - For \\(2 \\times 75\\):\n     \\[\n     2 \\times 75 = 150\n     \\]\n4. Add the results of the two parts:\n   \\[\n   3000 + 150 = 3150\n   \\]\n\nWe can verify this result using another method by multiplying 42 by 75 directly:\n1. Multiply 42 by 5:\n   \\[\n   42 \\times 5 = 210\n   \\]\n2. Multiply 42 by 70 (since 75 is 70 + 5, and 7 is in the tens place):\n   \\[\n   42 \\times 70 = 2940\n   \\]\n3. Add the two results:\n   \\[\n   210 + 2940 = 3150\n   \\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 42 and 75 is \\(\\boxed{3150}\\).",
