messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 82 and 68?', "<think>:.\nOkay, so I need to find the product of 82 and 68. Hmm, let me think. Multiplying two-digit numbers can sometimes be tricky, but I remember there are different methods to do this. Maybe I can use the standard algorithm, or perhaps there's a quicker way by breaking it down?.\n\nFirst, let me recall the standard multiplication method. If I write 82 times 68, I can do it vertically. Let me set it up:.\n\n```.\n   82.\nx 68.\n-------.\n```.\n\nStarting with the ones place of the bottom number (which is 8), I multiply it by 82. So 8 times 2 is 16. I write down 6 and carry over 1. Then 8 times 8 is 64, plus the carried 1 makes 65. So that gives me 656. .\n\nNext, I move to the tens place of 68, which is 6. Since this is the tens place, I need to remember to shift one position to the left. So I'll write a 0 under the 6 of the first partial product. Then multiply 6 by 2, which is 12. Write down 2 and carry over 1. Then 6 times 8 is 48, plus the 1 gives 49. So that gives me 4920. .\n\nNow, adding the two partial products together: .\n\n656.\n+4920.\n-------. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
