 56*40=2240. 2464-2240=224. Then 56*4=224. So 40+4=44. So that works too. \n\nTherefore, I'm confident the product of 44 and 56 is 2464.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 44 and 56 can be calculated using different methods, all leading to the same result:\n\n1. **Distributive Property**:\n   \\[\n   (40 + 4)(50 + 6) = 40 \\times 50 + 40 \\times 6 + 4 \\times 50 + 4 \\times 6 = 2000 + 240 + 200 + 24 = 2464\n   \\]\n\n2. **Difference of Squares**:\n   \\[\n   (50 - 6)(50 + 6) = 50^2 - 6^2 = 2500 - 36 = 2464\n   \\]\n\n3. **Standard Multiplication**:\n   \\[\n   44 \\times 56 = 44 \\times (50 + 6) = (44 \\times 50) + (44 \\times 6) = 2200 + 264 = 2464\n   \\]\n\n**Verification**:\n- Dividing \\(2464 \\div 44 = 56\\)\n- Dividing \\(2464 \\div 56 = 44\\)\n\nAll methods confirm the result is consistent.\n\n**Answer**: \\(\\boxed{2464}\\)",
