messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 13 and 90?', "<think>:.\nOkay, so I need to find the product of 13 and 90. Hmm, product means multiplication, right? Let me make sure I remember that correctly. Yeah, product is when you multiply two numbers together. So, 13 multiplied by 90. Alright, let me think about how to do this.\n\nFirst, maybe I can break it down into simpler parts. 90 is the same as 9 times 10, so maybe I can use that to make the multiplication easier. Let me try that. So, 13 times 90 is the same as 13 times 9 times 10. Wait, that might work. Let me do 13 times 9 first. .\n\nWhat's 13 times 9? Let me recall my multiplication tables. 9 times 10 is 90, and then subtract 9, so 90 minus 9 is 81. Wait, no, that would be 9 times 9. Wait, no, hold on. 13 times 9. Hmm, maybe I should do it step by step. .\n\n13 times 9 can be thought of as 10 times 9 plus 3 times 9. Yeah, that's distributive property. So 10*9 is 90, and 3*9 is 27. Then add them together. 90 plus 27 is 117. Okay, so 13 times 9 is 117. Then I need to multiply that by 10? Wait, no, actually, since I broke down 90 into 9*10, the original problem was 13*(9*10) which is (13*9)*10. So that would be 117*10. .\n\nMultiplying by 10 is straightforward, just add a zero at the end. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
