p, that seems consistent. I think that's the correct product.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 31 and 69 is \\boxed{2139}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 31 and 69, we can use the distributive property by breaking down 69 into 70 - 1:\n\n\\[\n31 \\times 69 = 31 \\times (70 - 1)\n\\]\n\nFirst, calculate \\(31 \\times 70\\):\n\n\\[\n31 \\times 70 = 31 \\times 7 \\times 10 = 217 \\times 10 = 2170\n\\]\n\nNext, subtract \\(31 \\times 1\\):\n\n\\[\n2170 - 31 = 2139\n\\]\n\nTo verify, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n   \\quad 31 \\\\\n\\times 69 \\\\\n\\hline\n   279 \\quad (\\text{31} \\times 9) \\\\\n+1860 \\quad (\\text{31} \\times 60, \\text{shifted one position left}) \\\\\n\\hline\n   2139 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product is 2139. Additionally, using the expansion method:\n\n\\[\n(30 + 1)(70 - 1) = 30 \\times 70 + 30 \\times (-1) + 1 \\times 70 + 1 \\times (-1)\n\\]\n\\[\n= 2100 - 30 + 70 - 1 = 2100 + 40 - 1 = 2139\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 31 and 69 is \\boxed{2139}.",
