messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 56 and 20?', "<think>:.\nOkay, so I need to find the product of 56 and 20. Hmm, product means multiplication, right? Let me make sure I remember that correctly. Yeah, product is when you multiply two numbers together. So, 56 multiplied by 20. Alright, let me think about how to do this.\n\nFirst, maybe I can break it down into simpler parts. 20 is the same as 2 times 10, so maybe I can use that to make the multiplication easier. Let me try that. If I take 56 times 2 first, that should be straightforward. 56 times 2 is.. let's see, 50 times 2 is 100, and 6 times 2 is 12, so adding those together gives 112. Okay, so 56 times 2 is 112. Then I need to multiply that result by 10 because 2 times 10 is 20. Wait, no, actually, hold on. Since 20 is 2 times 10, then 56 times 20 is the same as 56 times 2 times 10. So first multiply 56 by 2 to get 112, then multiply that by 10. Multiplying by 10 is easy, just add a zero at the end. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
