eds), 9 (tens), 3 (units): 2993. Ah, there we go! I must have miscalculated earlier.\n\nSo the thousands digit is 2, hundreds 9, tens 9, units 3 \u2192 2993. That matches the other methods. So the lattice method also confirms it's 2993. I must have added incorrectly before.\n\nTherefore, after going through multiple methods\u2014standard multiplication, distributive property, and lattice multiplication\u2014all confirm that 73 multiplied by 41 is 2993. I think that settles it. Initially, I was doubting myself, but verifying through different techniques helped ensure the answer is correct.\n\nJust to recap:\n\n- 73 times 40 is 2920.\n\n- 73 times 1 is 73.\n\n- Adding them gives 2920 +73 =2993.\n\nYep. Definitely, that's the right answer. So the product of 73 and 41 is 2993.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 73 and 41 is \\boxed{2993}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 73 and 41, we can use multiple methods to ensure accuracy:\n\n1. **Standard Multiplication**:\n   - Multiply 73 by 1 (ones place): \\(73 \\times 1 = 73\\).\n   - Multiply 73 by 40 (tens place): \\(73 \\times 40 = 2920\\).\n   - Add the results: \\(2920 + 73 = 2993\\).\n\n2. **Distributive Property**:\n   - Break down the numbers: \\(73 = 70 + 3\\) and \\(41 = 40 + 1\\).\n   - Expand using the distributive property:\n     \\[\n     (70 + 3)(40 + 1) = 70 \\times 40 + 70 \\times 1 + 3 \\times 40 + 3 \\times 1\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     = 2800 + 70 + 120 + 3 = 2800 + 70 = 2870; \\quad 2870 + 120 = 2990; \\quad 2990 + 3 = 2993\n     \\]\n\n3. **Lattice Method**:\n   - Set up a 2x2 grid for 73 (top) and 41 (right).\n   - Multiply each digit pair and split results into tens and units:\n     - \\(7 \\times 4 = 28\\) (2 above, 8 below)\n     - \\(3 \\times 4 = 12\\) (1 above, 2 below)\n     - \\(7 \\times 1 = 7\\) (0 above, 7 below)\n     - \\(3 \\times 1 = 3\\) (0 above, 3 below)\n   - Sum along the diagonals:\n     - Units: 3\n     - Tens: \\(7 + 2 = 9\\)\n     - Hundreds: \\(8 + 1 + 0 = 9\\)\n     - Thousa