n be confident that 97 multiplied by 83 is 8051. \n\nI think that's solid. I don't see any mistakes in my calculations. So the answer should be 8051. \n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 97 and 83 is \\boxed{8051}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 97 and 83, we can use multiple methods to ensure accuracy:\n\n1. **Using the Vedic Math Trick for Numbers Close to 100**:\n   - \\(97 = 100 - 3\\) and \\(83 = 100 - 17\\)\n   - Applying the formula \\((100 - a)(100 - b) = 100 \\times (100 - a - b) + (a \\times b)\\):\n     - \\(100 - 3 - 17 = 80\\)\n     - \\(3 \\times 17 = 51\\)\n     - Combining these: \\(100 \\times 80 + 51 = 8000 + 51 = 8051\\)\n\n2. **Standard Multiplication**:\n   - \\(97 \\times 83\\):\n     - \\(97 \\times 3 = 291\\)\n     - \\(97 \\times 80 = 7760\\)\n     - Adding results: \\(291 + 7760 = 8051\\)\n\n3. **Distributive Property**:\n   - \\(97 \\times 83 = (90 + 7)(80 + 3)\\)\n     - \\(90 \\times 80 = 7200\\)\n     - \\(90 \\times 3 = 270\\)\n     - \\(7 \\times 80 = 560\\)\n     - \\(7 \\times 3 = 21\\)\n     - Adding these: \\(7200 + 270 + 560 + 21 = 8051\\)\n\n4. **Base 80 Method**:\n   - \\(97 = 80 + 17\\) and \\(83 = 80 + 3\\)\n   - Applying the formula \\((a + b)(a + c) = a^2 + a(b + c) + bc\\):\n     - \\(80^2 + 80 \\times (17 + 3) + 17 \\times 3\\)\n     - \\(6400 + 1600 + 51 = 8051\\)\n\nAll methods confirm the product of 97 and 83 is \\(\\boxed{8051}\\).",
