messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 64 and 37?', '<think>:.\nOkay, let me figure out how to multiply 64 by 37. Hmm, I remember that multiplying two numbers can be done by breaking them down into smaller parts. Maybe I can use the distributive property here. Let me think.. 64 times 37. .\n\nFirst, I can split 37 into 30 and 7 because 30 + 7 is 37. So that would make the problem 64*(30 + 7). Using the distributive property, that becomes 64*30 plus 64*7. Alright, let me calculate each part separately.\n\nStarting with 64*30. Well, 64 times 3 is 192, right? So if I multiply that by 10 to get the 30, it would be 192*10 = 1920. Wait, no, actually, 30 is 3*10, so 64*3 is 192, then times 10 gives 1920. Yeah, that seems right.\n\nNow the other part is 64*7. Let me do that. 60*7 is 420, and 4*7 is 28. Adding those together gives 420 + 28 = 448. So 64*7 is 448.\n\nNow I need to add the two results together: 1920 + 448. Let me add them step by step. Therefore, my final answer is: ']]
