e the lattice method, but that might take longer. Let me see. Wait, maybe not necessary since all methods so far give the same answer. Alternatively, check for divisibility. Let me see if 2982 divided by 42 gives 71. Let me do the division.\n\nDivide 2982 \u00f7 42. Let's see:\n\n42 \u00d7 70 = 2940. Subtract that from 2982: 2982 -2940 =42. Then 42 \u00f742 =1. So total is 70+1=71. Perfect, that works. So that confirms that 42\u00d771=2982.\n\nAlternatively, divide 2982 by 71 to see if it gives 42. Let's check that too.\n\n71 \u00d740 = 2840. 2982 -2840 =142. 71\u00d72=142. So 40+2=42. So that works as well. So division confirms it.\n\nTherefore, I'm pretty confident the answer is 2982. I think that's solid. Let me just recap all the steps once more to ensure I didn't skip anything.\n\nFirst method: standard multiplication:\n\n42  \n\u00d7\u00a071  \n------  \n42 (from 42\u00d71)  \n2940 (from 42\u00d770, shifted left)  \nTotal: 2982.\n\nSecond method: expanding (40+2)(70+1)=2800+40+140+2=2982.\n\nThird method: 42\u00d770=2940; 2940+42=2982.\n\nFourth method: 71\u00d740=2840; 71\u00d72=142; 2840+142=2982.\n\nFifth method: division check: 2982 \u00f742=71 and 2982 \u00f771=42.\n\nAll methods confirm the same result. So I can't see any mistake here. Therefore, the product of 42 and 71 is 2982.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 42 and 71 is \\boxed{2982}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 42 and 71, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n1. Multiply 42 by 1 (the units place of 71):\n   \\[\n   42 \\times 1 = 42\n   \\]\n\n2. Multiply 42 by 70 (the tens place of 71, which is 7 in the tens place, so 70):\n   \\[\n   42 \\times 70 = 42 \\times 7 \\times 10 = 294 \\times 10 = 2940\n   \\]\n\n3. Add the results of the two multiplications:\n   \\[\n   42 + 2940 = 2982\n   \\]\n\nWe can verify this result using different methods:\n\n- **Distributive Property**:\n  \\[\n  (40 + 2) \\times (70 + 1) = 40 \\times 70 + 40 \\times 1 + 2 \\times 70 + 2 \\times 1\n  \\]\n  \\[\n  = 2800 + 40 + 140 + 2 = 2982\n  \\]\n\n- **Division Check**:\n  - Dividing 2982 by 42 gives 71:\n    \\[\n    2982 \\div 42 = 71\n    \\]\n  - Dividing 2982 by 71 gives 42:\n    \\[\n    2982 \\div 71 = 42\n    \\]\n\nAll methods confirm the result is consistent. Therefore, the product of 42 and 71 is \\(\\boxed{2982}\\).",
