tiply 32 by 0 (units place of 80), which is 0, then multiply 32 by 8 (tens place), which is 256, but shifted one position to the left, so 2560. Adding the two gives 2560 + 0 = 2560. \n\nYes, that's exactly right. \n\nAlternatively, maybe using distributive property again. \n\n32 * 80 = (30 + 2) * (80) = 30*80 + 2*80 = 2400 + 160 = 2560. \n\nYep, same result. \n\nHmm, I think I've checked it multiple ways. Seems solid. I don't think I made a mistake here. The answer should be 2560.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 32 and 80 is calculated as follows:\n\nFirst, recognize that multiplying by 80 is the same as multiplying by 8 and then by 10:\n\\[\n32 \\times 80 = 32 \\times (8 \\times 10) = (32 \\times 8) \\times 10\n\\]\n\nCalculate \\(32 \\times 8\\):\n\\[\n32 \\times 8 = 256\n\\]\n\nThen multiply the result by 10:\n\\[\n256 \\times 10 = 2560\n\\]\n\n**Verification using the distributive property:**\n\\[\n32 \\times 80 = (30 + 2) \\times 80 = 30 \\times 80 + 2 \\times 80 = 2400 + 160 = 2560\n\\]\n\nBoth methods confirm the result is consistent.\n\n**Answer:** \\(\\boxed{2560}\\)",
