oxed{1472}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 32 and 46, we can use multiple methods to ensure accuracy.\n\n**Method 1: Standard Algorithm**\n\n1. Multiply 32 by 6 (the ones place of 46):\n   \\[\n   32 \\times 6 = 192\n   \\]\n2. Multiply 32 by 40 (the tens place of 46, which is 4 shifted one position to the left):\n   \\[\n   32 \\times 40 = 1280\n   \\]\n3. Add the partial products:\n   \\[\n   192 + 1280 = 1472\n   \\]\n\n**Method 2: Distributive Property**\n\n1. Break down the numbers:\n   \\[\n   (30 + 2) \\times (40 + 6)\n   \\]\n2. Expand and calculate each term:\n   \\[\n   30 \\times 40 + 30 \\times 6 + 2 \\times 40 + 2 \\times 6 = 1200 + 180 + 80 + 12\n   \\]\n3. Sum the results:\n   \\[\n   1200 + 180 = 1380 \\\\\n   1380 + 80 = 1460 \\\\\n   1460 + 12 = 1472\n   \\]\n\n**Method 3: Alternative Breakdown**\n\n1. Use the distributive property with 32:\n   \\[\n   32 \\times 46 = 30 \\times 46 + 2 \\times 46\n   \\]\n2. Calculate each term:\n   \\[\n   30 \\times 46 = 1380 \\\\\n   2 \\times 46 = 92\n   \\]\n3. Sum the results:\n   \\[\n   1380 + 92 = 1472\n   \\]\n\n**Method 4: Using 50 - 4**\n\n1. Rewrite 46 as 50 - 4:\n   \\[\n   32 \\times (50 - 4) = 32 \\times 50 - 32 \\times 4\n   \\]\n2. Calculate each term:\n   \\[\n   32 \\times 50 = 1600 \\\\\n   32 \\times 4 = 128\n   \\]\n3. Subtract the results:\n   \\[\n   1600 - 128 = 1472\n   \\]\n\nAll methods confirm that the product of 32 and 46 is \\(\\boxed{1472}\\).",
