messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 12 and 63?', "<think>:.\nOkay, so I need to find the product of 12 and 63. Let me think about how to do this step by step. First, I remember that the product means multiplication, right? So basically, I have to multiply 12 by 63.\n\nHmm, how do I multiply these two numbers? Let me recall the standard multiplication method. Maybe breaking it down into smaller parts would help. Let me try the distributive property. So, 12 times 63 can be split into 12 times 60 plus 12 times 3. That should make it easier.\n\nCalculating 12 times 60 first. Well, 12 times 6 is 72, so 12 times 60 would be 720 because I add a zero at the end. Then, 12 times 3 is straightforward—that's 36. Now, adding those two results together: 720 plus 36. Let me add the tens first. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
