 verification:\n\n1. **Decomposition Method**:\n   - Recognize that 38 is 40 minus 2.\n   - Compute \\(40 \\times 90 = 3600\\).\n   - Subtract the excess: \\(2 \\times 90 = 180\\).\n   - Result: \\(3600 - 180 = 3420\\).\n\n2. **Standard Multiplication**:\n   - Multiply 38 by 90:\n     ```\n      38\n    \u00d7 90\n    -----\n      0  (38 \u00d7 0)\n    3420  (38 \u00d7 90, shifted one position left)\n    -----\n     3420\n    ```\n\n3. **Distributive Property**:\n   - Break into \\( (30 + 8) \\times 90 \\).\n   - Calculate \\(30 \\times 90 = 2700\\) and \\(8 \\times 90 = 720\\).\n   - Sum the results: \\(2700 + 720 = 3420\\).\n\n4. **Verification via Division**:\n   - Divide the result by one of the factors: \\(3420 \u00f7 90 = 38\\), confirming correctness.\n\nAll methods consistently yield **3420**. \n\n**Answer:** The product of 38 and 90 is \\boxed{3420}.",
