ing each part separately:\n- \\(41 \\times 10 = 410\\)\n- \\(41 \\times 7 = 287\\) (since \\(40 \\times 7 = 280\\) and \\(1 \\times 7 = 7\\), adding these gives \\(280 + 7 = 287\\))\n\nAdding the results together:\n\\[\n410 + 287 = 697\n\\]\n\nWe can verify this using another method by expressing 17 as \\(20 - 3\\):\n\\[\n41 \\times 17 = 41 \\times (20 - 3) = 41 \\times 20 - 41 \\times 3\n\\]\n\nCalculating each part separately:\n- \\(41 \\times 20 = 820\\)\n- \\(41 \\times 3 = 123\\)\n\nSubtracting the results:\n\\[\n820 - 123 = 697\n\\]\n\nAnother verification method involves multiplying 17 by 40 and then adding 17:\n\\[\n17 \\times 40 = 680 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 680 + 17 = 697\n\\]\n\nAll methods confirm that the product of 41 and 17 is \\(\\boxed{697}\\).",
