se the distributive property by breaking down 12 into 10 and 2:\n\n\\[\n86 \\times 12 = 86 \\times (10 + 2) = 86 \\times 10 + 86 \\times 2\n\\]\n\nFirst, calculate \\(86 \\times 10\\):\n\n\\[\n86 \\times 10 = 860\n\\]\n\nNext, calculate \\(86 \\times 2\\):\n\n\\[\n86 \\times 2 = 172\n\\]\n\nAdd the results of these two calculations together:\n\n\\[\n860 + 172 = 1032\n\\]\n\nWe can verify this result using another method, such as the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n   86 \\\\\n\\times 12 \\\\\n\\hline\n   172 \\quad (\\text{which is } 86 \\times 2) \\\\\n+ 860 \\quad (\\text{which is } 86 \\times 10) \\\\\n\\hline\n  1032 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 86 and 12 is \\(\\boxed{1032}\\).",
