      "text": "2100 plus 300 is 2400, then plus 36 is 2436. Wait, no, 2100 + 336. Let me check again. 2100 + 300 is 2400, then +36 is indeed 2436. Hmm, so is that the answer?\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can do it another way to confirm. Let me try the standard multiplication algorithm. Writing it out vertically:\n\n\u2003\u00a058  \n\u00d7\u00a042  \n------  \nFirst multiply 58 by 2: that's 116.  \nThen multiply 58 by 40 (since the 4 is in the tens place). So 58 \u00d7 40.  \n58 \u00d7 4 is 232, so times 10 is 2320.  \nNow add 116 and 2320 together.  \n116 + 2320: 2320 + 100 is 2420, plus 16 is 2436. Okay, same result. That's good.\n\nWait, just to be thorough, maybe I can check using another method. How about the difference of squares or something? Let me see. 58 and 42, hmm, maybe express them as (50 + 8) and (40 + 2). But that's similar to my first approach. Alternatively, is there a way to use the identity (a + b)(a - b) = a\u00b2 - b\u00b2? Hmm, but 58 and 42 aren't equidistant from a central number. Let me see: 58 and 42 have an average of (58 + 42)/2 = 50. So 58 is 50 +8, and 42 is 50 -8? Wait, no, 50 -8 is 42? 50 -8 is 42? Wait, 50 minus 8 is 42? 50 minus 8 is 42? Wait, 50 minus 8 is 42? Let me check that: 50 minus 8 is 42? 50 -8 is 42? 50 -8 is 42? Wait, 50 minus 8 is 42? No, 50 minus 8 is 42? Wait, 50 minus 8 is 42? Wait, 50 minus 8 equals 42? Let me compute 50-8: that is 42. Oh! Wait really? 50 minus 8 is 42? Wait a second, 50 minus 8 is indeed 42? Because 42 +8 is 50. So yes, 50-8=42. So that means 58 is 50+8, and 42 is 50-8. Therefore, 58 \u00d742 is (50 +8)(50 -8). Which is a difference of squares: 50\u00b2 minus 8\u00b2. That would be 2500 - 64. Let me compute that: 2500 minus 60 is 2440, minus 4 more is 2436. So that also gives the same answer. Wow, that was a smarter way. I should have thought of that first. \n\nSo all three methods give me 2436. That gives me confidence that the answer is correct. Let me recap:\n\n1. Distributive property splitting 58 into 50 +8: (50\u00d742)+(8\u00d742)=2100+336=2436.\n\n2. Standard vertical multiplication: 58\u00d72=116, 58\u00d740=2320, sum=2436.\n\n3. Difference of squares since 58 and 42 are equidistant from 50: (50+8)(50-8)=50\u00b2-8\u00b2=2500-64=2436.\n\nAll methods confirm that the product is 2436. I think that's solid. I don't see any mistakes in my calculations, so I think that's the right answer.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 58 and 42 is \\boxed{2436}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 58 and 42, we can use multiple methods to ensure accuracy:\n\n1. **Distributive Property**:\n   - Break down 58 into 50 and 8:\n     \\[\n     58 \\times 42 = (50 + 8) \\times 42 = (50 \\times 42) + (8 \\times 42)\n     \\]\n   - Calculate each part:\n     \\[\n     50 \\times 42 = 2100 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 8 \\times 42 = 336\n     \\]\n   - Sum the results:\n     \\[\n     2100 + 336 = 2436\n     \\]\n\n2. **Standard Multiplication Algorithm**:\n   - Multiply 58 by 2 and then by 40:\n     \\[\n     58 \\times 2 = 116 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 58 \\times 40 = 2320\n     \\]\n   - Sum the results:\n     \\[\n     116 + 2320 = 2436\n     \\]\n\n3. **Difference of Squares**:\n   - Recognize that 58 and 42 are equidistant from 50:\n     \\[\n     58 = 50 + 8 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 42 = 50 - 8\n     \\]\n   - Apply the difference of squares formula:\n     \\[\n     (50 + 8)(50 - 8) = 50^2 - 8^2 = 2500 - 64 = 2436\n     \\]\n\nAll methods confirm that the product of 58 and 42 is \\(\\boxed{2436}\\).",
