 try.\n\nWait, maybe overcomplicating. Alternatively, maybe use the fact that 45 is half of 90, but not sure if that helps. Alternatively, 68 \u00d7 45 is the same as (70 -2)\u00d745 as above. But since I did that already.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps using fractions. 45 is 45/1, so multiplying 68*45. Alternatively, maybe 68*(40 +5) as I did first. Yeah, that's the same as the first method. Either way.\n\nAlternatively, using the commutative property, maybe 45 \u00d768. Let me try multiplying 45 by 68:\n\n45 \u00d7 60 = 2700,\n\n45 \u00d78 = 360,\n\nAdding them gives 2700 + 360 = 3060. There we go again. So, same answer.\n\nHmm, so all methods confirm that it's 3060. Therefore, I can be confident that the product of 68 and 45 is 3060.\n\nWait, but just to make sure, perhaps using a calculator? Well, since I don't have a calculator here, but let me do it step by step again. Let's do 68 \u00d745.\n\nStarting with 68 \u00d7 45. Let me write it out vertically:\n\n\u2003\u2003\u200368\n\n\u00d7\u00a045\n\n----------\n\nFirst, multiply 68 by 5: 5\u00d78 is 40, carry over the 4. 5\u00d76 is 30, plus 4 is 34. So that gives 340.\n\nThen multiply 68 by 40. Since the 4 is in the tens place, so 4\u00d78 is 32, write down 2 and carry over 3. 4\u00d76 is 24, plus 3 is 27. So that gives 272, but since it's the tens place, we add a zero at the end, making it 2720.\n\nAdding 340 and 2720: 340 + 2720. Let's add the thousands: 2000 + 700 = 2700, then 20 + 340 = 360, so total would be 2700 + 360 = 3060. Wait, no, perhaps better to add straight: 2720 + 340. 2720 + 300 is 3020, plus 40 is 3060. Yep.\n\nAlright, I think that's thorough. I can't see any mistakes in my calculations. All different methods lead to the same result, so I think it's correct.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 68 and 45 is \\boxed{3060}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 68 and 45, we can use the distributive property by breaking down the numbers into smaller parts:\n\n\\[\n(60 + 8) \\times (40 + 5) = 60 \\times 40 + 60 \\times 5 + 8 \\times 40 + 8 \\times 5\n\\]\n\nCalculating each term separately:\n- \\(60 \\times 40 = 2400\\)\n- \\(60 \\times 5 = 300\\)\n- \\(8 \\times 40 = 320\\)\n- \\(8 \\times 5 = 40\\)\n\nAdding these results together:\n\\[\n2400 + 300 + 320 + 40 = 2700 + 320 + 40 = 3020 + 40 = 3060\n\\]\n\nVerification using the standard multiplication algorithm:\n- \\(68 \\times 5 = 340\\)\n- \\(68 \\times 40 = 2720\\)\n- Adding these results: \\(340 + 2720 = 3060\\)\n\nAnother method using rounding and compensation:\n- \\(68 \\times 45 = (70 - 2) \\times 45 = 70 \\times 45 - 2 \\times 45 = 3150 - 90 = 3060\\)\n\nAll methods confirm the result is consistent. Therefore, the product of 68 and 45 is \\(\\boxed{3060}\\).",
