s (5 \\times 10)\\).\n   - Rearrange using properties of multiplication: \\(6 \\times 5 \\times 10 \\times 10\\).\n   - Calculate \\(6 \\times 5 = 30\\) and \\(10 \\times 10 = 100\\).\n   - Combine the results: \\(30 \\times 100 = 3000\\).\n\n2. **Straight Multiplication**:\n   - Ignore the zeros first: \\(6 \\times 5 = 30\\).\n   - Add the two zeros back: \\(30 \\times 100 = 3000\\).\n\n3. **Standard Algorithm**:\n   - Multiply 60 by 50:\n     - \\(60 \\times 0 = 0\\) (units place of 50).\n     - \\(60 \\times 50 = 60 \\times 5 \\times 10 = 300 \\times 10 = 3000\\).\n   - Sum the results: \\(0 + 3000 = 3000\\).\n\n4. **Alternative Verification**:\n   - Recognize that \\(60 \\times 50\\) is half of \\(60 \\times 100\\).\n   - Since \\(60 \\times 100 = 6000\\), half of that is \\(3000\\).\n\nAll methods confirm the product is \\(\\boxed{3000}\\).",
