 should be 1880.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 47 and 40 is \\boxed{1880}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 47 and 40, we can use the following steps:\n\n1. Recognize that multiplying by 40 is the same as multiplying by 4 and then by 10.\n2. First, calculate \\( 47 \\times 4 \\):\n   \\[\n   47 \\times 4 = 188\n   \\]\n3. Then, multiply the result by 10:\n   \\[\n   188 \\times 10 = 1880\n   \\]\n\nWe can verify this using different methods:\n- **Distributive Property**: Break down 47 into 40 and 7:\n  \\[\n  47 \\times 40 = (40 + 7) \\times 40 = 40 \\times 40 + 7 \\times 40 = 1600 + 280 = 1880\n  \\]\n- **Approximation Check**: Using 50 (close to 47) and adjusting:\n  \\[\n  50 \\times 40 = 2000 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 2000 - (3 \\times 40) = 2000 - 120 = 1880\n  \\]\n\nAll methods confirm the result is consistent.\n\n### Final Answer\nThe product of 47 and 40 is \\boxed{1880}.",
