      "text": "14 multiplied by 50 equals...?\n\nAlternatively, maybe breaking it down into smaller parts would be easier. Let's see, 14 times 50 can be thought of as 14 times 5 times 10. Let me compute 14 times 5 first. 14 times 5 is 70. Then multiply that by 10, so 70 times 10 is 700. Wait, that seems straightforward. So the result is 700?\n\nAlternatively, another way: 50 is half of 100, so 14 times 100 is 1400, then half of that would be 700. Yeah, that also gives the same answer. Hmm, so both methods give me 700. Let me check with another method just to be sure.\n\nMaybe using the distributive property. 14 can be split into 10 + 4. So, 10 times 50 plus 4 times 50. 10*50 is 500, and 4*50 is 200. Adding those together, 500 + 200 is 700. Yep, that matches. Okay, so all three methods give me 700. I think that's correct. Let me just do the vertical multiplication again to confirm.\n\n14 multiplied by 50. Since 50 has a 5 in the tens place and 0 in the ones. So multiplying 14 by 0 gives 0, then multiplying 14 by 5 (but shifted one position to the left because it's the tens place). So 14 times 5 is 70, shifted left one digit becomes 700. Then adding the 0 from the first step (which is actually 0 shifted by zero digits, so just 0). So total is 700 + 0 = 700. Perfect, that's the same answer again.\n\nI don't see any discrepancies here. All the different methods lead to the same result. So I'm confident that the product of 14 and 50 is 700.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 14 and 50 is calculated by multiplying the two numbers together:\n\n\\[\n14 \\times 50 = 700\n\\]\n\n**Step-by-Step Explanation:**\n1. **Breakdown Method:**  \n   \\(14 \\times 50 = 14 \\times (5 \\times 10) = (14 \\times 5) \\times 10 = 70 \\times 10 = 700\\).\n\n2. **Place Value Method:**  \n   Multiply 14 by 5 (the tens digit of 50) and shift the result one place left:  \n   \\(14 \\times 5 = 70\\) \u2192 \\(70 \\times 10 = 700\\).\n\n3. **Distributive Property:**  \n   Split 14 into \\(10 + 4\\):  \n   \\((10 + 4) \\times 50 = 10 \\times 50 + 4 \\times 50 = 500 + 200 = 700\\).\n\nAll methods confirm the final answer is **700**.  \n\n\\boxed{700}",
