es 50) + (74 \\times 1)\n   \\]\n   \n2. **Compute each part:**\n   - \\( 74 \\times 50 = 3,\\!700 \\)  \n     (Since \\( 74 \\times 5 = 370 \\), then \\( 370 \\times 10 = 3,\\!700 \\))\n   - \\( 74 \\times 1 = 74 \\)\n\n3. **Add the results:**\n   \\[\n   3,\\!700 + 74 = 3,\\!774\n   \\]\n\n**Verification using alternative methods:**\n- **Standard algorithm:**\n  \\[\n  \\begin{array}{r}\n    \\quad 74 \\\\\n  \\times 51 \\\\\n  \\hline\n    \\quad 74 \\quad (\\text{74 \u00d7 1}) \\\\\n  + 3,\\!700 \\quad (\\text{74 \u00d7 50, shifted one position left}) \\\\\n  \\hline\n    3,\\!774 \\\\\n  \\end{array}\n  \\]\n- **Rounding and adjusting:**\n  \\[\n  (75 \\times 50) + \\text{adjustments} = 3,\\!750 + ( -1 \\times 50 + 1 \\times 75 - 1 \\times 1 ) = 3,\\!774\n  \\]\n\n**Final Answer:**  \n\\boxed{3774}",
