But let me try the standard multiplication again step by step to ensure I didn't make an error there.\n\nFirst, writing 37 \u00d7 67.\n\nMultiplying 37 by 7: 7\u00d77=49, write 9, carryover 4. Then 3\u00d77=21 plus 4 is 25, so 25. So that's 259. Correct.\n\nThen multiplying by 60: so 37\u00d76. 7\u00d76=42, write 2, carryover 4. 3\u00d76=18 plus 4 is 22, so 222. Then since it's the tens place, we shift one position, so 2220. Then adding 2220 +259:.\n\n2220\n+\u00a0259\n------\nLet's add units digit: 0 +9 =9.\n\nTens digit: 2 +5 =7.\n\nHundreds digit: 2 +2 =4.\n\nThousands digit: 2 +0 =2.\n\nSo yes, 2479. Okay, that's consistent.\n\nAlternatively, just to check with another multiplication. Let's see, 37\u00d770 would be 37\u00d77\u00d710. 37\u00d77 is 259, so 2590. Then subtract 37\u00d73 which is 111. So 2590 -111 =2479. Yep, same answer.\n\nAlright, so after verifying through multiple methods: standard algorithm, distributive property, breaking into (40-3)(60+7), using the (a+b)(c+d) expansion, and also using the approximation method with adjustment, all give me 2479. So I think that must be the correct product of 37 and 67.\n\nI don't see any mistakes in my calculations, so I feel confident that the answer is 2479.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 37 and 67 is \\boxed{2479}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 37 and 67, we can use multiple methods to verify the result:\n\n1. **Standard Multiplication Algorithm:**\n   - Multiply 37 by 7 (units place of 67):\n     \\[\n     37 \\times 7 = 259\n     \\]\n   - Multiply 37 by 60 (tens place of 67, which is 6 shifted one position to the left):\n     \\[\n     37 \\times 60 = 2220\n     \\]\n   - Add the results:\n     \\[\n     259 + 2220 = 2479\n     \\]\n\n2. **Distributive Property:**\n   - Expand \\((30 + 7)(60 + 7)\\):\n     \\[\n     30 \\times 60 + 30 \\times 7 + 7 \\times 60 + 7 \\times 7\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     1800 + 210 + 420 + 49 = 2479\n     \\]\n\n3. **Breaking Down Numbers:**\n   - Use \\(37 = 40 - 3\\) and apply the distributive property:\n     \\[\n     67 \\times (40 - 3) = 67 \\times 40 - 67 \\times 3\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     2680 - 201 = 2479\n     \\]\n\n4. **Approximation and Adjustment:**\n   - Calculate \\(35 \\times 70\\) and adjust:\n     \\[\n     (35 + 2)(70 - 3) = 35 \\times 70 - 35 \\times 3 + 2 \\times 70 - 2 \\times 3\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     2450 - 105 + 140 - 6 = 2479\n     \\]\n\nAll methods consistently yield the result 2479. Therefore, the product of 37 and 67 is \\(\\boxed{2479}\\).",
