the carried 2 is 9. So that gives 98, but shifted one place to the left, making it 980. \n\nAdding 14 and 980 gives 994. Yep, same as before. \n\nI think I can be confident that 14 multiplied by 71 is indeed 994. I don't see any mistakes in my calculations, and all the different methods cross-check to the same result. So I think that's the answer.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 14 and 71 is calculated as follows:\n\n1. **Break down the multiplication using the distributive property**:\n   \\[\n   14 \\times 71 = 14 \\times (70 + 1) = (14 \\times 70) + (14 \\times 1)\n   \\]\n   \n2. **Compute each part**:\n   - \\(14 \\times 70 = 980\\)\n   - \\(14 \\times 1 = 14\\)\n   \n3. **Add the results**:\n   \\[\n   980 + 14 = 994\n   \\]\n\n**Final Answer**: \\(\\boxed{994}\\)",
