      "text": "6580 + 470 = 7050? Wait, let me check that addition again. 6580 plus 400 is 6980, plus 70 more is 7050. Okay, that seems right.\n\nAlternatively, maybe there's another way to do this mentally or with a different method. Perhaps using distributive property?\n\n94 x 75 can be thought of as (90 + 4)(70 + 5). Let's expand that:\n\n90*70 + 90*5 + 4*70 + 4*5.\n\nCalculating each term:\n\n90*70 = 6300,\n\n90*5 = 450,\n\n4*70 = 280,\n\n4*5 = 20.\n\nAdding them all together: 6300 + 450 is 6750, plus 280 is 7030, plus 20 is 7050. Same result. That's good, so it checks out.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using some other trick. I remember that sometimes multiplying numbers close to a base can help. Let me see if that applies here. 94 is close to 100, but 75 isn't so close. Alternatively, 75 is three-quarters of 100. Hmm, maybe 94 multiplied by 75 is the same as 94 multiplied by (3/4)*100, so that would be 94*(3/4)*100. Wait, that might complicate things, but let's try:\n\n94*(3/4) = (94*3)/4. 94*3 is 282, divided by 4 is 70.5. Then multiply by 100 gives 7050. Oh, that works too! So that's another way to get the same answer. Nice, that's clever.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use the fact that 75 is 25 times 3, so 94*25*3. But 25 times 4 is 100, so maybe 94*25 is (94*100)/4 = 9400/4 = 2350. Then multiply by 3: 2350*3. Let's see, 2000*3=6000, 350*3=1050, so total is 7050. Again the same answer. So multiple methods confirm the same result.\n\nAlternatively, maybe breaking down 94 into 90 + 4 and 75 into 70 +5 as I did before. Either way, all methods seem to point to 7050. I think that's the right answer. Let me just do a quick check with a calculator in my mind. 94 times 70 is 6580 and 94 times 5 is 470. Adding them gives 6580 + 470. Let me add 6580 + 400 first, which is 6980, then +70 is 7050. Yep, that's correct. So I think that's the answer. I don't see any mistakes in my calculations. All different methods give the same result, so I'm confident it's 7050.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 94 and 75 is \\boxed{7050}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 94 and 75, we can use the standard multiplication method and verify with alternative strategies:\n\n1. **Standard Multiplication Method:**\n   - Multiply 94 by 5:\n     \\[\n     94 \\times 5 = 470\n     \\]\n   - Multiply 94 by 70 (since 7 is in the tens place):\n     \\[\n     94 \\times 70 = 94 \\times 7 \\times 10 = 658 \\times 10 = 6580\n     \\]\n   - Add the two results together:\n     \\[\n     470 + 6580 = 7050\n     \\]\n\n2. **Distributive Property:**\n   - Expand \\((90 + 4)(70 + 5)\\):\n     \\[\n     90 \\times 70 + 90 \\times 5 + 4 \\times 70 + 4 \\times 5\n     \\]\n   - Calculate each term:\n     \\[\n     90 \\times 70 = 6300, \\quad 90 \\times 5 = 450, \\quad 4 \\times 70 = 280, \\quad 4 \\times 5 = 20\n     \\]\n   - Sum the terms:\n     \\[\n     6300 + 450 + 280 + 20 = 7050\n     \\]\n\n3. **Alternative Trick Using Base 100:**\n   - Recognize that \\(75 = \\frac{3}{4} \\times 100\\):\n     \\[\n     94 \\times 75 = 94 \\times \\left(\\frac{3}{4} \\times 100\\right) = \\left(\\frac{94 \\times 3}{4}\\right) \\times 100 = \\left(\\frac{282}{4}\\right) \\times 100 = 70.5 \\times 100 = 7050\n     \\]\n\n4. **Breaking Down 75 into 25 and 3:**\n   - Calculate \\(94 \\times 25 \\times 3\\):\n     \\[\n     94 \\times 25 = \\frac{94 \\times 100}{4} = \\frac{9400}{4} = 2350\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     2350 \\times 3 = 7050\n     \\]\n\nAll methods confirm that the product of 94 and 75 is \\(\\boxed{7050}\\).",
