messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 99 and 81?', "<think>:.\nOkay, so I need to find the product of 99 and 81. Hmm, let me think. Multiplying 99 by 81.. I guess the straightforward way is just to do the multiplication, but maybe there's a trick to make it easier? Let me recall some math tricks. .\n\nWait, 99 is close to 100, right? So maybe I can use that to simplify the calculation. If I think of 99 as 100 minus 1, then 99 times 81 would be the same as (100 - 1) multiplied by 81. That might be easier because multiplying by 100 is simple. Let me write that down:.\n\n99 × 81 = (100 - 1) × 81.\n\nNow, using the distributive property, that would be 100×81 minus 1×81. Let me compute each part separately. .\n\nFirst, 100 multiplied by 81. Well, multiplying by 100 just adds two zeros to the end of 81, so that's 8100. Then, 1 multiplied by 81 is just 81. .\n\nSo subtracting those, it would be 8100 - 81. Let me do that subtraction. 8100 minus 81. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
