    {
      "index": 0,
      "text": "1500 - 75 = 1425. Let me check that again to be sure.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using the distributive property another way. 19 times 75 can be written as (20 - 1) * 75. Then distributing gives 20*75 - 1*75, which is exactly what I did before. Yep, that makes sense. So 20*75 is 1500, subtract 75 gives 1425. \n\nAnother way to verify could be multiplying directly. Let's do the standard multiplication method. 19 multiplied by 75. \n\nFirst, write 19\n           x75\n       --------\nMultiply 19 by 5: 19*5 = 95\nThen multiply 19 by 70 (since the 7 is in the tens place, so 7*10). So 19*70. 19*7 is 133, so 133*10 = 1330\nAdd the two results: 95 + 1330 = 1425. \n\nSame result. That's reassuring. Maybe another method, like breaking 75 into 70 +5. Then 19*(70+5) = 19*70 +19*5. \n\nCalculating 19*70: 19*7=133, so times 10 is 1330. 19*5 is 95. Adding 1330 +95 = 1425. Yep, same answer again.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using some other multiplication tricks. For example, since 75 is 3/4 of 100, perhaps? Wait, 75 is 3/4 of 100? Wait no, 3/4 of 100 is 75. Hmm, so 19 multiplied by 75 is 19 multiplied by 3/4 of 100. So that would be (19*3)/4 *100. Let me see. 19*3 is 57. Then 57 divided by 4 is 14.25, then times 100 is 1425. Wait, that works too. Interesting. \n\nSo that method also gives 1425. That's four different methods all leading to the same answer. That gives me confidence that 1425 is the correct product of 19 and 75. \n\nAlternatively, maybe using prime factors? Let's see. Prime factors of 19 is just 19 since it's a prime number. 75 is 25*3, which is 5^2 *3. So multiplying them together would be 19 *5^2 *3. So that's 19*3*25. Let's compute 19*3 first: 57, then 57*25. Hmm, 57*25. Well, 50*25 is 1250, and 7*25 is 175, so 1250 +175 = 1425. Yep, same answer again. \n\nI think that's enough verification. All methods point to 1425. I don't see any mistakes in my calculations. So the product of 19 and 75 is 1425.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 19 and 75 can be calculated using multiple methods:\n\n**Method 1: Using 20 as a reference**\n\\[\n19 \\times 75 = (20 - 1) \\times 75 = 20 \\times 75 - 1 \\times 75 = 1500 - 75 = 1425\n\\]\n\n**Method 2: Direct multiplication**\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n\\quad \\ 19 \\\\\n\\times 75 \\\\\n\\hline\n\\quad 95 \\ \\ (\\text{19 \u00d7 5}) \\\\\n+1330 \\ \\ (\\text{19 \u00d7 70, shifted one position left}) \\\\\n\\hline\n1425 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\n**Method 3: Breaking into components**\n\\[\n19 \\times 75 = 19 \\times (70 + 5) = (19 \\times 70) + (19 \\times 5) = 1330 + 95 = 1425\n\\]\n\n**Method 4: Prime factorization**\n\\[\n19 \\times 75 = 19 \\times (3 \\times 5^2) = (19 \\times 3) \\times 25 = 57 \\times 25 = 1425\n\\]\n\n**Final Answer:**  \nThe product of 19 and 75 is \\boxed{1425}.",
