100 \\), so half of that is \\( 4550 \\).\n   - \\( 91 \\times 4 = 364 \\)  \n     *Explanation*: \\( 90 \\times 4 = 360 \\) and \\( 1 \\times 4 = 4 \\), so \\( 360 + 4 = 364 \\).\n3. **Add the results**:\n   \\[\n   4550 + 364 = 4914\n   \\]\n\n**Verification**:\n- Using the standard algorithm:\n  \\[\n  \\begin{array}{r}\n      91 \\\\\n    \\times 54 \\\\\n    \\hline\n      364 \\ (\\text{91} \\times 4) \\\\\n    +4550 \\ (\\text{91} \\times 50) \\\\\n    \\hline\n      4914 \\\\\n  \\end{array}\n  \\]\n- Alternative method (\\(54 \\times (90 + 1)\\)):\n  \\[\n  54 \\times 90 = 4860 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 54 \\times 1 = 54 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad 4860 + 54 = 4914\n  \\]\n\n**Final Answer**:  \n\\boxed{4914}",
