0 + 16 = 376\n     \\]\n\n3. **Adding the results**:\n   \\[\n   3760 + 376 = 4136\n   \\]\n\n4. **Verification using alternative methods**:\n   - **Standard multiplication**:\n     \\[\n     \\begin{array}{r}\n       \\quad 94 \\\\\n     \\times 44 \\\\\n     \\hline\n       \\quad 376 \\quad (\\text{(94 \u00d7 4)}) \\\\\n     + 3760 \\quad (\\text{(94 \u00d7 40)}) \\\\\n     \\hline\n       4136 \\\\\n     \\end{array}\n     \\]\n\n   - **Difference of squares or other breakdowns**:\n     \\[\n     (90 + 4)(40 + 4) = 90 \\times 40 + 90 \\times 4 + 4 \\times 40 + 4 \\times 4\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     = 3600 + 360 + 160 + 16 = 4136\n     \\]\n\n   - **Estimation and adjustment**:\n     \\[\n     100 \\times 44 = 4400 \\quad \\text{and subtract} \\quad 6 \\times 44 = 264\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     4400 - 264 = 4136\n     \\]\n\nAll methods confirm that the product of 94 and 44 is \\(\\boxed{4136}\\).",
