    {
      "index": 0,
      "text": "1660 - 83 = ?\n\nWait, let me check that again. 1660 minus 80 would be 1580, and then minus 3 more is 1577. Wait, that doesn't seem right. Let me recalculate. Maybe I made a mistake in the subtraction part.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I should do it another way to verify. Let me try the standard multiplication method for 19 times 83.\n\nFirst, write 19 on top and 83 below, aligned to the right:\n\n\u2003\u00a019\n\u00d7\u00a083\n------\n\nMultiply 19 by 3 first. 9*3 is 27, write down 7 and carry over 2. Then 1*3 is 3 plus the carried 2 is 5. So the first partial product is 57.\n\nThen multiply 19 by 80 (since the 8 is in the tens place). So 19*80. Well, 19*8 is 152, and since it's 80, add a zero at the end to make it 1520.\n\nNow add the two partial products: 57 + 1520. Let's see, 1520 + 50 is 1570, plus 7 is 1577. Hmm, that's the same result as before. So maybe I was right the first time?\n\nBut wait, I thought maybe I made a mistake in subtraction. Let me check the first method again. 20*83 = 1660. Then subtract 83 from that. 1660 - 83: 1660 minus 60 is 1600, then minus 23 more is 1577. Yeah, that's the same answer. So both methods give me 1577. So maybe that's correct?\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can do another check using addition. 19 added 83 times. But that's obviously too time-consuming, but maybe breaking it down differently?\n\nAlternatively, let me try using another distributive approach. Maybe 83 can be broken into 80 + 3. So 19*(80 +3) = 19*80 +19*3. Let's see:\n\n19*80: 19*8=152, so 152*10=1520. Then 19*3 is 57. Adding them gives 1520 +57=1577. Same result again. Hmm, so that's consistent. So all three methods give me 1577. I think that must be the correct answer then. But just to be thorough, maybe use a calculator? Wait, since I can't use a calculator, but I can cross-verify once more.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use the difference of squares? Wait, not sure if that applies here. Let's see, 19*83. Hmm, 19 is 20-1, 83 is 80+3. Not sure if that helps, but maybe another way. Wait, 19*83 = (20 -1)(80 +3). Expanding this would give 20*80 +20*3 -1*80 -1*3 = 1600 +60 -80 -3 = 1600 +60 is 1660, minus 80 is 1580, minus 3 is 1577. Yep, same answer again. So all methods converge to 1577. I think that's solid. So the product of 19 and 83 is 1577.\n\nWait, hold on, let me just do the multiplication the long way again step by step:\n\nMultiplying 19 by 83:\n\nFirst, 9 (units place of 19) times 3 (units place of 83) is 27. Write down 7, carryover 2.\n\nThen 9 times 8 (tens place of 83) is 72, plus the carried over 2 is 74. So that partial product is 747.\n\nWait, hold on, no, maybe I confused the placement. Wait, actually, when multiplying 19 by 83, the standard algorithm is:\n\nFirst step: multiply 19 by 3 (the units digit of 83):\n\n19\n\u00d7\u00a03\n=\n57 (since 9\u00d73=27, carryover 2, then 1\u00d73 +2=5, so 57).\n\nSecond step: multiply 19 by 80 (the 8 in the tens place, so shifted one position to the left):\n\n19 \u00d7 8 = 152, then add a zero to make it 1520.\n\nThen add 57 + 1520 = 1577. That's correct. \n\nEarlier, when I thought of multiplying 9 by 8 first, that was a confusion in the steps. The correct way is to first do units digit, then the tens digit with a shift. So the partial products are 57 and 1520, adding to 1577. So yes, that's consistent.\n\nAnother way: 83\u00d719. Let's reverse the multiplication for cross-checking.\n\n83 \u00d7 19:\n\nFirst, 83 \u00d79: 80\u00d79=720, 3\u00d79=27 \u2192 720+27=747.\n\nSecond, 83 \u00d710 (since the 1 in 19 is in the tens place): 83\u00d710=830.\n\nAdd 747 +830: 747+800=1547, plus 30 is 1577. Yep, same result. \n\nTherefore, I'm confident that 19 multiplied by 83 is indeed 1577. \n\nWait, but just to ensure that I didn't make any arithmetic errors in my head, perhaps do the addition steps again:\n\nFor 1520 +57: 1520 +50 is 1570, plus 7 is 1577. Correct.\n\nAnother addition check: 747 + 830. 700 +800=1500, 40+30=70, 7+0=7. 1500+70=1570, +7=1577. Correct.\n\nAlright, I think that's solid. All methods lead to the same answer, so I can be sure that the product is 1577. I don't see any mistakes in my calculations now.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 19 and 83 is calculated as follows:\n\n**Method 1: Using Distributive Property**  \nBreak down 19 into (20 - 1):  \n\\[\n(20 - 1) \\times 83 = 20 \\times 83 - 1 \\times 83\n\\]  \nCalculate each term:  \n\\[\n20 \\times 83 = 1,\\!660 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 1 \\times 83 = 83\n\\]  \nSubtract:  \n\\[\n1,\\!660 - 83 = 1,\\!577\n\\]\n\n**Method 2: Standard Multiplication**  \nMultiply 19 by 3 and then by 80 (shifted one position left):  \n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n\\quad 19 \\\\\n\\times 83 \\\\\n\\hline\n\\quad 57 \\quad (\\text{19 \u00d7 3}) \\\\\n+1,\\!520 \\quad (\\text{19 \u00d7 80}) \\\\\n\\hline\n1,\\!577 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\n**Verification via Alternative Breakdown**  \nExpress 83 as (80 + 3):  \n\\[\n19 \\times (80 + 3) = 19 \\times 80 + 19 \\times 3 = 1,\\!520 + 57 = 1,\\!577\n\\]\n\n**Final Answer:**  \n\\boxed{1577}",
