      "index": 0,
      "text": "2314? Wait, that doesn't seem right because 20 added to 90 would be 110, but that's not the case here. Wait, no, I think I messed up the addition step. Let me check again. \n\nWait, 234 plus 2080. Let's see: 2000 + 200 is 2200, 80 + 34 is 114, so total 2314. Hmm, but let me verify with another method to make sure I didn't make a mistake.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use the distributive property. 26 times 89 can be thought of as 26*(90 - 1) which is 26*90 minus 26*1. Calculating 26*90 first. 26*9 is 234, so 26*90 is 2340. Then subtract 26: 2340 - 26 = 2314. Okay, so that matches the previous result. So that's good. \n\nBut wait, just to be thorough, maybe do another method. Let me try breaking down 26 into 20 + 6. Then, 89*(20 + 6) = 89*20 + 89*6. Calculating 89*20: 89*2 is 178, so times 10 is 1780. Then 89*6: 80*6=480 and 9*6=54, so 480+54=534. Adding those together: 1780 + 534. Let's see, 1700 + 500 is 2200, 80 + 34 is 114, so total 2314 again. \n\nHmm, same answer each time. Maybe I was right the first time. But let me just do straight multiplication again to confirm. \n\nMultiplying 26 by 89:\n\nFirst, 26 x 9: 6x9=54, write down 4, carryover 5. 2x9=18 +5=23. So that's 234. \n\nThen 26 x 80: since the 8 is in the tens place, it's 80. So 26x80. \n\nCalculating 26x8 first: 6x8=48, write 8 carryover 4. 2x8=16 +4=20. So that's 208. Then add a zero at the end to make it 2080. \n\nAdding 234 and 2080: 2080 + 200 is 2280, plus 34 is 2314. \n\nOkay, so three different methods all give me 2314. I think that's correct. \n\nBut just to make sure, maybe approximate the answer. 26 is close to 25, and 89 is close to 90. 25 times 90 is 2250. Since 26 is 1 more than 25, that adds another 90, making 2340, but since 89 is 1 less than 90, so the exact calculation would be 2340 -26, which is 2314. Yep, that still works. \n\nAlternatively, using calculator-like step-by-step:\n\n26 \u00d7 89:\n\nBreak it down as (20 + 6) \u00d7 (80 + 9). \n\nMultiply each term:\n\n20\u