ybe I was just second-guessing myself unnecessarily, but all the methods confirm it. So yeah, the product of 47 and 11 is 517.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 47 and 11 can be calculated using the following steps:\n\n1. **Using the 11-multiplication shortcut for two-digit numbers:**\n   - Split the digits of 47 into 4 and 7.\n   - Add the digits: \\(4 + 7 = 11\\).\n   - Place the sum (11) between the original digits. Since the sum is two digits, carry over the 1 to the hundreds place:\n     - Hundreds place: \\(4 + 1 = 5\\),\n     - Tens place: \\(1\\),\n     - Ones place: \\(7\\).\n   - Result: \\(517\\).\n\n2. **Verification by standard multiplication:**\n   - \\(47 \\times 11 = 47 \\times (10 + 1) = 47 \\times 10 + 47 \\times 1\\).\n   - \\(470 + 47 = 517\\).\n\n3. **Additional check by division:**\n   - \\(517 \\div 11 = 47\\), confirming the result.\n\n**Answer:** The product of 47 and 11 is \\boxed{517}.",
