ame answer again. \n\nAlright, so all methods confirm that 16 multiplied by 95 is 1520. I feel confident that's the right product.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 16 and 95 is calculated as follows:\n\n**Step 1:** Use the distributive property by breaking down 95 into \\(100 - 5\\):  \n\\[\n16 \\times 95 = 16 \\times (100 - 5)\n\\]\n\n**Step 2:** Multiply 16 by each term separately:  \n\\[\n16 \\times 100 = 1600 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 16 \\times 5 = 80\n\\]\n\n**Step 3:** Subtract the results:  \n\\[\n1600 - 80 = 1520\n\\]\n\n**Verification:**  \nUsing vertical multiplication:  \n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n   \\quad 95 \\\\\n\\times 16 \\\\\n\\hline\n   570 \\quad (\\text{95 \u00d7 6}) \\\\\n+ 950 \\quad (\\text{95 \u00d7 10}) \\\\\n\\hline\n  1520 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nBoth methods confirm the **final answer**:  \n\\[\n\\boxed{1520}\n\\]",
