on:\n\n67 \u00d721:\n\nMultiply 67 by 1 (units place): 67.\n\nMultiply 67 by 2 (tens place, so actually 20), so shift one position:\n\n134 shifted one digit to the left is 1340.\n\nAdd them together:\n\n67\n\n+1340\n\n=1407.\n\nYep, same answer. I think that's correct. I can't see any mistake here. So the answer should be 1407.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 67 and 21 is \\boxed{1407}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 67 and 21, we can use the distributive property by breaking down 21 into 20 and 1:\n\n\\[\n67 \\times 21 = 67 \\times (20 + 1) = (67 \\times 20) + (67 \\times 1)\n\\]\n\nFirst, calculate \\(67 \\times 20\\):\n\n\\[\n67 \\times 20 = 67 \\times 2 \\times 10 = 134 \\times 10 = 1340\n\\]\n\nNext, calculate \\(67 \\times 1\\):\n\n\\[\n67 \\times 1 = 67\n\\]\n\nAdd the two results together:\n\n\\[\n1340 + 67 = 1407\n\\]\n\nWe verified this result using different methods: the standard multiplication algorithm, lattice multiplication, and breaking down the numbers. All methods confirmed the same result.\n\nThe product of 67 and 21 is \\(\\boxed{1407}\\).",
