times 41\\) as \\((50 - 2)(40 + 1)\\).\n   - Expand using the distributive property:\n     \\[\n     (50 - 2)(40 + 1) = 50 \\times 40 + 50 \\times 1 - 2 \\times 40 - 2 \\times 1\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     = 2000 + 50 - 80 - 2 = 2000 + 50 = 2050 - 80 = 1970 - 2 = 1968\n     \\]\n\n3. **Another Distributive Approach**:\n   - Express \\(48 \\times 41\\) as \\((40 + 8) \\times 41\\).\n   - Expand and calculate:\n     \\[\n     40 \\times 41 + 8 \\times 41 = 1640 + 328 = 1968\n     \\]\n\n4. **Difference of Squares**:\n   - Recognize that \\(48\\) and \\(41\\) are equidistant from \\(44.5\\):\n     \\[\n     (44.5 + 3.5)(44.5 - 3.5) = (44.5)^2 - (3.5)^2\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     44.5^2 = 1980.25 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 3.5^2 = 12.25\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     1980.25 - 12.25 = 1968\n     \\]\n\n5. **Verification by Division**:\n   - Divide \\(1968\\) by \\(48\\): \\(1968 \\div 48 = 41\\).\n   - Divide \\(1968\\) by \\(41\\): \\(1968 \\div 41 = 48\\).\n\nAll methods confirm that the product of 48 and 41 is \\(\\boxed{1968}\\).",
