  "id": "cmpl-c151313a403f4ea482f716c4ed11e4c1",
  "object": "text_completion",
  "created": 1754638271,
  "model": "QwQ-32B",
  "choices": [
    {
      "index": 0,
      "text": "67 times 100 is 6700. Wait, but let me make sure I didn't make any mistakes here. Maybe I should write it out the long way.\n\n67 multiplied by 100. Let's break it down. 67 times 100 is the same as 67 times (10 times 10). So first, 67 times 10 is 670. Then, multiply that by 10 again. 670 times 10 is 6700. Yep, that checks out. Alternatively, using the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n   67\nx 100\n-------\n   00  (67 x 0)\n  00   (67 x 0, shifted one position to the left)\n67     (67 x 1, shifted two positions to the left)\n-------\n6700\n\nAdding those up gives 6700. Okay, that seems right. I don't think I made any errors here. So the product is definitely 6700.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 67 and 100 is calculated by multiplying the two numbers together. \n\n**Step-by-Step Explanation:**\n1. **Understand the operation:** The \"product\" means multiplication. \n2. **Multiply 67 by 100:**\n   - Multiplying any number by 100 appends two zeros to the end of that number.\n   - \\( 67 \\times 100 = 67{,}00 \\).\n   \n**Final Answer:**  \nThe product of 67 and 100 is \\(\\boxed{6700}\\).",
      "logprobs": null,
      "finish_reason": "stop",
      "stop_reason": null,
      "prompt_logprobs": null
    }
  ],
  "usage": {
    "prompt_tokens": 227,
    "total_tokens": 598,
    "completion_tokens": 371,
    "prompt_tokens_details": null
  }
}
