ent that 3350 is the correct product of 50 and 67. I don't see any mistakes in my reasoning, so I think that's the right answer.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 50 and 67 is calculated as follows:\n\n\\[\n50 \\times 67 = (5 \\times 10) \\times 67 = 5 \\times (10 \\times 67) = 5 \\times 670 = 3350\n\\]\n\n**Verification Steps:**\n1. **Standard Multiplication:**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{array}{r}\n     \\quad 67 \\\\\n   \\times 50 \\\\\n   \\hline\n     3350 \\quad (\\text{since } 67 \\times 5 = 335, \\text{ then append a zero})\n   \\end{array}\n   \\]\n2. **Distributive Property:**\n   \\[\n   50 \\times 67 = 50 \\times (60 + 7) = (50 \\times 60) + (50 \\times 7) = 3000 + 350 = 3350\n   \\]\n3. **Alternative Breakdown:**\n   \\[\n   50 \\times 67 = 50 \\times (70 - 3) = (50 \\times 70) - (50 \\times 3) = 3500 - 150 = 3350\n   \\]\n\nAll methods confirm the result is consistent. \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{3350}",
