messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 37 and 97?', "<think>Okay, so I need to find the product of 37 and 97. Hmm, let me think. Multiplying two numbers.. I remember that when you multiply two numbers, you just have to multiply each digit and add the results appropriately. But maybe there's a smarter way to do this without doing the standard multiplication step by step. Let me see.\n\nFirst, the straightforward way is to do 37 times 97. Let me write that down:.\n\n37  .\n×\xa097  .\n________.\n\nStarting with the standard algorithm. Multiply 37 by 7 first. 7 times 7 is 49. Write down 9 and carry over 4. Then 7 times 3 is 21, plus the carried over 4 is 25. So that gives 259. .\n\nThen, moving to the tens place, we multiply 37 by 90 (since the 9 is in the tens place). Wait, actually, in the standard method, you would do 37 × 9 (but shifted one position to the left because it's the tens place). Let me make sure I do this correctly.\n\nSo, starting over:.\n\nFirst line (units place):.\n\n37 × 7 = 259.\n\nSecond line (tens place):.\n\n37 × 9 = 333. But since the 9 is in the tens place, we have to shift this result one position to the left, so it becomes 3330.\n\nThen add the two results together: 259 + 3330.\n\nLet me add those: 259 + 3330. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
