Then, 45 goes into 315 exactly 7 times (since 45\u00d77=315). So total is 80 +7 =87. Perfect, so division confirms it. So that's another check.\n\nAlternatively, maybe check 3915 divided by 87 equals 45? Let's see.\n\nDivide 3915 by 87. Let's see how many times 87 goes into 3915.\n\n87\u00d740 is 3480. Subtract that from 3915: 3915-3480 = 435.\n\nThen, 87\u00d75 is 435. So total is 40 +5 =45. Yep, so that works too. So division checks out both ways.\n\nTherefore, I can be confident that 45 multiplied by 87 is indeed 3915. I think that's solid.\n\nWait, just to make sure, let me recount the steps in the first method again. 45\u00d780 is 3600? Let me recalculate that. 45\u00d780: 45 times 8 is 360, so 360 times 10 is 3600. Yes. Then 45\u00d77 is 315. Adding them together, 3600 + 315. 3600 + 300 is 3900, plus 15 is 3915. Correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I added wrong? Let me add 3600 + 315 again. 3600 + 300 is 3900, plus 15 is 3915. Yep.\n\nAlternatively, if I had messed up one of the components. For instance, if I had miscalculated 45\u00d780 as something else. Let me recalculate 45\u00d780. 45\u00d780 is 45 multiplied by 8 multiplied by 10. 45\u00d78: 40\u00d78 is 320, 5\u00d78 is 40. 320 +40 =360. So 360\u00d710 is 3600. That's correct.\n\nAlternatively, 45\u00d77: 40\u00d77=280, 5\u00d77=35, so 280+35=315. That's correct.\n\nSo, all steps check out. So I think the answer is definitely 3915. I can't find any errors in my calculations, and multiple methods confirm the same result.\n\nAlternatively, maybe visualize it as an area problem. Imagine a rectangle with sides 45 and 87. The area would be 45\u00d787. Breaking it down into smaller rectangles: 40+5 and 80+7. The areas would be 40\u00d780, 40\u00d77, 5\u00d780, 5\u00d77. Which again gives the same components as before, adding to 3915.\n\nHmm, another way to think is using the distributive property in a different order. For example, 87\u00d745 can be thought of as (90 -3) \u00d745, which we did earlier, but let me