e the 4 is in the tens place): 87\u00d740=3480. Add 435 + 3480. 3480 +400 is 3880, plus 35 is 3915. Same result. Yep, that works.\n\nAlright, so every method I try gives me the same answer, and all the checks confirm it. I think that's solid. So I can confidently say the product of 45 and 87 is 3915.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 45 and 87 is \\boxed{3915}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 45 and 87, we can use the distributive property and verify the result through multiple methods.\n\nFirst, using the distributive property:\n\\[\n45 \\times 87 = 45 \\times (80 + 7) = (45 \\times 80) + (45 \\times 7)\n\\]\nCalculating each term separately:\n\\[\n45 \\times 80 = 3600\n\\]\n\\[\n45 \\times 7 = 315\n\\]\nAdding the results:\n\\[\n3600 + 315 = 3915\n\\]\n\nVerification using the standard algorithm:\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n   \\quad 45 \\\\\n\\times 87 \\\\\n\\hline\n   315 \\quad (\\text{45} \\times 7) \\\\\n+3600 \\quad (\\text{45} \\times 80) \\\\\n\\hline\n  3915 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nAnother verification using the distributive property in a different form:\n\\[\n45 \\times 87 = (40 + 5) \\times (80 + 7)\n\\]\nExpanding the terms:\n\\[\n40 \\times 80 + 40 \\times 7 + 5 \\times 80 + 5 \\times 7\n\\]\nCalculating each term:\n\\[\n3200 + 280 + 400 + 35 = 3915\n\\]\n\nVerification using division:\n\\[\n3915 \\div 45 = 87 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 3915 \\div 87 = 45\n\\]\n\nAll methods confirm that the product of 45 and 87 is \\(\\boxed{3915}\\).",
