      "text": "86 + 3010. Let me compute that. 86 + 3000 is 3086, then plus 10 more? Wait, no, wait. 3010 is 3000+10. So 86+3010 = (86 + 3000) +10 = 3086 +10 = 3096. Wait, no, that can't be right. Wait, hold on, maybe I messed up the addition step. Let me check again. 86 plus 3010. 3010 plus 80 is 3090, then plus 6 is 3096. Okay, so that would be 3096. But let me verify this another way to be sure. .\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can do 43 \u00d7 72 directly. Let me try another method, like breaking down the numbers. 43 is 40 +3, and 72 is 70 +2. So using the distributive property: (40 +3)(70 +2) = 40\u00d770 + 40\u00d72 + 3\u00d770 + 3\u00d72. Let me compute each term. 40\u00d770 is 2800. 40\u00d72 is 80. 3\u00d770 is 210. 3\u00d72 is 6. Adding all those together: 2800 +80 = 2880; 2880 +210 = 3090; 3090 +6= 3096. Okay, same result. So that's good. .\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use another approach. Let me see if I can multiply 43 by 70 first, then add 43\u00d72. Wait, that's the same as before. So that gives me 3010 +86=3096 again. Hmm. So seems consistent. .\n\nAlternatively, perhaps I can use a calculator, but since this is a problem-solving exercise, I should stick to manual calculation. Let me check once more step by step. \n\nStarting with the standard multiplication:\n\n       43\n     \u00d772\n     -----\nFirst, multiply 43 by 2: 43\u00d72=86. Write that down.\n\nThen, multiply 43 by 70 (since the 7 is in the tens place, so 7\u00d710). So 43\u00d77=301, then add a zero at the end to make it 3010.\n\nNow add the two results:\n\n   86\n+3010\n-----\n3096\n\nYes, that's correct. Therefore, the product of 43 and 72 is 3096. I think that's the right answer. Let me see if there's another way to verify. Maybe approximate to check. 40\u00d770 is 2800, and 40\u00d772 would be 2880. Since 43 is 3 more than 40, so 3\u00d772 is 216, so 2880+216=3096. That also works. Yeah, that's the same answer. So seems like 3096 is correct. \n\nWait, another way: 72\u00d743. Let me reverse the multiplication. 72\u00d740=2880, and 72\u00d73=216, so adding them gives 2880+216=3096. Same result again. \n\nAlright, I think that's solid. So the answer should be 3096.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 43 and 72 is calculated as follows:\n\nFirst, break down the multiplication using the distributive property:\n\\[\n43 \\times 72 = 43 \\times (70 + 2) = (43 \\times 70) + (43 \\times 2)\n\\]\n\nCalculate each part separately:\n- \\(43 \\times 70 = 3010\\)\n- \\(43 \\times 2 = 86\\)\n\nAdd the results together:\n\\[\n3010 + 86 = 3096\n\\]\n\n**Final Answer:**  \n\\boxed{3096}",
