 194. Let's see, 3880 + 100 is 3980, plus 94 is 4074. Again the same answer. Hmm, so that's three different methods all leading to 4074. I think that's solid.\n\nAlternatively, maybe another way: 97 is 100-3, so 42\u00d797 = 42\u00d7(100-3) = 42\u00d7100 - 42\u00d73 = 4200 - 126 = 4074. Yep, same as before. So I think that's right. \n\nWait, but just to make sure, maybe I can estimate. 42\u00d7100 is 4200, so 42\u00d797 should be a bit less, which 4074 is. The difference is 126, which is exactly 42\u00d73, so that makes sense. \n\nAlternatively, maybe check with another multiplication method, like the lattice method? Not sure if I remember that, but let me try. \n\nWait, for lattice multiplication, you set up a grid. For 42 \u00d7 97, you have a 2x2 grid. The digits of 42 are 4 and 2, and 97 are 9 and 7. So placing them on the top and right sides. Then multiply each digit pair and split the products into diagonals. Let me see:\n\nFirst, 4\u00d79=36, 4\u00d77=28, 2\u00d79=18, 2\u00d77=14. Then arranging them in the grid. Then adding along the diagonals. Hmm, maybe I need to visualize this better. \n\nBut perhaps this is getting too complicated. Since all the other methods have given me 4074, and cross-verified, maybe I can be confident that's correct. \n\nAlternatively, maybe adding 42 seventy times and then 42 ninety times? No, that's too tedious. \n\nAlternatively, use the fact that 42\u00d797 is (40\u00d797) + (2\u00d797) as I did before. \n\nWait, 40\u00d797: 97\u00d74 is 388, so 97\u00d740 is 3880, right. Then 2\u00d797 is 194. 3880 + 194: 3880 + 200 would be 4080, minus 6 gives 4074. Yep, same result. \n\nAlternatively, perhaps think of 97\u00d742 as (90+7)\u00d742 = 90\u00d742 +7\u00d742. Let's see:\n\n90\u00d742: 9\u00d742=378, so times 10 is 3780. 7\u00d742 is 294. Then 3780 +294 = 4074. Again same answer. \n\nAlright, so after trying multiple methods\u2014breaking down using distributive property with 100-3, breaking down the original numbers into tens and units, using the vertical multiplication\u2014the answer consistently comes out to 4074. I think that's solid. \n\nTherefore, the product of 42 and 97 is 4074.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 42 and 97 is \\boxed{4074}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 42 and 97, we can use the distributive property by breaking down 97 into 100 - 3:\n\n\\[\n42 \\times 97 = 42 \\times (100 - 3)\n\\]\n\nApplying the distributive property:\n\n\\[\n42 \\times 100 - 42 \\times 3\n\\]\n\nCalculating each term separately:\n\n\\[\n42 \\times 100 = 4200\n\\]\n\\[\n42 \\times 3 = 126\n\\]\n\nSubtracting the second result from the first:\n\n\\[\n4200 - 126 = 4074\n\\]\n\nTo verify, we can use another method by breaking down the numbers and using vertical multiplication:\n\n\\[\n42 \\times 97 = (40 + 2) \\times 97\n\\]\n\nCalculating each part:\n\n\\[\n40 \\times 97 = 3880\n\\]\n\\[\n2 \\times 97 = 194\n\\]\n\nAdding the results:\n\n\\[\n3880 + 194 = 4074\n\\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 42 and 97 is \\(\\boxed{4074}\\).",
