 since 7 is in the tens place, the multiplication by 7 would be shifted one place to the left, so that would be 301 indented one space, making it 3010. So adding 86 and 3010 gives 3096.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I should check using a calculator, but since I can't use a calculator, I can do another verification method. Let me see.\n\nAnother way to verify is using the difference of squares or some other algebraic identity, but that might be more complicated. Alternatively, check if the product is divisible by some numbers. Let me see.\n\n43 is a prime number, right? So 43 \u00d772, so the prime factors would be 43 \u00d7 8 \u00d79, since 72 is 8\u00d79. So 43 \u00d78 is 344, then 344 \u00d79. Let me compute that.\n\n344 \u00d79: 300\u00d79=2700, 44\u00d79=396. So 2700 +396 = 3096. So that's the same answer again.\n\nAlternatively, 344 \u00d79: 344\u00d710=3440 minus 344 gives 3440 -344 = 3096. Yep.\n\nTherefore, that gives me more confidence that the answer is indeed 3096.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can check with estimation. 40 \u00d770 is 2800, and 40\u00d772 would be 2880, and 43\u00d772 is a bit more. 3\u00d772 is 216, so 2880 +216= 3096. So that's the exact value. Since 43 is 3 more than 40, so adding 3\u00d772 gives the correct amount.\n\nHmm, all methods seem to confirm that 43 multiplied by 72 is 3096. I don't see any mistakes in my calculations here. So I think that is the correct product.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 43 and 72 is calculated as follows:\n\n1. **Break down the multiplication using the distributive property:**\n   \\[\n   43 \\times 72 = 43 \\times (70 + 2) = (43 \\times 70) + (43 \\times 2)\n   \\]\n\n2. **Compute each part:**\n   - \\( 43 \\times 70 = 3010 \\)\n   - \\( 43 \\times 2 = 86 \\)\n\n3. **Add the results:**\n   \\[\n   3010 + 86 = 3096\n   \\]\n\n**Final Answer:**  \nThe product of 43 and 72 is \\(\\boxed{3096}\\).",
