at's the correct way.\n\nAlternatively, if I think of 37*82 as (40 -3)*(80 +2). Maybe expanding that:\n\n40*80 +40*2 -3*80 -3*2\n\nWhich is 3200 +80 -240 -6.\n\nCalculating that: 3200 +80 is 3280; 3280 -240 is 3040; 3040 -6 is 3034. That also gives the same result. So that's another way to confirm.\n\nHmm, so all methods are pointing towards 3034. I think that's the correct answer. Let me just try one more verification. Maybe using a calculator, but since I can't use an actual calculator, perhaps do the multiplication vertically again step by step.\n\nMultiplying 37 by 82:\n\nFirst, write 37\n\nx82\n\n--------\n\nMultiply 37 by 2: 74\n\nMultiply 37 by 80 (since the 8 is in the tens place, so 8*10, so it's 37*8*10). 37*8: 30*8=240, 7*8=56, so 240+56=296. Then times 10 is 2960.\n\nAdd 74 +2960. Let's do this addition again:\n\n2960\n\n+\u00a0 74\n\n------\n\n2960 + 70 is 3030, plus 4 is 3034. Yep, same result.\n\nAlright, so after multiple checks using different methods, I feel confident that the product of 37 and 82 is 3034. I don't see any mistakes in my calculations, so I think that's the right answer.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 37 and 82 is calculated as follows:\n\n**Step 1:** Use the standard multiplication algorithm.  \n- Multiply 37 by 2 (ones place of 82):  \n  \\( 37 \\times 2 = 74 \\).  \n- Multiply 37 by 80 (tens place of 82, treated as \\( 8 \\times 10 \\)):  \n  \\( 37 \\times 8 = 296 \\), then append a zero: \\( 2960 \\).  \n\n**Step 2:** Add the partial products:  \n\\( 74 + 2960 = 3034 \\).  \n\n**Verification via distributive property:**  \nBreak down \\( 37 \\times 82 \\) into:  \n\\( (30 + 7)(80 + 2) = 30 \\times 80 + 30 \\times 2 + 7 \\times 80 + 7 \\times 2 \\).  \n- \\( 30 \\times 80 = 2400 \\),  \n- \\( 30 \\times 2 = 60 \\),  \n- \\( 7 \\times 80 = 560 \\),  \n- \\( 7 \\times 2 = 14 \\).  \nAdding these:  \n\\( 2400 + 60 + 560 + 14 = 3034 \\).  \n\nBoth methods confirm the result.  \n\n**Answer:** \\(\\boxed{3034}\\)",
