 Correct.\n\nAlternatively, another way: 37 is close to 40. 72\u00d740 = 2880. Then subtract 3\u00d772 = 216, so 2880 - 216 = 2664. Exactly. That works too.\n\nHmm, all these different methods are leading me to 2664. So I think that's the correct answer. But just to be thorough, let me do the multiplication step by step again.\n\nMultiplying 72 by 37:\n\nFirst step: Multiply 72 by 7 (units digit of 37):\n\n7 \u00d7 2 = 14, write down 4 and carry over 1.\n\n7 \u00d7 7 = 49, plus the carried 1 is 50. So the first partial product is 504.\n\nSecond step: Multiply 72 by 30 (since the 3 in 37 is in the tens place, so 3\u00d710).\n\nSo 72 \u00d7 3 = 216, then add a zero at the end to make it \u00d710, so 2160.\n\nNow add 504 + 2160:\n\n504 + 2000 = 2504,\n\n2504 + 160 = 2664. Yep, that's consistent.\n\nAlright, I think that's solid. All the different methods give the same result. So I can be confident that 72 multiplied by 37 is 2664.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 72 and 37 is \\boxed{2664}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 72 and 37, we can use the standard multiplication method:\n\n1. **Multiply 72 by 7 (units place):**\n   \\[\n   72 \\times 7 = 504\n   \\]\n   - \\(7 \\times 2 = 14\\) (write down 4, carry over 1)\n   - \\(7 \\times 7 = 49 + 1 = 50\\)\n\n2. **Multiply 72 by 30 (tens place):**\n   \\[\n   72 \\times 30 = 2160\n   \\]\n   - \\(72 \\times 3 = 216\\)\n   - Add a zero to account for the tens place: \\(216 \\times 10 = 2160\\)\n\n3. **Add the partial products:**\n   \\[\n   504 + 2160 = 2664\n   \\]\n\nWe verified this result using different methods:\n- **Distributive Property:**\n  \\[\n  72 \\times (30 + 7) = 72 \\times 30 + 72 \\times 7 = 2160 + 504 = 2664\n  \\]\n- **Breaking down 72:**\n  \\[\n  (70 + 2) \\times 37 = 70 \\times 37 + 2 \\times 37 = 2590 + 74 = 2664\n  \\]\n- **Approximation Methods:**\n  - \\(70 \\times 37 + 2 \\times 37 = 2590 + 74 = 2664\\)\n  - \\(72 \\times 40 - 3 \\times 72 = 2880 - 216 = 2664\\)\n\nAll methods consistently 