messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 26 and 36?', '<think>:.\nOkay, so I need to find the product of 26 and 36. Hmm, let me think. Multiplying two numbers.. right, that means I have to do 26 times 36. Alright, how do I do this step by step?.\n\nFirst, maybe I can break it down using the distributive property. Like, 26 times 36 is the same as 20 times 36 plus 6 times 36. Let me check that. Yeah, because 26 is 20 + 6, so distributing the multiplication over addition should work.\n\nCalculating 20 times 36 first. Well, 20 times 30 is 600, and 20 times 6 is 120. Adding those together gives 600 + 120 = 720. Okay, so 20*36 is 720.\n\nNow 6 times 36. Let me do that. 6*30 is 180, and 6*6 is 36. Adding those gives 180 + 36 = 216. So 6*36 is 216.\n\nAdding the two results together: 720 + 216. Let me add 700 + 200 first, which is 900, then 20 + 16 is 36. Therefore, my final answer is: ']]
