messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 21 and 61?', "<think>:.\nOkay, so I need to find the product of 21 and 61. Hmm, let me think. Multiplication, right? So 21 times 61. I remember that multiplying two numbers means adding one of them to itself the other number of times. But doing that directly might take a while. Maybe there's a quicker way.\n\nWait, maybe I can break it down using the distributive property. Like, 21 times 60 plus 21 times 1? Because 61 is 60 + 1. Let me try that. So first, 21 multiplied by 60. Hmm, 21 times 60. Well, 21 times 6 is 126, so if I add a zero at the end, that would be 1260. Right? Because multiplying by 60 is the same as multiplying by 6 and then by 10. So that part is 1260.\n\nThen, 21 times 1 is just 21. So adding those two results together: 1260 + 21. Let me add those. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
