e same. So all methods lead to 1495. I think that's correct. Let me check once more with a calculator approach. \n\n23 multiplied by 65. \n\n23 \u00d760 is 1380, plus 23\u00d75 is 115, so total is 1380+115=1495. \n\nAlternatively, 23\u00d765: 23\u00d760=1380, 23\u00d75=115. 1380+115=1495. \n\nYes, I think that's correct. I can't see any mistakes in my calculations. All the different methods cross-verify each other. So I'm confident the product of 23 and 65 is 1495.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 23 and 65 is calculated as follows:\n\n1. **Break down using distributive property**:\n   - Split 65 into 60 and 5.\n   - Calculate \\(23 \\times 60\\):\n     \\[\n     23 \\times 60 = 23 \\times (6 \\times 10) = (23 \\times 6) \\times 10 = 138 \\times 10 = 1380\n     \\]\n   - Calculate \\(23 \\times 5\\):\n     \\[\n     23 \\times 5 = (20 \\times 5) + (3 \\times 5) = 100 + 15 = 115\n     \\]\n\n2. **Add the results**:\n   \\[\n   1380 + 115 = 1495\n   \\]\n\n**Final Answer**: \\(\\boxed{1495}\\)",
