 For \\( 79 \\times 11 \\), add the digits \\( 7 + 9 = 16 \\). Carry over the \\( 1 \\):  \n   \\( 7\\ (7+9)\\ 9 \\rightarrow 7\\ 6\\ 9 \\), plus the carried \\( 1 \\) in the hundreds place:  \n   \\( 869 \\).\n\n3. **Standard algorithm**:  \n   \\[\n   \\begin{array}{r}\n     \\quad 79 \\\\\n   \\times 11 \\\\\n   \\hline\n     \\quad 79 \\quad (79 \\times 1) \\\\\n   + 790 \\quad (79 \\times 10) \\\\\n   \\hline\n     869 \\\\\n   \\end{array}\n   \\]\n\n**Final Answer:**  \nThe product of 11 and 79 is \\(\\boxed{869}\\).",
