messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 13 and 92?', "<think>:.\nOkay, let's see. I need to find the product of 13 and 92. Hmm, multiplication, right? Alright, so 13 times 92. I should probably do this step by step. Let me think about the best way to approach it. Maybe breaking it down into smaller parts?.\n\nFirst, I remember that multiplying two numbers can sometimes be easier if you split one of them into parts. Like, 92 can be split into 90 and 2. So, 13 times 90 plus 13 times 2. That might work. Let me try that.\n\nStarting with 13 times 90. Hmm, 13 times 90. Well, 13 times 9 is 117, right? So if I multiply that by 10, since 90 is 9 times 10, then it would be 117 times 10, which is 1170. Okay, that part makes sense.\n\nNow, the other part is 13 times 2. That's straightforward. 13 times 2 is 26. So now I just add those two results together. 1170 plus 26. Let me add those. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
