5040. \n\nAdding 189 + 5040. Let's see: 5040 + 100 = 5140, then +89 = 5229. Yep, same as before. \n\nAlternatively, maybe use a calculator? Wait, since I can't use a calculator, but I can do another check via division. Let me see if 5229 divided by 63 equals 83. \n\nDividing 5229 by 63. Let's see: 63 \u00d7 80 is 5040. Subtract that from 5229: 5229 - 5040 = 189. Then 189 divided by 63 is 3. So total is 80 + 3 = 83. Perfect, that's correct. \n\nAlternatively, divide 5229 by 83 and see if it's 63. Let's try that. 83 \u00d7 60 is 4980. Subtract that from 5229: 5229 - 4980 = 249. Then 83 \u00d7 3 is 249. So 60 + 3 = 63. Yep, that works too. \n\nAll right, so all the verification methods confirm that the product is indeed 5229. I feel confident that's the right answer. \n\nJust to recap the steps clearly:\n\nMethod 1: Standard Algorithm\n- 63 \u00d7 3 = 189\n- 63 \u00d7 80 = 5040\n- Sum: 189 + 5040 = 5229\n\nMethod 2: Distributive Property\n- (60 + 3)(80 + 3) = 60\u00d780 + 60\u00d73 + 3\u00d780 + 3\u00d73\n- 4800 + 180 + 240 + 9 = 5229\n\nMethod 3: Difference of Squares\n- (73 -10)(73 +10) = 73\u00b2 -10\u00b2\n- 5329 - 100 = 5229\n\nVerification via division:\n- 5229 \u00f763 =83 and 5229 \u00f783=63\n\nAll checks out. I think that's thorough. So the answer is 5229.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 63 and 83 is \\boxed{5229}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 63 and 83, we can use multiple methods to ensure accuracy:\n\n1. **Standard Multiplication Algorithm**:\n   - Multiply 63 by 3 (units place of 83):\n     \\[\n     63 \\times 3 = 189\n     \\]\n   - Multiply 63 by 80 (tens place of 83, which is 8 shifted one position to the left):\n     \\[\n     63 \\times 80 = 5040\n     \\]\n   - Add the results:\n     \\[\n     189 + 5040 = 5229\n     \\]\n\n2. **Distributive Property**:\n   - Expand the product \\((60 + 3)(80 + 3)\\):\n     \\[\n     60 \\times 80 + 60 \\times 3 + 3 \\times 80 + 3 \\times 3\n     \\]\n   - Calculate each term:\n     \\[\n     60 \\times 80 = 4800, \\quad 60 \\times 3 = 180, \\quad 3 \\times 80 = 240, \\quad 3 \\times 3 = 9\n     \\]\n   - Sum the terms:\n     \\[\n     4800 + 180 + 240 + 9 = 5229\n     \\]\n\n3. **Difference of Squares**:\n   - Express 63 and 83 as \\((73 - 10)\\) and \\((73 + 10)\\):\n     \\[\n     (73 - 10)(73 + 10) = 73^2 - 10^2\n     \\]\n   - Calculate \\(73^2\\) and subtract \\(10^2\\):\n     \\[\n     73^2 = 5329, \\quad 5329 - 100 = 5229\n     \\]\n\n4. **Verification via Division**:\n   - Divide 5229 by 63:\n     \\[\n     5229 \\div 63 = 83\n     \\]\n   - Divide 5229 by 83:\n     \\[\n     5229 \\div 83 = 63\n     \\]\n\nAll methods confirm the product is \\(\\boxed{5229}\\).",
