s-verifying through different methods gives the same result. Therefore, I'm confident that 53 multiplied by 31 is 1643.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 53 and 31 is \\boxed{1643}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 53 and 31, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n1. Write down the numbers vertically:\n   ```\n    53\n  \u00d7 31\n  ------\n  ```\n\n2. Multiply 53 by the ones digit (1) of 31:\n   \\[\n   53 \\times 1 = 53\n   \\]\n\n3. Multiply 53 by the tens digit (3) of 31, which represents 30. Since this is the tens place, we shift the result one position to the left:\n   \\[\n   53 \\times 3 = 159 \\quad \\text{(then shift left by one digit to get 1590)}\n   \\]\n\n4. Add the results of the two multiplications:\n   \\[\n   53 + 1590 = 1643\n   \\]\n\nTo verify, we can use the distributive property:\n\\[\n(50 + 3)(30 + 1) = 50 \\times 30 + 50 \\times 1 + 3 \\times 30 + 3 \\times 1\n\\]\n\\[\n= 1500 + 50 + 90 + 3 = 1500 + 50 + 90 + 3 = 1643\n\\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 53 and 31 is \\(\\boxed{1643}\\).",
