38*(100-20) would be 38*100 minus 38*20, which is 3800 - 760. Let me calculate that: 3800 minus 700 is 3100, minus 60 more is 3040. Again, same result. \n\nWow, so multiple methods all leading to 3040. I think that's solid. So I can confidently say the product is 3040. \n\nAlternatively, maybe use a calculator? But since I don't have one here, but my manual calculations all check out. Let me just do one more quick verification. \n\nIf I approximate, 80*40 is 3200, so 80*38 is 2 less 80s, so 3200 - (80*2) = 3200 - 160 = 3040. Yep, that's the same as before. So all these cross-checks are making me sure that this is the correct answer. \n\nI think that's thorough enough. The answer is 3040.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 80 and 38 can be calculated using the distributive property:\n\n\\[\n80 \\times 38 = 80 \\times (30 + 8) = (80 \\times 30) + (80 \\times 8)\n\\]\n\nBreaking it down:\n- \\( 80 \\times 30 = 2400 \\)\n- \\( 80 \\times 8 = 640 \\)\n\nAdding the results:\n\\[\n2400 + 640 = 3040\n\\]\n\n**Verification using another method** (subtractive approach):\n\\[\n80 \\times 38 = 80 \\times (40 - 2) = (80 \\times 40) - (80 \\times 2)\n\\]\n- \\( 80 \\times 40 = 3200 \\)\n- \\( 80 \\times 2 = 160 \\)\n\nSubtracting the results:\n\\[\n3200 - 160 = 3040\n\\]\n\nBoth methods confirm the result is consistent. \n\n**Final Answer:** \\(\\boxed{3040}\\)",
