mes 49 = 13 \\times (50 - 1)\n\\]\n\nApplying the distributive property:\n\n\\[\n13 \\times 50 - 13 \\times 1\n\\]\n\nCalculating each part:\n\n\\[\n13 \\times 50 = 650 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 13 \\times 1 = 13\n\\]\n\nSubtracting these results:\n\n\\[\n650 - 13 = 637\n\\]\n\nTo verify, we can use another method by breaking down 13 into 10 + 3:\n\n\\[\n49 \\times 13 = 49 \\times (10 + 3)\n\\]\n\nApplying the distributive property again:\n\n\\[\n49 \\times 10 + 49 \\times 3\n\\]\n\nCalculating each part:\n\n\\[\n49 \\times 10 = 490 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 49 \\times 3 = 147\n\\]\n\nAdding these results:\n\n\\[\n490 + 147 = 637\n\\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 13 and 49 is \\boxed{637}.",
