over 5. Then 7*6 is 42 plus 5 is 47. So first partial product is 476.\n\nThen, next row, since it's the tens place, start with 0 (or shift one position). 7*8 is 56, write down 6 carryover 5. 7*6 is 42 plus 5 is 47. So that's 4760. Then add 476 + 4760 = 5236. \n\nAll methods lead to the same answer. Therefore, I can be confident that 68 multiplied by 77 is 5236.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 68 and 77 is \\boxed{5236}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 68 and 77, we can use the distributive property by breaking down the numbers into smaller parts:\n\n1. Calculate \\(68 \\times 70\\):\n   - \\(68 \\times 7 = 476\\)\n   - \\(476 \\times 10 = 4760\\)\n   - Therefore, \\(68 \\times 70 = 4760\\)\n\n2. Calculate \\(68 \\times 7\\):\n   - \\(60 \\times 7 = 420\\)\n   - \\(8 \\times 7 = 56\\)\n   - Adding these together: \\(420 + 56 = 476\\)\n   - Therefore, \\(68 \\times 7 = 476\\)\n\n3. Add the results of the two parts together:\n   - \\(4760 + 476 = 5236\\)\n\nWe can verify this using the standard multiplication algorithm:\n- Multiply 68 by 7: \\(68 \\times 7 = 476\\)\n- Multiply 68 by 70 (shifting one position to the left): \\(68 \\times 70 = 4760\\)\n- Adding these partial products: \n  ```\n    476\n  +4760\n  ------\n   5236\n  ```\n\nAnother verification using the distributive property:\n- \\( (70 - 2) \\times 77 = 70 \\times 77 - 2 \\times 77 \\)\n- \\( 70 \\times 77 = 5390 \\)\n- \\( 2 \\times 77 = 154 \\)\n- Subtracting these: \\( 5390 - 154 = 5236 \\)\n\nAll methods confirm that the product of 68 and 77 is \\(\\boxed{5236}\\).",
