ecks out. So I'm confident the product of 46 and 35 is 1610.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 46 and 35 is \\boxed{1610}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 46 and 35, we can use the distributive property by breaking down 35 into 30 and 5:\n\n\\[\n46 \\times 35 = 46 \\times (30 + 5) = (46 \\times 30) + (46 \\times 5)\n\\]\n\nFirst, calculate \\(46 \\times 30\\):\n\\[\n46 \\times 30 = 46 \\times 3 \\times 10 = 138 \\times 10 = 1380\n\\]\n\nNext, calculate \\(46 \\times 5\\):\n\\[\n46 \\times 5 = (40 \\times 5) + (6 \\times 5) = 200 + 30 = 230\n\\]\n\nAdd the two results together:\n\\[\n1380 + 230 = 1610\n\\]\n\nWe can verify this using another method by breaking down the numbers into prime factors:\n\\[\n46 = 2 \\times 23 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 35 = 5 \\times 7\n\\]\n\\[\n(2 \\times 23) \\times (5 \\times 7) = (2 \\times 5) \\times (23 \\times 7) = 10 \\times 161 = 1610\n\\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 46 and 35 is \\(\\boxed{1610}\\).",
