ifting this result one position to the left (equivalent to multiplying by 10) gives:\n   \\[\n   679 \\times 10 = 6790\n   \\]\n   This gives the second partial product:\n   \\[\n   \\begin{array}{r}\n     \\quad 97 \\\\\n   \\times 78 \\\\\n   \\hline\n     \\quad 776 \\\\\n   + 6790 \\\\\n   \\hline\n   \\end{array}\n   \\]\n\n4. Add the two partial products:\n   \\[\n   776 + 6790 = 7566\n   \\]\n\nThus, the product of 97 and 78 is \\(\\boxed{7566}\\).",
