\n\u2003\xa032.\n×\xa0\xa09.\n------.\n\xa0288.\n\nSecond partial product:.\n\u2003\xa032.\n×\xa020 (since it's the 2 in the tens place).\n------.\n\xa0640 (because 32×2=64, then add a zero to make it 640).\n\nWait, 32×20 is 640. Then adding the two partial products together: 288 + 640.\n\nLet me add those. 288 + 640. 200 + 600 is 800, 80 + 40 is 120, 8 + 0 is 8. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
