   - \\(9 \\times 2 = 18\\) (write down 8, carry over 1)\n   - \\(9 \\times 3 + 1 = 27 + 1 = 28\\)\n\n2. Multiply 32 by 20 (the tens place of 29, which is 2 shifted one position to the left):\n   \\[\n   \\begin{array}{r}\n     32 \\\\\n   \\times 20 \\\\\n   \\hline\n     640 \\\\\n   \\end{array}\n   \\]\n   - \\(2 \\times 2 = 4\\) (write down 4 in the tens place)\n   - \\(2 \\times 3 = 6\\)\n   - Add a zero to the result to account for the tens place, giving 640.\n\n3. Add the two partial products:\n   \\[\n   288 + 640 = 928\n   \\]\n\nVerification using the distributive property:\n- \\((30 + 2)(20 + 9) = 30 \\times 20 + 30 \\times 9 + 2 \\times 20 + 2 \\times 9\\)\n- \\(600 + 270 + 40 + 18 = 928\\)\n\nVerification using another method:\n- \\(32 \\times 30 - 32 = 960 - 32 = 928\\)\n\nThus, the product of 32 and 29 is \\(\\boxed{928}\\).",
