s in the tens place, so it's worth 80. Therefore, when we multiply 85 by 80, the partial product is 85 × 80. .\n\nAlternatively, breaking it down step by step:.\n\nFirst partial product: 85 × 5 = 425 (as before).\n\nSecond partial product: 85 × 80. Let's compute that. 85 × 80 is the same as 85 × 8 × 10. .\n\nWe already calculated 85 × 8 as 680, so 680 × 10 is 6800. So that partial product is 6800.\n\nNow, adding the two partial products together: 425 + 6800.\n\nLet me add those. 425 + 6800. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
