 1\\):  \n\\[\n16 \\times 49 = 16 \\times (50 - 1)\n\\]\n\n**Step 2:** Multiply and subtract:  \n\\[\n16 \\times 50 = 800 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 16 \\times 1 = 16\n\\]  \n\\[\n800 - 16 = 784\n\\]\n\n**Verification using standard multiplication:**  \n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n   \\quad 49 \\\\\n\\times 16 \\\\\n\\hline\n   294 \\quad (\\text{49 \u00d7 6}) \\\\\n+490 \\quad (\\text{49 \u00d7 10, shifted left}) \\\\\n\\hline\n   784 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\n**Final Answer:**  \n\\[\n\\boxed{784}\n\\]",
