\nWait, that's another approach, distributing the 23 into 20 and 3, but multiplied by 15. So yeah, same thing. \n\nHmm, I think all methods confirm that 23 multiplied by 15 is 345. I don't see any mistakes in my calculations, so I'm pretty confident the answer is 345.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 23 and 15 is calculated as follows:\n\n**Step-by-Step Explanation:**\n1. **Breakdown using Distributive Property:**\n   - Multiply 23 by 10: \\(23 \\times 10 = 230\\)\n   - Multiply 23 by 5: \\(23 \\times 5 = 115\\)\n   - Add the results: \\(230 + 115 = 345\\)\n\n2. **Alternative Verification:**\n   - Use the standard algorithm:\n     ```\n       23\n     \u00d7 15\n     -----\n       115  (23 \u00d7 5)\n      +230   (23 \u00d7 10, shifted left)\n     -----\n       345\n     ```\n\n**Final Answer:**  \n\\boxed{345}",
