is 2310, plus 140 is 2450, plus 14 is 2464. Yep, same result. \n\nAlright, I think that's enough verification. I'm confident the product of 32 and 77 is 2464. \n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 32 and 77 is \\boxed{2464}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 32 and 77, we can use the distributive property by breaking down 77 into 70 and 7:\n\n\\[\n32 \\times 77 = 32 \\times (70 + 7) = (32 \\times 70) + (32 \\times 7)\n\\]\n\nFirst, calculate \\(32 \\times 70\\):\n\\[\n32 \\times 70 = 32 \\times (7 \\times 10) = (32 \\times 7) \\times 10 = 224 \\times 10 = 2240\n\\]\n\nNext, calculate \\(32 \\times 7\\):\n\\[\n32 \\times 7 = 224\n\\]\n\nAdd the results of the two calculations together:\n\\[\n2240 + 224 = 2464\n\\]\n\nWe verified this result using different methods including the standard multiplication algorithm and breaking down both numbers further. All methods confirm the same result.\n\nThe product of 32 and 77 is \\(\\boxed{2464}\\).",
