      "text": "720 plus 36 equals 756. Wait, let me check that again to be sure. 720 plus 30 is 750, then plus 6 more is 756. Yeah, that seems correct. \n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use another method to verify. Let's try the standard multiplication algorithm. Writing it out vertically:\n\n   18\n\u00d7 42\n------\nFirst, multiply 18 by 2 (the units digit of 42). 18\u00d72=36. Write down 36. \n\nThen multiply 18 by 40 (the tens digit part). So 18\u00d74=72, and since it's the tens place, that's 720. Then add them together, which again gives 720 + 36 = 756. \n\nHmm, same result. That's good. Maybe another way to cross-verify? Let's see. \n\nAlternatively, using the distributive property: (10 + 8) \u00d7 (40 + 2). Wait, that might be more complicated, but let's try expanding it. \n\nSo, (10 + 8)(40 + 2) = 10\u00d740 + 10\u00d72 + 8\u00d740 + 8\u00d72. \n\nCalculating each term:\n\n10\u00d740 = 400,\n\n10\u00d72 = 20,\n\n8\u00d740 = 320,\n\n8\u00d72 = 16.\n\nAdding them all together: 400 + 20 is 420, plus 320 is 740, plus 16 is 756. \n\nOkay, that matches as well. So three different methods all give me 756. I think that's solid. \n\nAlternatively, maybe using some mental math tricks. For example, 18 is 2\u00d79, and 42 is 6\u00d77. Maybe rearrange the factors? 2\u00d76=12 and 9\u00d77=63, so 12\u00d763. Hmm, let me see. 12\u00d760 is 720, and 12\u00d73 is 36, so again adding those gives 756. Yep, same answer. \n\nAnother way: 18\u00d742. Since 18 is close to 20, maybe think of it as (20 - 2) \u00d742. That would be 20\u00d742 - 2\u00d742. \n\n20\u00d742 is 840, and 2\u00d742 is 84. So 840 -84 = 756. \n\nWow, that also works. So that's another method. \n\nI think all these different approaches are leading me to the same result, so I must be correct. 756 is the product of 18 and 42. \n\nLet me just confirm once more with a calculator in my mind. 18\u00d740 is 720, plus 18\u00d72 is 36, so total 756. Yep. \n\nAlternatively, 42\u00d718. Let me flip them. 42\u00d710 is 420, 42\u00d78 is 336. Adding them together: 420+336. 420+300 is 720, plus 36 is 756. \n\nSame answer again. Alright, I think that's thorough enough. No mistakes detected in my reasoning.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 18 and 42 is calculated as follows:\n\n1. **Breakdown using distributive property**:\n   - \\( 18 \\times 42 = 18 \\times (40 + 2) \\)\n   - \\( = (18 \\times 40) + (18 \\times 2) \\)\n   - \\( = 720 + 36 \\)\n   - \\( = 756 \\)\n\n2. **Verification with alternative methods**:\n   - **Standard multiplication**:\n     ```\n       18\n     \u00d7 42\n     -----\n       36  (18 \u00d7 2)\n      720  (18 \u00d7 40, shifted left)\n     -----\n      756\n     ```\n   - **Factoring**:\n     - \\( 18 = 2 \\times 9 \\), \\( 42 = 6 \\times 7 \\)\n     - \\( (2 \\times 9) \\times (6 \\times 7) = (2 \\times 6) \\times (9 \\times 7) = 12 \\times 63 = 756 \\)\n   - **Reverse multiplication**:\n     - \\( 42 \\times 18 = (42 \\times 10) + (42 \\times 8) = 420 + 336 = 756 \\)\n\nAll methods confirm the result is consistent.\n\n**Final Answer**: \\(\\boxed{756}\\)",
