messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 60 and 31?', "<think>:.\nOkay, so I need to find the product of 60 and 31. Hmm, let's see. Product means multiplication, right? Yeah, so basically, I have to multiply 60 by 31. Alright, how do I do that?.\n\nWell, I remember that multiplying by tens can be easier if I break it down. Maybe I can use the distributive property here. Let me think. 60 times 31.. Maybe I can split 31 into 30 and 1. So that would be 60*(30 + 1). Then I can distribute the multiplication over addition. That should work.\n\nSo first, 60 times 30. Hmm, 60 times 30. Well, 60 times 10 is 600, so 60 times 30 would be three times that, right? 600*3. Let me calculate that. 600 times 3 is 1800. Okay, got that part.\n\nThen, the other part is 60 times 1. That's easy, that's just 60. So now I have to add those two results together. 1800 plus 60. Let me add those. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
