Wait, actually, the method is:\n\nWrite the two numbers at the top of two columns. Then, repeatedly divide the first column by two, discarding any remainders, and multiply the second column by two, until the first column is 1. Then add up all the numbers in the second column that are next to an odd number in the first column. \n\nWait, let me see. Let me check if I recall correctly. Maybe starting with the numbers:\n\nLeft column (starting with 84) | Right column (starting with 86)\n\nBut actually, maybe it's better to have one number halved and the other doubled. Let me check the steps again.\n\nAlternatively, here's the step-by-step:\n\nStart with a = 84, b =86\n\nWhile a > 0:\n\n- If a is odd, add b to the result\n\n- Halve a, double b\n\nProceed until a is 0.\n\nWait, perhaps better to use the method where you halve one and double the other. Let me try:\n\nStarting with:\n\n84 | 86\n\nHalve 84 to get 42, double 86 to 172. \n\n42 | 172\n\nHalve 42 to 21, double 172 to 344.\n\n21 | 344\n\nNow, 21 is odd, so we note this. Then halve 21 to get 10.5, but since we discard remainders, it's 10. Double 344 to 688.\n\n10 | 688\n\n10 is even, so nothing. Halve to 5, double to 1376.\n\n5 | 1376\n\n5 is odd, so note 1376. Halve 5 to 2 (discarding .5), double to 2752.\n\n2 | 2752\n\nEven. Halve to 1, double to 5504.\n\n1 | 5504\n\n1 is odd, so note 5504. Halve to 0.5 (discard to 0), so stop.\n\nNow, the numbers to add are the right column entries where the left was odd: at 21, 5, and 1. So 344 +1376 +5504. Let's compute that:\n\n344 +1376 = 1720; 1720 +5504=7224. \n\nWow, that works too. So that also gives 7224. \n\nAlright, so all methods are confirming that the product is 7224. Therefore, I can confidently say that the answer is 7224. \n\nJust to recap, the first method using the difference of squares was the quickest, recognizing that 84 and 86 are equidistant from 85, so (85 -1)(85 +1) =85\u00b2 -1. Then calculating 85 squared as 7225 and subtracting 1 gives 7224. That was efficient. The other methods were good for verification. \n\nI think that's thorough. I don't see any mistakes in my calculations, and all methods cross-validate each other. So yeah, the answer should be 7224.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 84 and 86 can be efficiently calculated using the difference of squares formula:\n\n\\[\n(85 - 1)(85 + 1) = 85^2 - 1^2\n\\]\n\nFirst, compute \\(85^2\\):\n\\[\n85^2 = (80 + 5)^2 = 80^2 + 2 \\cdot 80 \\cdot 5 + 5^2 = 6400 + 800 + 25 = 7225\n\\]\n\nSubtracting 1 gives:\n\\[\n7225 - 1 = 7224\n\\]\n\nVerification via traditional multiplication:\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n   \\quad 84 \\\\\n\\times 86 \\\\\n\\hline\n   504 \\quad (\\text{84 \u00d7 6}) \\\\\n+6720 \\quad (\\text{84 \u00d7 80, shifted left}) \\\\\n\\hline\n   7224 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nBoth methods confirm the result. \n\n**Answer:** \\(\\boxed{7224}\\)",
