00. Since 87 is 3 less than 90, and 43 is 3 more than 40, the actual product should be a bit less than 3600 + (adjustments). Wait, maybe that's not the best way, but 3741 is 141 more than 3600, which seems reasonable given the adjustments. Alternatively, exact calculation is better.\n\nAlternatively, let me do 87\u00d740 first, which is 3480, and then add 87\u00d73, which is 261. 3480+261=3741. Yep, that's exactly the same as before. So all methods point to 3741. I think that's correct. \n\nWait another way: 43\u00d787. Maybe reverse the numbers. 43\u00d780 is 3440, and 43\u00d77 is 301. Then add those together: 3440+301. 3440+300 is 3740, plus 1 is 3741. Yep, same answer. So I think that's solid. \n\nTherefore, the product of 87 and 43 is 3741.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 87 and 43 is \\boxed{3741}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 87 and 43, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n1. Multiply 87 by 3 (the units digit of 43):\n   \\[\n   \\begin{array}{r}\n    \\quad 87 \\\\\n   \\times \\quad 3 \\\\\n   \\hline\n    \\quad 261 \\\\\n   \\end{array}\n   \\]\n   Calculation: \\(3 \\times 7 = 21\\) (write down 1, carry over 2), then \\(3 \\times 8 = 24 + 2 = 26\\). The partial product is 261.\n\n2. Multiply 87 by 40 (the tens digit of 43, which is 4 shifted one position to the left):\n   \\[\n   \\begin{array}{r}\n    \\quad 87 \\\\\n   \\times \\quad 40 \\\\\n   \\hline\n   \\quad 3480 \\\\\n   \\end{array}\n   \\]\n   Calculation: \\(4 \\times 7 = 28\\) (write down 8, carry over 2), then \\(4 \\times 8 = 32 + 2 = 34\\). The partial product is 3480 (since we multiply by 40, we shift one position left).\n\n3. Add the partial products:\n   \\[\n   261 + 3480 = 3741\n   \\]\n\nVerification using the distributive property:\n\\[\n(80 + 7)(40 + 3) = 80 \\times 40 + 80 \\times 3 + 7 \\times 40 + 7 \\times 3\n\\]\n\\[\n= 3200 + 240 + 280 + 21 = 3200 + 240 = 3440; \\quad 3440 + 280 = 3720; \\quad 3720 + 21 = 3741\n\\]\n\nVerification by reversing the multiplication:\n\\[\n43 \\times 80 = 3440 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 43 \\times 7 = 301\n\\]\n\\[\n3440 + 301 = 3741\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 87 and 43 is \\(\\boxed{3741}\\).",
