ace, so \u00d770). So 93\u00d770. Well, 93\u00d77 is 651, so \u00d770 would be 6510. Then add 837 +6510.\n\nAdding those together:\n\n837\n\n+6510\n\n------\n\nStarting from the rightmost digits: 7 +0 =7\n\n3 +1=4\n\n8 +5=13, write 3 carryover 1.\n\n0 (since there's no thousands digit in 837) +6 plus the 1 carried over is 7.\n\nSo 7347. Yep, same as before. Okay, I'm confident now that the product is 7347. So the answer should be 7,347. Wait, the question didn't specify commas, so just 7347. Alright, that's my final answer.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 93 and 79 is \\boxed{7347}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 93 and 79, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n1. Write the numbers vertically:\n   ```\n    93\n  \u00d7 79\n  ----\n   ```\n\n2. Multiply 93 by 9 (the ones place of 79):\n   - 9 \u00d7 3 = 27, write down 7 and carry over 2.\n   - 9 \u00d7 9 = 81, add the carried-over 2 to get 83.\n   - The first partial product is 837.\n\n3. Multiply 93 by 70 (the tens place of 79, which is 7 \u00d7 10):\n   - 7 \u00d7 3 = 21, write down 1 and carry over 2.\n   - 7 \u00d7 9 = 63, add the carried-over 2 to get 65.\n   - The second partial product is 6510 (shifted one place to the left).\n\n4. Add the partial products:\n   ```\n    837\n  +6510\n  ----\n   7347\n   ```\n\nVerification using the distributive property:\n- Break down the numbers: (90 + 3)(70 + 9)\n- Calculate each term:\n  - 90 \u00d7 70 = 6300\n  - 90 \u00d7 9 = 810\n  - 3 \u00d7 70 = 210\n  - 3 \u00d7 9 = 27\n- Sum the results: 6300 + 810 + 210 + 27 = 7347\n\nVerification using another method:\n- Multiply 93 by 80 and subtract 93:\n  - 93 \u00d7 80 = 7440\n  - 7440 - 93 = 7347\n\nAll methods confirm the product is \\boxed{7347}.",
