ion using different methods:\n- Distributive property: \\(64 \\times (70 + 9) = 64 \\times 70 + 64 \\times 9 = 4480 + 576 = 5056\\).\n- Breaking down both numbers: \\((60 + 4) \\times (70 + 9) = 60 \\times 70 + 60 \\times 9 + 4 \\times 70 + 4 \\times 9 = 4200 + 540 + 280 + 36 = 5056\\).\n- Estimation: \\(64 \\approx 60\\) and \\(79 \\approx 80\\), so \\(60 \\times 80 = 4800\\). The actual product is slightly higher, confirming 5056 is reasonable.\n\nThus, the product of 64 and 79 is \\(\\boxed{5056}\\).",
