      "text": "2140 + 70 is 2210, plus 2 more is 2212? Wait a second, hold on. Wait, 2140 + 72. Let me check again. 2140 + 70 is 2210, then +2 is 2212. Hmm, but let me verify that another way. 2140 plus 72. Let me add 2140 + 72. 2140 + 60 is 2200, and then +12 is 2212. Yeah, that's correct. So total is 2212?\n\nWait, but I feel like maybe I made a mistake in the addition steps somewhere. Let me go through each calculation again step by step to confirm.\n\nFirst part: 20*70 is indeed 1400. Correct.\n\n20*9 is 180. That's right.\n\n8*70 is 560. Correct.\n\n8*9 is 72. Correct.\n\nAdding them all together:\n\n1400 + 180 = 1580. That's correct.\n\n1580 + 560. Let me add 1580 + 500 first which is 2080, then plus 60 more: 2080 +60 = 2140. Correct.\n\n2140 +72. 2140 + 70 is 2210, plus 2 is 2212. So the total is 2212?\n\nWait, but I thought maybe 28*80 would be 2240, so 28*79 would be 2240 -28=2212. Oh, that's another way to do it. Let me check that method as well.\n\nAlternatively, 28*79 can be thought of as 28*(80 -1). Which would be 28*80 -28*1.\n\n28*80: 28*8 is 224, so 28*80 is 2240. Then subtract 28 gives 2240-28=2212. So that matches the previous result. Okay, so that's a good check. So both methods give me 2212. So I think that's correct.\n\nBut let me do the multiplication the standard way, vertically, to confirm.\n\nMultiplying 28 by 79.\n\nFirst, write it down:\n\n\u2003\u200328\n\n\u00d779\n\n--------\n\nMultiply 28 by 9 first. 9*8 is 72, write down 2 and carryover 7. Then 9*2 is 18 plus 7 is 25. So that gives 252.\n\nThen multiply 28 by 70 (since the 7 is in the tens place, so it's 70). 70*28. Let me compute 7*28 first, which is 196, then add a zero at the end to make it 1960.\n\nNow add the two results: 252 +1960.\n\n252 + 1960. Let's see: 1960 + 200 is 2160, then +52 is 2212. Yep, same result. So that's three different methods, all leading to 2212. So I think that's solid.\n\nTherefore, the product of 28 and 79 is 2212.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 28 and 79 is \\boxed{2212}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 28 and 79, we can use the distributive property by breaking down the numbers into smaller parts:\n\n\\[\n(20 + 8)(70 + 9)\n\\]\n\nApplying the distributive property:\n\n\\[\n20 \\times 70 + 20 \\times 9 + 8 \\times 70 + 8 \\times 9\n\\]\n\nCalculating each term separately:\n\n\\[\n20 \\times 70 = 1400\n\\]\n\\[\n20 \\times 9 = 180\n\\]\n\\[\n8 \\times 70 = 560\n\\]\n\\[\n8 \\times 9 = 72\n\\]\n\nAdding these results together:\n\n\\[\n1400 + 180 = 1580\n\\]\n\\[\n1580 + 560 = 2140\n\\]\n\\[\n2140 + 72 = 2212\n\\]\n\nAnother method to verify is by considering \\(28 \\times 79\\) as \\(28 \\times (80 - 1)\\):\n\n\\[\n28 \\times 80 - 28 \\times 1 = 2240 - 28 = 2212\n\\]\n\nUsing the standard vertical multiplication method:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n\\quad 28 \\\\\n\\times 79 \\\\\n\\hline\n\\quad 252 \\quad (\\text{28} \\times 9) \\\\\n+1960 \\quad (\\text{28} \\times 70) \\\\\n\\hline\n2212 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nAll methods confirm that the product of 28 and 79 is \\(\\boxed{2212}\\).",
