e can use multiple methods to verify the result:\n\n1. **Breaking down 70 into 7 and 10:**\n   - First, calculate \\(73 \\times 7\\):\n     \\[\n     73 \\times 7 = (70 \\times 7) + (3 \\times 7) = 490 + 21 = 511\n     \\]\n   - Then multiply the result by 10:\n     \\[\n     511 \\times 10 = 5110\n     \\]\n\n2. **Using the standard multiplication algorithm:**\n   - Multiply 73 by 0 (units place of 70) to get 0.\n   - Multiply 73 by 7 (tens place of 70, which is actually 70):\n     \\[\n     73 \\times 70 = 73 \\times 7 \\times 10 = 511 \\times 10 = 5110\n     \\]\n\n3. **Using the distributive property:**\n   - Express 73 as \\(70 + 3\\):\n     \\[\n     (70 + 3) \\times 70 = 70 \\times 70 + 3 \\times 70 = 4900 + 210 = 5110\n     \\]\n\nAll methods confirm that the product of 73 and 70 is \\(\\boxed{5110}\\).",
