      "text": "3000 + 300 = 3300. Wait, that seems right?\n\nLet me check another way to make sure I didn't make a mistake. Maybe using the standard multiplication algorithm. Let me write it out:\n\n   44\n\u00d7 75\n------\nFirst, multiply 44 by 5. 4\u00d75 is 20, carry over the 2. 4\u00d75 plus the carried 2 is 22. Wait, actually, let me correct that. Wait, 44 \u00d75: the units digit is 4\u00d75=20, so write down 0 and carry 2. Then the tens place: 4\u00d75=20 plus the carried 2 is 22. So that gives 220. \n\nThen multiply 44 by 70. Since the 7 is in the tens place, it's actually 70. So 44 \u00d770. To compute this, first compute 44\u00d77 and then add a zero at the end. 44\u00d77: 4\u00d77=28 and 4\u00d77=28, so 28 + 280 = 308? Wait, no. Let me do that again. 44\u00d77: 4\u00d77 is 28, write down 8 and carry 2. Then 4\u00d77 is 28 plus the carried 2 is 30. So that's 308. So, adding a zero gives 3080. \n\nNow add the two results: 220 + 3080. 220 + 3080 is 3300. Okay, that's the same answer as before. So that's good.\n\nAlternatively, maybe there's another method. Since 75 is 3/4 of 100, maybe we can think of it as 44 \u00d7 75 = 44 \u00d7 (3/4 \u00d7 100) = 44 \u00d7 3/4 \u00d7 100. Wait, that might complicate, but let me see. 44 divided by 4 is 11, then times 3 is 33, so 33 \u00d7 100 is 3300. Oh, that's a quicker way! So that also gives 3300. Nice, that works too.\n\nHmm, so all methods lead to 3300, so I think that's the correct answer. Let me just confirm with a calculator in my mind. 44 times 75. 44 times 70 is 3080, plus 44 times 5 is 220, so total 3080 +220=3300. Yep. Definitely 3300. I think that's solid. So, the product is 3,300.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 44 and 75 is \\boxed{3300}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 44 and 75, we can use the distributive property:\n\n1. Break down 44 into 40 and 4:\n   \\[\n   (40 + 4) \\times 75\n   \\]\n2. Distribute the multiplication over addition:\n   \\[\n   40 \\times 75 + 4 \\times 75\n   \\]\n3. Calculate each part separately:\n   - For \\(40 \\times 75\\):\n     \\[\n     40 \\times 75 = 40 \\times (70 + 5) = 40 \\times 70 + 40 \\times 5 = 2800 + 200 = 3000\n     \\]\n   - For \\(4 \\times 75\\):\n     \\[\n     4 \\times 75 = 4 \\times (70 + 5) = 4 \\times 70 + 4 \\times 5 = 280 + 20 = 300\n     \\]\n4. Add the results of the two parts:\n   \\[\n   3000 + 300 = 3300\n   \\]\n\nAnother method using the standard multiplication algorithm:\n1. Multiply 44 by 5:\n   \\[\n   44 \\times 5 = 220\n   \\]\n2. Multiply 44 by 70 (since 75 is 70 + 5):\n   \\[\n   44 \\times 70 = 44 \\times 7 \\times 10 = 308 \\times 10 = 3080\n   \\]\n3. Add the results:\n   \\[\n   220 + 3080 = 3300\n   \\]\n\nUsing another approach by recognizing 75 as \\(\\frac{3}{4} \\times 100\\):\n1. Calculate \\(44 \\times \\frac{3}{4}\\):\n   \\[\n   44 \\div 4 \\times 3 = 11 \\times 3 = 33\n   \\]\n2. Multiply by 100:\n   \\[\n   33 \\times 100 = 3300\n   \\]\n\nAll methods confirm that the product of 44 and 75 is \\(\\boxed{3300}\\).",
