 This partial product is shifted one place to the left:\n   \\[\n   35 \\times 50 = 1750\n   \\]\n\n4. Add the partial products together:\n   \\[\n   140 + 1750 = 1890\n   \\]\n\nWe can verify this using the distributive property:\n\\[\n35 \\times 54 = (30 + 5)(50 + 4) = 30 \\times 50 + 30 \\times 4 + 5 \\times 50 + 5 \\times 4\n\\]\n\\[\n= 1500 + 120 + 250 + 20 = 1890\n\\]\n\nAnother verification by reversing the multiplication:\n\\[\n54 \\times 35 = (50 + 4) \\times 35 = 50 \\times 35 + 4 \\times 35 = 1750 + 140 = 1890\n\\]\n\nAll methods confirm the result is \\(\\boxed{1890}\\).",
