on step by step again. 46 \u00d785. Let's write it vertically again:\n\n\u2003\u200346\n\u00d7\u00a085\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nFirst step: 46 \u00d75 = 230.\n\nSecond step: 46 \u00d780 = 3680.\n\nAdding 230 + 3680. Let's add 230 + 3680. 3680 + 200 is 3880, plus 30 is 3910. Yep.\n\nAlternatively, use calculator? Well, since I can't actually use a calculator, but I can do another check by dividing. Let's see, if 46 \u00d785 = 3910, then 3910 divided by 46 should be 85. Let me check that.\n\nDivide 3910 by 46. Let's see, 46 \u00d780 is 3680. Subtract that from 3910: 3910 - 3680 = 230. Then 230 divided by 46 is 5. So 80 +5 =85. Perfect, that checks out.\n\nAlternatively, 3910 divided by 85 should be 46. Let's see. 85 \u00d740 is 3400. Subtract that from 3910: 3910 -3400 =510. 85 \u00d76 is 510. So total is 40+6=46. Yep, that works too.\n\nSo all the methods confirm that 46 multiplied by 85 is indeed 3910. I think that's solid. I don't see any mistakes in my calculations, and cross-verifying by division worked. So I'm confident the answer is 3910.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 46 and 85 is \\boxed{3910}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 46 and 85, we can use the distributive property and the standard algorithm for multiplication.\n\nFirst, using the distributive property:\n\\[\n46 \\times 85 = (40 + 6) \\times (80 + 5)\n\\]\nExpanding this, we get:\n\\[\n(40 \\times 80) + (40 \\times 5) + (6 \\times 80) + (6 \\times 5)\n\\]\nCalculating each term separately:\n\\[\n40 \\times 80 = 3200\n\\]\n\\[\n40 \\times 5 = 200\n\\]\n\\[\n6 \\times 80 = 480\n\\]\n\\[\n6 \\times 5 = 30\n\\]\nAdding these results together:\n\\[\n3200 + 200 + 480 + 30 = 3200 + 200 = 3400\n\\]\n\\[\n3400 + 480 = 3880\n\\]\n\\[\n3880 + 30 = 3910\n\\]\n\nUsing the standard algorithm:\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n\\quad 46 \\\\\n\\times 85 \\\\\n\\hline\n\\quad 230 \\quad (\\text{46} \\times 5) \\\\\n+ 3680 \\quad (\\text{46} \\times 80) \\\\\n\\hline\n\\quad 3910 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 46 and 85 is \\(\\boxed{3910}\\).",
