te \\(24 \\times 30\\):\n     \\[\n     24 \\times 30 = 720\n     \\]\n   - Calculate \\(24 \\times 6\\):\n     \\[\n     24 \\times 6 = 144\n     \\]\n   - Add the results:\n     \\[\n     720 + 144 = 864\n     \\]\n\n2. **Standard multiplication algorithm**:\n   - Multiply 24 by 6:\n     \\[\n     24 \\times 6 = 144\n     \\]\n   - Multiply 24 by 30 (since the 3 in 36 is in the tens place):\n     \\[\n     24 \\times 30 = 720\n     \\]\n   - Add the results:\n     \\[\n     144 + 720 = 864\n     \\]\n\n3. **Distributive property**:\n   - Expand \\((20 + 4) \\times (30 + 6)\\):\n     \\[\n     20 \\times 30 + 20 \\times 6 + 4 \\times 30 + 4 \\times 6\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     = 600 + 120 + 120 + 24 = 864\n     \\]\n\n4. **Alternative multiplication trick**:\n   - Rewrite \\(24 \\times 36\\) as \\((12 \\times 2) \\times (36)\\):\n     \\[\n     12 \\times 72 = 864\n     \\]\n\nAll methods confirm that the product of 24 and 36 is \\(\\boxed{864}\\).",
